w+1`. No bpp special case, no early-exit-free prologue.\n- avg: first loop `i < bpp`: `*dp++ = (*rp++ - (*pp++ / 2)) & 0xff`; second loop: `*dp++ = (*rp++ - ((*pp++ + *lp++)/2)) & 0xff`.\n- paeth: first loop `i < bpp`: `*dp++ = (*rp++ - *pp++) & 0xff`; second loop with `a=*lp++, b=*pp++, c=*cp++`, `p = b-c`, `pc = a-c`, `pa=|p|, pb=|pc|, pc=|p+pc|` (PNG_USE_ABS → abs(), else ternary negation), predictor `p = (pa <= pb && pa <= pc) ? a : (pb <= pc) ? b : c`.\n\n## png_write_filtered_row (2746)\n- Always `png_compress_IDAT(png_ptr, filtered_row, full_row_length, Z_NO_FLUSH)`.\n- `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED` `if (png_ptr->prev_row != NULL)` → swap prev_row and row_buf.\n- `png_write_finish_row(png_ptr)`.\n- `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED` `flush_rows++`; `if (png_ptr->flush_dist > 0 && png_ptr->flush_rows >= png_ptr->flush_dist) png_write_flush(png_ptr);`\n\n## png_compress_IDAT (932)\n- First-time init: `if (png_ptr->zowner != png_IDAT)`:\n  - `zbuffer_list == NULL` → malloc one buffer, `next = NULL`; else `png_free_buffer_list(&zbuffer_list->next)` (trim to one).\n  - `png_deflate_claim(png_ptr, png_IDAT, png_image_size(png_ptr)) != Z_OK` → png_error(zstream.msg).\n  - set next_out/avail_out from zbuffer_list.\n- Loop: `avail = ZLIB_IO_MAX; if (avail > input_len) avail = input_len;` `ret = deflate(&zstream, input_len > 0 ? Z_NO_FLUSH : flush)`.\n- `if (png_ptr->zstream.avail_out == 0)`: (MNG/CMF) `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF_SUPPORTED` `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0 && compression_type == PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE` → optimize_cmf(data, png_image_size); `if (size > 0)` write IDAT; `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT`; reset out; `if (ret == Z_OK && flush != Z_NO_FLUSH) continue;`\n- `if (ret == Z_OK)`: `if (input_len == 0) { if (flush == Z_FINISH) png_error(\"Z_OK on Z_FINISH with output space\"); return; }`\n- `else if (ret == Z_STREAM_END && flush == Z_FINISH)`: `size = zbuffer_size - avail_out`; same optimize_cmf guard; `if (size > 0)` write final IDAT; `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`; `zowner = 0`; return.\n- `else` → png_zstream_error + png_error(zstream.msg).\n\n## png_deflate_claim (309) — the compression-parameter branch set\n- `png_ptr->zowner != 0` → build msg; PNG_RELEASE_BUILD: warning, and `if (zowner == png_IDAT)` → return Z_STREAM_ERROR (\"in use by IDAT\"), else `zowner = 0`; non-release: png_error.\n- `owner == png_IDAT`: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZLIB_CUSTOM_STRATEGY) != 0` → `strategy = zlib_strategy`; `else if (png_ptr->do_filter != PNG_FILTER_NONE)` → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY`; `else` → `PNG_Z_DEFAULT_NOFILTER_STRATEGY`.\n- else (text chunks): `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED` use zlib_text_* for level/method/windowBits/memLevel/strategy; `#else` inherit IDAT values, `strategy = Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY`.\n- `if (data_size <= 16384)` → shrink windowBits while `data_size + 262 <= half_window_size`.\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) != 0 && (zlib_set_level != level || zlib_set_method != method || zlib_set_window_bits != windowBits || zlib_set_mem_level != memLevel || zlib_set_strategy != strategy)` → deflateEnd (warn \"deflateEnd failed (ignored)\" if != Z_OK), clear INITIALIZED.\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) != 0` → deflateReset; else deflateInit2 and `if (ret == Z_OK) flags |= PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED`.\n- `ret == Z_OK` → `zowner = owner`; else png_zstream_error.\n\n## optimize_cmf (267)\n- `data_size <= 16384` (else windowBits must stay 15); `(z_cmf & 0x0f) == 8 && (z_cmf & 0xf0) <= 0x70`; `data_size <= half_z_window_size` (else no change); inner `do {...} while (z_cinfo > 0 && data_size <= half_z_window_size)`.\n\n## png_image_size (221)\n- `png_ptr->rowbytes < 32768 && h < 32768`: `interlaced != 0` → sum over pass 0..6 of `(PNG_ROWBYTES(pd, pw)+1) * PNG_PASS_ROWS(h,pass)` for `pw > 0`; else `(rowbytes+1) * h`. Else → `0xffffffffU`.\n\n## png_text_compress (505) / png_write_compressed_data_out (654)\n- png_text_compress: `ret = png_deflate_claim(...); if (ret != Z_OK) return ret;`\n  - loop: `avail_in = ZLIB_IO_MAX; if (avail_in > input_len) avail_in = input_len;`\n  - `if (png_ptr->zstream.avail_out == 0)`: `if (output_len + prefix_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) { ret = Z_MEM_ERROR; break; }`; `next = *end; if (next == NULL) { malloc; if (next == NULL) { ret = Z_MEM_ERROR; break; } next->next = NULL; *end = next; }`\n  - `deflate(&zstream, input_len > 0 ? Z_NO_FLUSH : Z_FINISH)`; `while (ret == Z_OK)`.\n  - after: `if (output_len + prefix_len >= PNG_UINT_31_MAX)` → msg \"compressed data too long\", `ret = Z_MEM_ERROR`; else png_zstream_error. `zowner = 0`.\n  - `if (ret == Z_STREAM_END && input_len == 0)` → (optimize_cmf on comp->output if CMF enabled) return Z_OK; `else` return ret.\n- png_write_compressed_data_out: starts with `avail = sizeof comp->output` (1024) and `next = zbuffer_list`; loop `if (avail > output_len) avail = output_len;` write; `if (output_len == 0 || next == NULL) break;` then `avail = zbuffer_size; output = next->output; next = next->next;`. Post-loop `if (output_len > 0)` → png_error \"error writing ancillary chunked compressed data\".\n\n## Other chunk writers — exact guards\n- png_write_sig (68): `if (png_ptr->sig_bytes < 3) mode |= PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE`; writes `8 - sig_bytes` bytes from offset sig_bytes.\n- png_write_chunk_header (90): `png_ptr == NULL` → return. png_write_chunk_data (144): `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `data != NULL && length > 0` → write + CRC. png_write_chunk_end (163): NULL → return. png_write_complete_chunk (192): NULL → return; `length > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` → png_error \"length exceeds PNG maximum\".\n- png_write_sCAL_s (1848): `wlen = strlen(width); hlen = strlen(height); total_len = wlen+hlen+2;` `if (total_len > 64)` → warning \"Can't write sCAL (buffer too small)\" + return. Else buf[0]=unit, memcpy width incl NUL, memcpy height without NUL.\n- png_write_pCAL (1783): `type >= PNG_EQUATION_LAST` → png_error \"Unrecognized equation type for pCAL chunk\"; `purpose_len == 0` (from png_check_keyword) → png_error \"pCAL: invalid keyword\"; `units_len = strlen(units) + (nparams == 0 ? 0 : 1)`; per-param `params_len[i] = strlen(params[i]) + (i == nparams-1 ? 0 : 1)`; params_len malloc'd of `nparams * sizeof(size_t)` (no nparams range check).\n- png_write_iCCP (1118): `profile == NULL` → png_error \"No profile for iCCP chunk\"; `profile_len < 132` → \"ICC profile too short\"; `png_get_uint_32(profile) != profile_len` → \"Incorrect data in iCCP\"; `temp = *(profile+8); if (temp > 3 && (profile_len & 0x03))` → \"ICC profile length invalid (not a multiple of 4)\"; redundant `profile_len != embedded_profile_len` → \"Profile length does not match profile\"; `name_len == 0` → \"iCCP: invalid keyword\"; `png_text_compress(...) != Z_OK` → png_error(zstream.msg).\n- png_write_sPLT (1180): `entry_size = (spalette->depth == 8 ? 6 : 10)`; `name_len == 0` → png_error \"sPLT: invalid keyword\"; per entry `spalette->depth == 8` → 4 bytes + uint16 frequency; else → five uint16s. Length `name_len + 2 + palette_size`.\n- png_write_eXIf (1516): no validity guard at all; header length `num_exif`, then a 1-byte chunk_data call per byte (`for (i = 0; i < num_exif; i++)`). Negative num_exif is not checked.\n- png_write_cICP (1449): no guards; fixed 4-byte payload (colour_primaries, transfer_function, matrix_coefficients, video_full_range_flag).\n- png_write_cLLI_fixed (1471): no guards; 8 bytes (maxCLL, maxFALL).\n- png_write_mDCV_fixed (1487): no guards; 24 bytes (8 uint16 chromaticities + maxDL + minDL as uint32).\n- png_write_gAMA_fixed (1085), png_write_cHRM_fixed (1294), png_write_pHYs (1878, `unit_type >= PNG_RESOLUTION_LAST` → warning only), png_write_oFFs (1763, `unit_type >= PNG_OFFSET_LAST` → warning only), png_write_sRGB (1100, `srgb_intent >= PNG_sRGB_INTENT_LAST` → warning only, still written), png_write_IEND (1074).\n- png_write_hIST (1538): `num_hist > (int)png_ptr->num_palette` → warning + return.\n- png_write_tIME (1902): `month > 12 || month < 1 || day > 31 || day < 1 || hour > 23 || second > 60` → warning \"Invalid time specified for tIME chunk\" + return. (minute unchecked.)\n- png_write_tEXt (1569): `key_len == 0` → error \"tEXt: invalid keyword\"; `text == NULL || *text == '\\0'` → text_len = 0 else `text_len = strlen(text)` (the passed-in text_len is discarded); `text_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX - (key_len+1)` → error \"tEXt: text too long\"; `if (text_len != 0)` write text.\n- png_write_zTXt (1612): `compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE` → delegate to png_write_tEXt and return; `compression != PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` → error \"zTXt: invalid compression type\"; `key_len == 0` → error; `png_text_compress != Z_OK` → error.\n- png_write_iTXt (1663): `key_len == 0` → error; `switch (compression)`: `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE`/`PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE` → flag 0; `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`/`PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` → flag 1; `default:` → error \"iTXt: invalid compression\". `lang == NULL` → \"\"; `lang_key == NULL` → \"\"; `text == NULL` → \"\"; prefix_len saturates at PNG_UINT_31_MAX on each of the two additions; `compression != 0` → png_text_compress (error on != Z_OK) else `comp.input_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX-prefix_len` → error \"iTXt: uncompressed text too long\"; write path branches again on `compression != 0` (compressed_data_out vs raw text).\n- png_do_write_interlace (2103): `if (pass < 6)` (pass 6 = no-op); `switch (row_info->pixel_depth)` arms `1`, `2`, `4`, `default` (whole-byte pixels via `pixel_bytes = pixel_depth >> 3`, memcpy only `if (dp != sp)`); each low-depth arm has a `if (shift == 0) {reset; flush} else shift -= n` inner branch and a tail `if (shift != <start>) *dp = d`. Then width and rowbytes recomputed.\n\n# 4. pngwrite.c (classic API)\n\n## png_write_info_before_PLTE (83)\n- `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` → return.\n- `(png_ptr->mode & PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE) == 0` gates the whole body (idempotent).\n- png_write_sig; MNG: `(mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) != 0 && mng_features_permitted != 0` → warning \"MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream\", `mng_features_permitted = 0`.\n- png_write_IHDR (interlace_type from info_ptr only `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED`, else literal 0).\n- Then, in this exact order, each gated by an info_ptr->valid bit:\n  1. `write_unknown_chunks(png_ptr, info_ptr, PNG_HAVE_IHDR)`\n  2. `(valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) != 0` → png_write_sBIT(..., info_ptr->color_type)\n  3. `(valid & PNG_INFO_cLLI) != 0` → png_write_cLLI_fixed\n  4. `(valid & PNG_INFO_mDCV) != 0` → png_write_mDCV_fixed\n  5. `(valid & PNG_INFO_cICP) != 0` → png_write_cICP (priority 4)\n  6. `(valid & PNG_INFO_iCCP) != 0` → png_write_iCCP (priority 3)\n  7. `(valid & PNG_INFO_sRGB) != 0` → png_write_sRGB (priority 2)\n  8. `(valid & PNG_INFO_gAMA) != 0` → png_write_gAMA_fixed (priority 1)\n  9. `(valid & PNG_INFO_cHRM) != 0` → png_write_cHRM_fixed\n- `mode |= PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE`.\n\n## png_write_info (223)\n- NULL png_ptr or info_ptr → return; calls png_write_info_before_PLTE first.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_PLTE) != 0` → png_write_PLTE; `else if (info_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE)` → png_error \"Valid palette required for paletted images\".\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_tRNS) != 0`: nested `(png_ptr->transformations & PNG_INVERT_ALPHA) != 0 && info_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE` → in-place invert trans_alpha for `j < jend` where `jend = num_trans` clamped by `jend > PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH → PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH`; then png_write_tRNS.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_bKGD) != 0` → png_write_bKGD.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_eXIf) != 0` → png_write_eXIf, `mode |= PNG_WROTE_eXIf`.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_hIST) != 0` → png_write_hIST(hist, num_palette).\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_oFFs) != 0` → png_write_oFFs.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_pCAL) != 0` → png_write_pCAL.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_sCAL) != 0` → png_write_sCAL_s.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_pHYs) != 0` → png_write_pHYs.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_tIME) != 0` → png_write_tIME, `mode |= PNG_WROTE_tIME`.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_sPLT) != 0` → loop `i < (int)info_ptr->splt_palettes_num`, png_write_sPLT each.\n- text loop `for (i = 0; i < info_ptr->num_text; i++)`: `compression > 0` → png_write_iTXt (then `compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE ? …NONE_WR : …zTXt_WR`); `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt)` → png_write_zTXt, mark zTXt_WR; `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE)` → png_write_tEXt, mark NONE_WR; (already-`_WR` negative values match nothing → skipped). Each arm has an `#else png_warning(\"Unable to write …\")` variant when the sub-feature is compiled out.\n- `write_unknown_chunks(png_ptr, info_ptr, PNG_HAVE_PLTE)`.\n\n## write_unknown_chunks (23)\n- `info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num != 0`; per chunk `(up->location & where) != 0`; `#ifdef PNG_SET_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` extra: `keep != PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER && ((up->name[3] & 0x20) || keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS || (keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT && png_ptr->unknown_default == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS))`; then `up->size == 0` → warning \"Writing zero-length unknown chunk\" (still written).\n\n## png_write_row (746)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return (note: `png_debug2` dereferences png_ptr *before* the NULL check).\n- First-row init: `png_ptr->row_number == 0 && png_ptr->pass == 0`:\n  - `(mode & PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE) == 0` → png_error \"png_write_info was never called before png_write_row\".\n  - Seven conditional \"defined out\" warnings, each `#if !defined(PNG_WRITE_x_SUPPORTED) && defined(PNG_READ_x_SUPPORTED)` + `(transformations & PNG_{INVERT_MONO,FILLER,PACKSWAP,PACK,SHIFT,BGR,SWAP_BYTES}) != 0`.\n  - png_write_start_row.\n- Interlace row skip: `png_ptr->interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0`, `switch (png_ptr->pass)`:\n  - 0: `(row_number & 0x07) != 0` → finish_row + return\n  - 1: `(row_number & 0x07) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 5` → skip\n  - 2: `(row_number & 0x07) != 4` → skip\n  - 3: `(row_number & 0x03) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 3` → skip\n  - 4: `(row_number & 0x03) != 2` → skip\n  - 5: `(row_number & 0x01) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 2` → skip\n  - 6: `(row_number & 0x01) == 0` → skip\n  - `default:` → \"error: ignore it\", break.\n- row_info built from `color_type, usr_width, usr_channels, usr_bit_depth`, `pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(...)`; `memcpy(row_buf+1, row, row_info.rowbytes)`.\n- Interlace compaction: `png_ptr->interlaced && png_ptr->pass < 6 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → png_do_write_interlace; then `if (row_info.width == 0)` → finish_row + return.\n- `if (png_ptr->transformations != 0)` → png_do_write_transformations.\n- Depth check: `row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->pixel_depth || row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->transformed_pixel_depth` → png_error \"internal write transform logic error\".\n- MNG: `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && png_ptr->filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → png_do_write_intrapixel.\n- `row_info.color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE && png_ptr->num_palette_max >= 0` → png_do_check_palette_indexes.\n- png_write_find_filter; then `if (png_ptr->write_row_fn != NULL)` → callback(png_ptr, row_number, pass).\n\n## png_do_write_intrapixel (682, MNG only)\n- Guard `(row_info->color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0`.\n- `bit_depth == 8`: RGB → bytes_per_pixel 3; RGB_ALPHA → 4; `else return;`. Then `*rp -= *(rp+1); *(rp+2) -= *(rp+1)`.\n- `else if (bit_depth == 16)` (WRITE_16BIT): RGB → 6; RGB_ALPHA → 8; `else return;`. 16-bit red = (s0-s1)&0xffff, blue = (s2-s1)&0xffff.\n\n## png_write_rows (627) / png_write_image (649)\n- png_write_rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; plain `for (i = 0; i < num_rows; i++) png_write_row(*rp++)`. No pass/interlace logic.\n- png_write_image: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `num_pass = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` (7 if interlaced, else 1) — `#else num_pass = 1`. Nested loops: `for (pass = 0; pass < num_pass; pass++) for (i = 0; i < png_ptr->height; i++) png_write_row(image[i])` — the same full image is re-fed once per pass.\n\n## png_write_end (392)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0` → png_error \"No IDATs written into file\".\n- `png_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE && png_ptr->num_palette_max >= png_ptr->num_palette` → png_benign_error \"Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette\".\n- `if (info_ptr != NULL)`:\n  - `(valid & PNG_INFO_tIME) != 0 && (mode & PNG_WROTE_tIME) == 0` → png_write_tIME.\n  - text loop: `compression > 0` → iTXt (+ mark); `else if (compression >= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt)` (note `>=`, unlike `==` in png_write_info) → zTXt; `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE)` → tEXt.\n  - `(valid & PNG_INFO_eXIf) != 0 && (mode & PNG_WROTE_eXIf) == 0` → png_write_eXIf.\n  - `write_unknown_chunks(png_ptr, info_ptr, PNG_AFTER_IDAT)`.\n- `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT`; png_write_IEND; `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED / #ifdef PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_AFTER_IEND_SUPPORTED` → png_flush.\n\n## png_set_flush / png_write_flush (956, 968)\n- png_set_flush: NULL → return; `flush_dist = (nrows < 0 ? 0 : (png_uint_32)nrows)`.\n- png_write_flush: NULL → return; `png_ptr->row_number >= png_ptr->num_rows` → return (already done); else `png_compress_IDAT(NULL, 0, Z_SYNC_FLUSH)`, `flush_rows = 0`, png_flush.\n\n## png_write_destroy (987) / png_destroy_write_struct (1037)\n- destroy: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) != 0` → deflateEnd; free zbuffer_list, row_buf(+NULL); `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED` free/NULL prev_row, try_row, tst_row; `#ifdef PNG_SET_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` free chunk_list; `#if defined(PNG_tRNS_SUPPORTED)` free trans_alpha; free palette. Error/memory handling left intact.\n- png_destroy_write_struct: `png_ptr_ptr != NULL` and `*png_ptr_ptr != NULL` → destroy info struct, NULL out, png_write_destroy, png_destroy_png_struct; otherwise silently nothing.\n\n## png_set_filter (1058) — validity checks\n- NULL → return. MNG: `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && method == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → `method = PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`.\n- `method == PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`, `switch (filters & (PNG_ALL_FILTERS | 0x07))`:\n  - `case 5: case 6: case 7:` (only with WRITE_FILTER) → `png_app_error(\"Unknown row filter for method 0\")` then FALLTHROUGH into\n  - `case PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE (0):` → `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_NONE`\n  - `case PNG_FILTER_VALUE_SUB (1):` → PNG_FILTER_SUB; `case ..._UP (2):` → UP; `case ..._AVG (3):` → AVG; `case ..._PAETH (4):` → PAETH; `default:` → `do_filter = (png_byte)filters` (raw mask). Without WRITE_FILTER, `default:` → app_error \"Unknown row filter for method 0\".\n  - Post-switch (WRITE_FILTER only) `if (png_ptr->row_buf != NULL)` (i.e. after writing started):\n    - `png_ptr->height == 1` → `filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`; `png_ptr->width == 1` → `filters &= ~(SUB|AVG|PAETH)`\n    - `(filters & (UP|AVG|PAETH)) != 0 && png_ptr->prev_row == NULL` → app_warning \"png_set_filter: UP/AVG/PAETH cannot be added after start\" and `filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`\n    - count num_filters over SUB/UP/AVG/PAETH; `buf_size = PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_channels*usr_bit_depth, width)+1`; `try_row == NULL` → malloc; `num_filters > 1 && tst_row == NULL` → malloc.\n    - then unconditionally `do_filter = (png_byte)filters` (overrides the switch result).\n- `else` → png_error \"Unknown custom filter method\".\n\n## png_set_filter_heuristics / _fixed (1187, 1201)\nBoth are empty deprecated stubs (`PNG_UNUSED` on every argument) inside `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`; no branches, no weighted heuristic implementation remains.\n\n## png_set_compression_* / png_set_text_compression_* clamping\nAll: `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n- png_set_compression_level (1216): no clamp, `zlib_level = level`.\n- png_set_compression_mem_level (1227): no clamp.\n- png_set_compression_strategy (1238): unconditionally `flags |= PNG_FLAG_ZLIB_CUSTOM_STRATEGY` (disables the do_filter-based auto choice in png_deflate_claim), then store.\n- png_set_compression_window_bits (1255): `window_bits > 15` → warning \"Only compression windows <= 32k supported by PNG\", forced 15; `else if (window_bits < 8)` → warning \"Only compression windows >= 256 supported by PNG\", forced 8; else as-is.\n- png_set_compression_method (1284): `method != 8` → warning \"Only compression method 8 is supported by PNG\" but the bad value is still stored.\n- png_set_text_compression_level / _mem_level / _strategy (1304, 1315, 1326): no clamp; note _strategy does NOT set the CUSTOM_STRATEGY flag.\n- png_set_text_compression_window_bits (1340): identical >15 → 15 / <8 → 8 clamping with the same two warnings.\n- png_set_text_compression_method (1363): `method != 8` → warning, value still stored.\n- png_set_write_status_fn (1379), png_set_write_user_transform_fn (1391): NULL → return; the latter unconditionally `transformations |= PNG_USER_TRANSFORM` and stores fn (even if fn == NULL, in which case png_do_write_transformations' inner NULL check skips it).\n- png_create_write_struct(_2) (543/557): defaults zbuffer_size = PNG_ZBUF_SIZE, zlib_strategy = PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY, level = PNG_Z_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION, mem_level = 8, window_bits = 15, method = 8; text equivalents under `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_COMPRESSED_TEXT_SUPPORTED`; `#ifdef PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` → `flags |= PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN`; `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` → `flags |= PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN`; then png_set_write_fn(NULL,NULL,NULL).\n\n## png_write_png (1407) — transform flags\n- `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` → return; `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_IDAT) == 0` → app_error \"no rows for png_write_image to write\" + return.\n- png_write_info first, then the transforms are set *after* the header (order in source):\n  1. `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_MONO` → png_set_invert_mono (`#else` app_error \"…not supported\")\n  2. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SHIFT` → nested `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) != 0` → png_set_shift(&info_ptr->sig_bit) (silently skipped if sBIT invalid)\n  3. `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKING` → png_set_packing\n  4. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ALPHA` → png_set_swap_alpha\n  5. `(transforms & (PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER_AFTER|PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER_BEFORE)) != 0`: `AFTER` set → if `BEFORE` also set, app_error \"PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER: BEFORE+AFTER not supported\" then (if benign) png_set_filler(0, PNG_FILLER_AFTER); `else if (BEFORE)` → png_set_filler(0, PNG_FILLER_BEFORE)\n  6. `PNG_TRANSFORM_BGR` → png_set_bgr\n  7. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ENDIAN` → png_set_swap\n  8. `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKSWAP` → png_set_packswap\n  9. `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_ALPHA` → png_set_invert_alpha\n  Each has an `#else png_app_error(\"PNG_TRANSFORM_x not supported\")` variant.\n- png_write_image(info_ptr->row_pointers); png_write_end(png_ptr, info_ptr); `PNG_UNUSED(params)`.\n\n# 5. Simplified write API (pngwrite.c, `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED`)\n\n## png_image_write_to_file (2395)\n- `image != NULL && image->version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`, `file_name != NULL && buffer != NULL`, `fp = fopen(file_name,\"wb\") != NULL`, then delegates to png_image_write_to_stdio.\n- On write success: `fflush(fp) == 0 && ferror(fp) == 0` → `fclose(fp) == 0` → return 1; else `error = errno` (fclose) → remove(file_name) + png_image_error(strerror(error)). If fflush/ferror failed: `error = errno`, fclose, remove, png_image_error.\n- On write failure: fclose + remove + return 0.\n- `fp == NULL` → png_image_error(strerror(errno)); bad file_name/buffer → png_image_error \"png_image_write_to_file: invalid argument\"; wrong version → \"…incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"; `image == NULL` → return 0.\n\n## png_image_write_to_stdio (2346)\n- `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`; `file != NULL && buffer != NULL`; `png_image_write_init(image) != 0` → sets `png_ptr->io_ptr = file` directly (bypasses png_init_io), zeroes display, fills image/buffer/row_stride/colormap/convert_to_8bit (memory/memory_bytes left 0), `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_write_main, &display)`, png_image_free, return result. Else 0 / invalid-argument / version / NULL arms as above.\n\n## png_image_write_to_memory (2279)\n- `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`; `memory_bytes != NULL && buffer != NULL` else png_image_error \"…invalid argument\"; `image == NULL` → 0; bad version → \"…incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\".\n- `if (memory == NULL) *memory_bytes = 0;` (size-query mode: still runs the full write, only counting).\n- `png_image_write_init != 0` → display.memory = memory, display.memory_bytes = *memory_bytes, output_bytes = 0; `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_write_memory, &display)`; png_image_free.\n- `if (result)`: `memory != NULL && display.output_bytes > *memory_bytes` → `result = 0` (buffer too small) but `*memory_bytes` is still updated to the required size. Init failure → 0.\n- image_memory_write (2232) per-call: `size <= ((png_alloc_size_t)-1) - ob` else png_error \"png_image_write_to_memory: PNG too big\"; `size > 0`; `display->memory_bytes >= ob+size` → memcpy, otherwise skip the copy but always `output_bytes = ob+size`.\n- png_image_write_memory (2263): png_set_write_fn(png_ptr, display, image_memory_write, image_memory_flush) then png_image_write_main. image_memory_flush is a no-op.\n- png_image_write_init (1534): `png_ptr != NULL` → `info_ptr != NULL` → `control != NULL` → memset 0, control->for_write = 1, image->opaque = control, return 1; each failure unwinds and falls to `png_image_error(image, \"png_image_write_: out of memory\")`.\n\n## png_image_write_main (1998) — the full branch set\n- Derived booleans: `colormap = (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP)`; `linear = !colormap && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_LINEAR)`; `alpha = !colormap && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA)`; `write_16bit = linear && (display->convert_to_8bit == 0)`. Note: LINEAR and ALPHA are forced off for colormapped input.\n- `#ifdef PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` → png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 0) — all benign errors become hard errors for this path.\n- row_stride block, `channels = PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_CHANNELS(image->format)`:\n  - `image->width <= 0x7fffffffU/channels` else png_error \"image row stride too large\".\n  - `png_row_stride = image->width * channels`.\n  - `display->row_stride == 0` → defaulted to `(png_int_32)png_row_stride`.\n  - `display->row_stride < 0` → `check = -(png_uint_32)row_stride`; else `check = (png_uint_32)row_stride` (negative stride = bottom-up image, magnitude used).\n  - `check >= png_row_stride` → `image->height > 0xffffffffU/png_row_stride` → png_error \"memory image too large\"; else OK.\n  - `check < png_row_stride` → png_error \"supplied row stride too small\".\n- IHDR selection:\n  - `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP) != 0`:\n    - `display->colormap != NULL && image->colormap_entries > 0` → `png_set_IHDR(..., entries > 16 ? 8 : (entries > 4 ? 4 : (entries > 2 ? 2 : 1)), PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE, PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, ...)` then png_image_set_PLTE. (4 depth arms: >16→8, 5..16→4, 3..4→2, 1..2→1.)\n    - else → png_error \"no color-map for color-mapped image\".\n  - else → `png_set_IHDR(..., write_16bit ? 16 : 8, ((format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLOR) ? PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR : 0) + ((format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA) ? PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA : 0), PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, ...)` → color type 0/2/4/6. Never interlaced.\n- Colorspace chunks (3-way):\n  - `write_16bit != 0` → png_set_gAMA_fixed(PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR); plus nested `(image->flags & PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB) == 0` → png_set_cHRM_fixed(sRGB primaries 31270/32900, 64000/33000, 30000/60000, 15000/6000).\n  - `else if ((image->flags & PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB) == 0)` → png_set_sRGB(PNG_sRGB_INTENT_PERCEPTUAL).\n  - `else` → png_set_gAMA_fixed(PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE).\n- png_write_info, then transforms (must be after the header):\n  - `write_16bit != 0` → `png_uint_16 le = 0x0001; if ((*(png_const_bytep)&le) != 0) png_set_swap(png_ptr);` (little-endian host detection).\n  - `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_BGR_SUPPORTED` `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_BGR) != 0`: nested `colormap == 0 && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLOR) != 0` → png_set_bgr; then `format &= ~PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_BGR` unconditionally (BGR on a colormapped or gray image is consumed silently; colormapped BGR is handled inside png_image_set_PLTE instead).\n  - `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_AFIRST_SUPPORTED` `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_AFIRST) != 0`: nested `colormap == 0 && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` → png_set_swap_alpha; then clear the flag.\n  - `colormap != 0 && image->colormap_entries <= 16` → png_set_packing (app data is byte-packed but IHDR depth is 1/2/4).\n  - Residual check: `(format & ~(png_uint_32)(PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLOR | PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_LINEAR | PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA | PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP)) != 0` → png_error \"png_write_image: unsupported transformation\". Note PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ASSOCIATED_ALPHA is never cleared, so setting it reaches this error (the simplified writer always assumes premultiplied/associated handling internally via png_unpremultiply); BGR/AFIRST only survive here if their `#ifdef` is off.\n- first_row / row_step: `row_step = display->row_stride`; `if (linear != 0) row_step *= 2` (16-bit components); `if (row_step < 0) row += (image->height-1) * (-row_step)` (start at the last row); store first_row/row_step.\n- `(image->flags & PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_FAST) != 0` → png_set_filter(PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE, PNG_NO_FILTERS) and (`#ifdef PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`) png_set_compression_level(png_ptr, 3).\n- Row-writing dispatch (the top-level 2-way):\n  - `linear != 0 && (alpha != 0 || display->convert_to_8bit != 0)` → malloc local_row of `png_get_rowbytes(png_ptr, info_ptr)`; then `write_16bit != 0` → png_safe_execute(png_write_image_16bit) else png_safe_execute(png_write_image_8bit); local_row = NULL; free; `if (result == 0) return 0` (skip write_end).\n    - Sub-cases: (linear, alpha, 16-bit out) → 16bit path; (linear, alpha, convert_to_8bit) → 8bit path alpha branch; (linear, no alpha, convert_to_8bit) → 8bit path no-alp