\nAll ten are independent (no else); order is fixed as above. Whole function is inside `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_TRANSFORMS_SUPPORTED`.\n\n## png_do_pack (line 24), args (row_info, row, bit_depth = png_ptr->bit_depth)\n- Outer guard: `row_info->bit_depth == 8 && row_info->channels == 1` — else entire function is a no-op (no row_info mutation).\n- `switch ((int)bit_depth)`:\n  - `case 1:` mask starts 0x80, `if (*sp != 0) v |= mask`; inner `if (mask > 1) mask >>= 1; else {mask=0x80; *dp=v; v=0;}`; tail `if (mask != 0x80) *dp = v`.\n  - `case 2:` shift starts 6, `value = *sp & 0x03`; inner `if (shift == 0) {shift=6; flush} else shift -= 2`; tail `if (shift != 6) *dp = v`.\n  - `case 4:` shift starts 4, `value = *sp & 0x0f`; inner `if (shift == 0) {shift=4; flush} else shift -= 4`; tail `if (shift != 4) *dp = v`.\n  - `default: break;` — no data change but still falls through to the updates below.\n- Unconditionally (inside outer guard): bit_depth = bit_depth, pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels, rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width). So `default` (bit_depth 8/16/other) still rewrites row_info.\n\n## png_do_shift (line 171)\n- Outer guard: `row_info->color_type != PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE`.\n- Channel-set selection:\n  - `(row_info->color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0` → 3 channels seeded from bit_depth->red/green/blue.\n  - else → 1 channel seeded from bit_depth->gray.\n  - then `(row_info->color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA) != 0` → append alpha channel (channels becomes 2 or 4).\n- Depth arms:\n  - `row_info->bit_depth < 8` (1/2/4; only channel [0] used):\n    - `bit_depth->gray == 1 && row_info->bit_depth == 2` → mask = 0x55\n    - `row_info->bit_depth == 4 && bit_depth->gray == 3` → mask = 0x11\n    - else → mask = 0xff\n    - inner shift loop `for (j = shift_start[0]; j > -shift_dec[0]; j -= shift_dec[0])`: `if (j > 0) out |= v << j; else out |= (v >> -j) & mask;`\n  - `else if (row_info->bit_depth == 8)`: iterates `channels * width` bytes, `c = i % channels`; `if (j 