row_info->bit_depth) && png_ptr->num_palette > 0`.\n  - `padding = PNG_PADBITS(row_info->pixel_depth, row_info->width)`; `rp = row_buf + rowbytes`, walking backwards to `> row_buf`, `padding` zeroed after the first (rightmost) byte.\n  - `switch (row_info->bit_depth)`: `case 1:` `if ((*rp >> padding) != 0) num_palette_max = 1`; `case 2:` four 2-bit fields (`&0x03` at shifts 0,2,4,6 after `>>padding`) each max'd; `case 4:` two 4-bit fields (`&0x0f`, shifts 0 and 4); `case 8:` `if (*rp > num_palette_max) num_palette_max = *rp`; `default: break;` (16 → no-op).\n- png_set_user_transform_info (833): NULL → return; `#ifdef PNG_READ_USER_TRANSFORM_SUPPORTED` extra guard: `(mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT) != 0 && (flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) != 0` → app_error \"info change after png_start_read_image or png_read_update_info\" + return. Else store ptr/depth/channels.\n- png_get_user_transform_ptr (864): NULL → NULL, else ptr. png_get_current_row_number (875): non-NULL → row_number, else PNG_UINT_32_MAX. png_get_current_pass_number (887): non-NULL → pass, else 8.\n- png_set_write_user_transform_fn is in pngwrite.c (see §4), not pngtrans.c.\n\n# 3. pngwutil.c\n\n## png_write_IHDR (689) — bit_depth × color_type validity\n- `switch (color_type)`:\n  - `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY (0)`: `switch (bit_depth) case 1/2/4/8` (+`case 16` only `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_16BIT_SUPPORTED`) → channels = 1; `default:` → png_error \"Invalid bit depth for grayscale image\".\n  - `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB (2)`: `is_invalid_depth = (bit_depth != 8)`; with WRITE_16BIT also `&& bit_depth != 16`; `if (is_invalid_depth)` → png_error \"Invalid bit depth for RGB image\"; else channels = 3.\n  - `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE (3)`: `case 1/2/4/8` → channels = 1 (16 NOT allowed); `default:` → png_error \"Invalid bit depth for paletted image\".\n  - `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY_ALPHA (4)`: same 8/(16) test → png_error \"Invalid bit depth for grayscale+alpha image\"; else channels = 2.\n  - `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB_ALPHA (6)`: same 8/(16) test → png_err