>= (1 << png_ptr->bit_depth)` → app_warning \"Ignoring attempt to write tRNS chunk out-of-range for bit_depth\" + return; else 2-byte chunk.\n- `else if (color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB)`: guard `png_ptr->bit_depth == 8 && (buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]) != 0` (with WRITE_16BIT) / `(buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]) != 0` (without) → app_warning \"…16-bit tRNS chunk when bit_depth is 8\" + return; else 6-byte chunk.\n- `else` (GRAY_ALPHA / RGB_ALPHA) → app_warning \"Can't write tRNS with an alpha channel\".\n\n## png_write_bKGD (1386)\n- `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE`: `(MNG: (num_palette != 0 || (mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_EMPTY_PLTE) == 0) &&) back->index >= png_ptr->num_palette` → warning \"Invalid background palette index\" + return; else 1-byte chunk.\n- `else if ((color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0)`: `bit_depth == 8 && (buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]) != 0` (16BIT build) / `(buf[0]|buf[2]|buf[4]) != 0` → warning + return; else 6-byte chunk.\n- `else` (gray/gray+alpha): `back->gray >= (1 << bit_depth)` → warning + return; else 2-byte chunk.\n\n## png_write_sBIT (1235)\n- `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0`: `maxbits = (color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE ? 8 : png_ptr->usr_bit_depth)`; `sbit->red == 0 || red > maxbits || green == 0 || green > maxbits || blue == 0 || blue > maxbits` → warning \"Invalid sBIT depth specified\" + return; else size = 3.\n- else: `sbit->gray == 0 || gray > usr_bit_depth` → warning + return; else size = 1.\n- then `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_ALPHA) != 0`: `sbit->alpha == 0 || alpha > usr_bit_depth` → warning + return; else `buf[size++] = alpha`.\n\n## png_write_start_row (1929)\n- `usr_pixel_depth = usr_channels * usr_bit_depth`; `buf_size = PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_pixel_depth, width) + 1`; `transformed_pixel_depth = pixel_depth`; `maximum_pixel_depth = usr_pixel_depth`; row_buf malloc'd, `row_buf[0] = PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE`.\n- `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`, `filters = do_filter`:\n  - `png_ptr->height == 1` → `filters &= 0xff & ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`\n  - `png_ptr->width == 1` → `filters &= 0xff & ~(SUB|AVG|PAETH)`\n  - `filters == 0` → `filters = PNG_FILTER_NONE`\n  - `((filters & (SUB|UP|AVG|PAETH)) != 0) && png_ptr->try_row == NULL` → alloc try_row; count num_filters over SUB/UP/AVG/PAETH; `num_filters > 1` → alloc tst_row.\n  - `(filters & (AVG|UP|PAETH)) != 0` → `prev_row = png_calloc(buf_size)` (zeroed).\n- `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` `png_ptr->interlaced != 0`:\n  - `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` → num_rows/usr_width computed from pass-0 arrays (app supplies sub-images)\n  - else → num_rows = height, usr_width = width\n  - `else` (not interlaced, or interlacing unsupported) → num_rows = height, usr_width = width.\n\n## png_write_finish_row (2028)\n- `row_number++`; `if (row_number < num_rows) return;`\n- `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` `interlaced != 0`: row_number = 0;\n  - `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → `pass++` only.\n  - else → `do { pass++; if (pass >= 7) break; recompute usr_width, num_rows from pass arrays; if ((transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0) break; } while (usr_width == 0 || num_rows == 0);` (skips empty passes)\n  - `if (pass < 7)` → `if (prev_row != NULL) memset(prev_row, 0, PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_channels*usr_bit_depth, width)+1)` then return.\n- Fall-through (non-interlaced last row, or pass >= 7) → `png_compress_IDAT(png_ptr, NULL, 0, Z_FINISH)`.\n\n## png_write_find_filter (2549)\n- `#ifndef PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED` → single arm: `png_write_filtered_row(png_ptr, png_ptr->row_buf, row_info->rowbytes+1)`.\n- Else: `filter_to_do = png_ptr->do_filter`; `bpp = (row_info->pixel_depth + 7) >> 3`; `mins = PNG_SIZE_MAX - 256`; `best_row = row_buf`.\n- Row-0 vs later is NOT branched here; the \"row 0\" case is handled by prev_row being calloc'd to zeros in png_write_start_row / memset at pass end.\n- Overflow / none-filter selection:\n  - `if (PNG_SIZE_MAX/128 <= row_bytes)` → `filter_to_do &= 0U-filter_to_do` (keep only lowest set bit;