d & PNG_INFO_sCAL) != 0` → png_write_sCAL_s.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_pHYs) != 0` → png_write_pHYs.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_tIME) != 0` → png_write_tIME, `mode |= PNG_WROTE_tIME`.\n- `(valid & PNG_INFO_sPLT) != 0` → loop `i < (int)info_ptr->splt_palettes_num`, png_write_sPLT each.\n- text loop `for (i = 0; i < info_ptr->num_text; i++)`: `compression > 0` → png_write_iTXt (then `compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE ? …NONE_WR : …zTXt_WR`); `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt)` → png_write_zTXt, mark zTXt_WR; `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE)` → png_write_tEXt, mark NONE_WR; (already-`_WR` negative values match nothing → skipped). Each arm has an `#else png_warning(\"Unable to write …\")` variant when the sub-feature is compiled out.\n- `write_unknown_chunks(png_ptr, info_ptr, PNG_HAVE_PLTE)`.\n\n## write_unknown_chunks (23)\n- `info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num != 0`; per chunk `(up->location & where) != 0`; `#ifdef PNG_SET_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` extra: `keep != PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER && ((up->name[3] & 0x20) || keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS || (keep == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT && png_ptr->unknown_default == PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS))`; then `up->size == 0` → warning \"Writing zero-length unknown chunk\" (still written).\n\n## png_write_row (746)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return (note: `png_debug2` dereferences png_ptr *before* the NULL check).\n- First-row init: `png_ptr->row_number == 0 && png_ptr->pass == 0`:\n  - `(mode & PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE) == 0` → png_error \"png_write_info was never called before png_write_row\".\n  - Seven conditional \"defined out\" warnings, each `#if !defined(PNG_WRITE_x_SUPPORTED) && defined(PNG_READ_x_SUPPORTED)` + `(transformations & PNG_{INVERT_MONO,FILLER,PACKSWAP,PACK,SHIFT,BGR,SWAP_BYTES}) != 0`.\n  - png_write_start_row.\n- Interlace row skip: `png_ptr->interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0`, `switch (png_ptr->pass)`:\n  - 0: `(row_number & 0x07) != 0` → finish_row + return\n  - 1: `(row_number & 0x07) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 5` → skip\n  - 2: `(row_number & 0x07) != 4` → skip\n  - 3: `(row_number & 0x03) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 3` → skip\n  - 4: `(row_number & 0x03) != 2` → skip\n  - 5: `(row_number & 0x01) != 0 || png_ptr->width < 2` → skip\n  - 6: `(row_number & 0x01) == 0` → skip\n  - `default:` → \"error: ignore it\", break.\n- row_info built from `color_type, usr_width, usr_channels, usr_bit_depth`, `pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(...)`; `memcpy(row_buf+1, row, row_info.rowbytes)`.\n- Interlace compaction: `png_ptr->interlaced && png_ptr->pass < 6 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → png_do_write_interlace; then `if (row_info.width == 0)` → finish_row + return.\n- `if (png_ptr->transformations != 0)` → png_do_write_transformations.\n- Depth check: `row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->pixel_depth || row_info.pixel_depth != png_ptr->transformed_pixel_depth` → png_error \"internal write transform logic error\".\n- MNG: `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && png_ptr->filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → png_do_write_intrapixel.\n- `row_info.color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE && png_ptr->num_palette_max >= 0` → png_do_check_palette_indexes.\n- png_write_find_filter; then `if (png_ptr->write_row_fn != NULL)` → callback(png_ptr, row_number, pass).\n\n## png_do_write_intrapixel (682, MNG only)\n- Guard `(row_info->color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0`.\n- `bit_depth == 8`: RGB → bytes_per_pixel 3; RGB_ALPHA → 4; `else return;`. Then `*rp -= *(rp+1); *(rp+2) -= *(rp+1)`.\n- `else if (bit_depth == 16)` (WRITE_16BIT): RGB → 6; RGB_ALPHA → 8; `else return;`. 16-bit red = (s0-s1)&0xffff, blue = (s2-s1)&0xffff.\n\n## png_write_rows (627) / png_write_image (649)\n- png_write_rows: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; plain `for (i = 0; i < num_rows; i++) png_write_row(*rp++)`. No pass/interlace logic.\n- png_write_image: `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `num_pass = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` (7 if interlaced, else 1) — `#else num_pass = 1`. Nested loops: `for (pass = 0; pass < num_pass; pass++) for (i = 0; i < png_ptr->height; i++) png_write_row(image[i])` — the same full image is re-fed once per pass.\n\n## png_write_end (392)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` → return; `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0` → png_error \"No IDATs written into file\".\n- `png_ptr->color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE && png_ptr->num_palette_max >= png_ptr->num_palette` → png_benign_error \"Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette\".\n- `if (info_ptr != NULL)`:\n  - `(valid & PNG_INFO_tIME) != 0 && (mode & PNG_WROTE_tIME) == 0` → png_write_tIME.\n  - text loop: `compression > 0` → iTXt (+ mark); `else if (compression >= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt)` (note `>=`, unlike `==` in png_write_info) → zTXt; `else if (compression == PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE)` → tEXt.\n  - `(valid & PNG_INFO_eXIf) != 0 && (mode & PNG_WROTE_eXIf) == 0` → png_write_eXIf.\n  - `write_unknown_chunks(png_ptr, info_ptr, PNG_AFTER_IDAT)`.\n- `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT`; png_write_IEND; `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED / #ifdef PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_AFTER_IEND_SUPPORTED` → png_flush.\n\n## png_set_flush / png_write_flush (956, 968)\n- png_set_flush: NULL → return; `flush_dist = (nrows < 0 ? 0 : (png_uint_32)nrows)`.\n- png_write_flush: NULL → return; `png_ptr->row_number >= png_ptr->num_rows` → return (already done); else `png_compress_IDAT(NULL, 0, Z_SYNC_FLUSH)`, `flush_rows = 0`, png_flush.\n\n## png_write_destroy (987) / png_destroy_write_struct (1037)\n- destroy: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) != 0` → deflateEnd; free zbuffer_list, row_buf(+NULL); `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED` free/NULL prev_row, try_row, tst_row; `#ifdef PNG_SET_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` free chunk_list; `#if defined(PNG_tRNS_SUPPORTED)` free trans_alpha; free palette. Error/memory handling left intact.\n- png_destroy_write_struct: `png_ptr_ptr != NULL` and `*png_ptr_ptr != NULL` → destroy info struct, NULL out, png_write_destroy, png_destroy_png_struct; otherwise silently nothing.\n\n## png_set_filter (1058) — validity checks\n- NULL → return. MNG: `(mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && method == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` → `method = PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`.\n- `method == PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`, `switch (filters & (PNG_ALL_FILTERS | 0x07))`:\n  - `case 5: case 6: case 7:` (only with WRITE_FILTER) → `png_app_error(\"Unknown row filter for method 0\")` then FALLTHROUGH into\n  - `case PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE (0):` → `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_NONE`\n  - `case PNG_FILTER_VALUE_SUB (1):` → PNG_FILTER_SUB; `case ..._UP (2):` → UP; `case ..._AVG (3):` → AVG; `case ..._PAETH (4):` → PAETH; `default:` → `do_filter = (png_byte)filters` (raw mask). Without WRITE_FILTER, `default:` → app_error \"Unknown row filter for method 0\".\n  - Post-switch (WRITE_FILTER only) `if (png_ptr->row_buf != NULL)` (i.e. after writing started):\n    - `png_ptr->height == 1` → `filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`; `png_ptr->width == 1` → `filters &= ~(SUB|AVG|PAETH)`\n    - `(filters & (UP|AVG|PAETH)) != 0 && png_ptr->prev_row == NULL` → app_warning \"png_set_filter: UP/AVG/PAETH cannot be added after start\" and `filters &= ~(UP|AVG|PAETH)`\n    - count num_filters over SUB/UP/AVG/PAETH; `buf_size = PNG_ROWBYTES(usr_channels*usr_bit_depth, width)+1`; `try_row == NULL` → malloc; `num_filters > 1 && tst_row == NULL` → malloc.\n    - then unconditionally `do_filter = (png_byte)filters` (overrides the switch result).\n- `else` → png_error \"Unknown custom filter method\".\n\n## png_set_filter_heuristics / _fixed (1187, 1201)\nBoth are empty deprecated stubs (`PNG_UNUSED` on every argument) inside `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`; no branches, no weighted heuristic implementation remains.\n\n## png_set_compression_* / png_set_text_compression_* clamping\nAll: `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n- png_set_compression_level (1216): no clamp, `zlib_level = level`.\n- png_set_compression_mem_level (1227): no clamp.\n- png_set_compression_strategy (1238): unconditionally `flags |= PNG_FLAG_ZLIB_CUSTOM_STRATEGY` (disables the do_filter-based auto choice in png_deflate_claim), then store.\n- png_set_compression_window_bits (1255): `window_bits > 15` → warning \"Only compression windows <= 32k supported by PNG\", forced 15; `else if (window_bits < 8)` → warning \"Only compression windows >= 256 supported by PNG\", forced 8; else as-is.\n- png_set_compression_method (1284): `method != 8` → warning \"Only compression method 8 is supported by PNG\" but the bad value is still stored.\n- png_set_text_compression_level / _mem_level / _strategy (1304, 1315, 1326): no clamp; note _strategy does NOT set the CUSTOM_STRATEGY flag.\n- png_set_text_compression_window_bits (1340): identical >15 → 15 / <8 → 8 clamping with the same two warnings.\n- png_set_text_compression_method (1363): `method != 8` → warning, value still stored.\n- png_set_write_status_fn (1379), png_set_write_user_transform_fn (1391): NULL → return; the latter unconditionally `transformations |= PNG_USER_TRANSFORM` and stores fn (even if fn == NULL, in which case png_do_write_transformations' inner NULL check skips it).\n- png_create_write_struct(_2) (543/557): defaults zbuffer_size = PNG_ZBUF_SIZE, zlib_strategy = PNG_Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY, level = PNG_Z_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION, mem_level = 8, window_bits = 15, method = 8; text equivalents under `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_COMPRESSED_TEXT_SUPPORTED`; `#ifdef PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` → `flags |= PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN`; `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` → `flags |= PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN`; then png_set_write_fn(NULL,NULL,NULL).\n\n## png_write_png (1407) — transform flags\n- `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` → return; `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_IDAT) == 0` → app_error \"no rows for png_write_image to write\" + return.\n- png_write_info first, then the transforms are set *after* the header (order in source):\n  1. `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_MONO` → png_set_invert_mono (`#else` app_error \"…not supported\")\n  2. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SHIFT` → nested `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) != 0` → png_set_shift(&info_ptr->sig_bit) (silently skipped if sBIT invalid)\n  3. `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKING` → png_set_packing\n  4. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ALPHA` → png_set_swap_alpha\n  5. `(transforms & (PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER_AFTER|PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER_BEFORE)) != 0`: `AFTER` set → if `BEFORE` also set, app_error \"PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER: BEFORE+AFTER not supported\" then (if benign) png_set_filler(0, PNG_FILLER_AFTER); `else if (BEFORE)` → png_set_filler(0, PNG_FILLER_BEFORE)\n  6. `PNG_TRANSFORM_BGR` → png_set_bgr\n  7. `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ENDIAN` → png_set_swap\n  8. `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKSWAP` → png_set_packswap\n  9. `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_ALPHA` → png_set_invert_alpha\n  Each has an `#else png_app_error(\"PNG_TRANSFORM_x not supported\")` variant.\n- png_write_image(info_ptr->row_pointers); png_write_end(png_ptr, info_ptr); `PNG_UNUSED(params)`.\n\n# 5. Simplified write API (pngwrite.c, `#ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED`)\n\n## png_image_write_to_file (2395)\n- `image != NULL && image->version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`, `file_name != NULL && buffer != NULL`, `fp = fopen(file_name,\"wb\") != NULL`, then delegates to png_image_write_to_stdio.\n- On write success: `fflush(fp) == 0 && ferror(fp) == 0` → `fclose(fp) == 0` → return 1; else `error = errno` (fclose) → remove(file_name) + png_image_error(strerror(error)). If fflush/ferror failed: `error = errno`, fclose, remove, png_image_error.\n- On write failure: fclose + remove + return 0.\n- `fp == NULL` → png_image_error(strerror(errno)); bad file_name/buffer → png_image_error \"png_image_write_to_file: invalid argument\"; wrong version → \"…incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"; `image == NULL` → return 0.\n\n## png_image_write_to_stdio (2346)\n- `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`; `file != NULL && buffer != NULL`; `png_image_write_init(image) != 0` → sets `png_ptr->io_ptr = file` directly (bypasses png_init_io), zeroes display, fills image/buffer/row_stride/colormap/convert_to_8bit (memory/memory_bytes left 0), `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_write_main, &display)`, png_image_free, return result. Else 0 / invalid-argument / version / NULL arms as above.\n\n## png_image_write_to_memory (2279)\n- `image != NULL && version == PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`; `memory_bytes != NULL && buffer != NULL` else png_image_error \"…invalid argument\"; `image == NULL` → 0; bad version → \"…incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\".\n- `if (memory == NULL) *memory_bytes = 0;` (size-query mode: still runs the full write, only counting).\n- `png_image_write_init != 0` → display.memory = memory, display.memory_bytes = *memory_bytes, output_bytes = 0; `png_safe_execute(image, png_image_write_memory, &display)`; png_image_free.\n- `if (result)`: `memory != NULL && display.output_bytes > *memory_bytes` → `result = 0` (buffer too small) but `*memory_bytes` is still updated to the required size. Init failure → 0.\n- image_memory_write (2232) per-call: `size <= ((png_alloc_size_t)-1) - ob` else png_error \"png_image_write_to_memory: PNG too big\"; `size > 0`; `display->memory_bytes >= ob+size` → memcpy, otherwise skip the copy but always `output_bytes = ob+size`.\n- png_image_write_memory (2263): png_set_write_fn(png_ptr, display, image_memory_write, image_memory_flush) then png_image_write_main. image_memory_flush is a no-op.\n- png_image_write_init (1534): `png_ptr != NULL` → `info_ptr != NULL` → `control != NULL` → memset 0, control->for_write = 1, image->opaque = control, return 1; each failure unwinds and falls to `png_image_error(image, \"png_image_write_: out of memory\")`.\n\n## png_image_write_main (1998) — the full branch set\n- Derived booleans: `colormap = (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP)`; `linear = !colormap && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_LINEAR)`; `alpha = !colormap && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA)`; `write_16bit = linear && (display->convert_to_8bit == 0)`. Note: LINEAR and ALPHA are forced