= PNG_DIV257(alpha)`, `out_ptr[aindex] = alphabyte`, `if (alphabyte > 0 && alphabyte < 255) reciprocal = UNP_RECIPROCAL(alpha)`, each component via png_unpremultiply.\n  - No-alpha branch: `row_end = output_row + width*channels`; per component `component *= 255; *out_ptr++ = PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(component)`; writes `output_row` directly (not display->local_row).\n  - Both: `input_row += display->row_step / 2`.\n- png_unpremultiply (1710): `component >= alpha || alpha < 128` → 255; `else if (component > 0)`: `alpha < 65407` → `component = (component*reciprocal + 64) >> 7`, else `component *= 255`; then `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(component)`; `else` (component == 0) → 0.\n\n## png_image_set_PLTE (1852)\n- `entries = image->colormap_entries > 256 ? 256 : (int)image->colormap_entries` (silently truncates; caller has already checked cmap != NULL && entries > 0).\n- `channels = PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_CHANNELS(format)`; `afirst = (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_AFIRST) != 0 && (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` (or `#define afirst 0`); `bgr = (format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_BGR) != 0 ? 2 : 0` (or 0).\n- tRNS pre-filled 255, palette zeroed. Per entry `i < entries`:\n  - `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_LINEAR) != 0` (16-bit colormap):\n    - `(channels & 1) != 0` (no alpha): `channels >= 3` → RGB from `entry[2^bgr]`, `entry[1]`, `entry[bgr]` via PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(255*v); else (gray) → all three from `*entry`.\n    - else (alpha): `alpha = entry[afirst ? 0 : channels-1]`, `alphabyte = PNG_DIV257(alpha)`, `if (alphabyte > 0 && alphabyte < 255) reciprocal = ((0xffff*0xff)<<7)+(alpha>>1))/alpha`; `tRNS[i] = alphabyte`; `if (alphabyte < 255) num_trans = i+1`; `channels >= 3` → RGB via png_unpremultiply(entry[afirst + (2^bgr)] / +1 / +bgr); else gray → png_unpremultiply(entry[afirst]).\n  - else (8-bit sRGB colormap), `switch (channels)`: `case 4:` `tRNS[i] = entry[afirst ? 0 : 3]`, `if (tRNS[i] < 255) num_trans = i+1`, FALLTHROUGH; `case 3:` blue/green/red from `entry[afirst + (2^bgr)] / [afirst+1] /