{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5jfyiugskc24pkkrzxkd4rahunkgsharszsp3r7lvtrhlp6kt3dq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Read-pipeline input-configuration enumeration\n\nFiles: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/c_src/src/pngrutil.c` (4684 lines), `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/c_src/src/pngread.c` (4205 lines).\n\n**Not present in these files** (asked about, but absent in this 1.6.4x-table-driven version): `png_check_chunk_name`, `png_check_chunk_length` (replaced by the `read_chunks[]` table + `png_handle_chunk`), `png_set_option`, `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_set_user_limits`, `png_set_chunk_cache_max`, `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`, `png_set_compression_buffer_size`, `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` (all in `pngset.c`). `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` is a macro (`include/pngpriv.h:1126-1136`): `user_chunk_malloc_max` / compile-time `PNG_USER_CHUNK_MALLOC_MAX` / `65536U` if `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K` / else `PNG_SIZE_MAX`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. pngrutil.c\n\n### png_read_sig (115)\n- `png_ptr->sig_bytes >= 8` -> return, no I/O\n- `png_sig_cmp(...) != 0 && num_checked < 4 && png_sig_cmp(sig,num_checked,num_to_check-4) != 0` -> png_error \"Not a PNG file\"\n- `png_sig_cmp(...) != 0` otherwise -> png_error \"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\"\n- `num_checked < 3` -> set `PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE`\n\n### png_read_chunk_header (182) / check_chunk_name (152)\n- `png_get_uint_31`: `uval > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` -> png_error \"PNG unsigned integer out of range\"\n- `buf[0] >= 0x80U` -> png_chunk_error \"bad header (invalid length)\"\n- `!check_chunk_name(chunk_name)` i.e. any of 4 bytes outside 65..90 after clearing bit 5 -> png_chunk_error \"bad header (invalid type)\"\n- `PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED` -> io_state = READING|CHUNK_HDR then READING|CHUNK_DATA\n- else: returns `length`; CRC reset + run over the 4 type bytes\n\n### png_crc_read (226)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- else read `length` bytes and always `png_calculate_crc`\n\n### png_crc_error (238) — the 4 PNG_FLAG_CRC_* combos\nAncillary branch guard: `handle_as_ancillary || PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(chunk_name) != 0`\n- ANCILLARY: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_ANCILLARY_MASK) == (USE|NOWARN)` -> `need_crc = 0` (no compare, return 0)\n- ANCILLARY: USE only -> need_crc=1; on mismatch png_crc_finish sees `(flags & ANCILLARY_NOWARN)==0` -> **warning**\n- ANCILLARY: NOWARN only -> need_crc=1; `(flags & ANCILLARY_NOWARN)!=0` -> **error**\n- ANCILLARY: neither (default) -> need_crc=1; -> **error**\n- CRITICAL: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_CRITICAL_IGNORE) != 0` -> `need_crc = 0`\n- CRITICAL: `(flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_CRITICAL_USE) != 0` -> need_crc=1, on mismatch **warning**\n- CRITICAL: neither (default) -> need_crc=1, on mismatch **error**\n- 4-byte CRC is always read regardless (`png_read_data(png_ptr, crc_bytes, 4)`)\n\n### png_crc_finish_critical (311) / png_crc_finish (359)\n- `skip > 0` -> loop consuming `min(sizeof tmpbuf==PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE, skip)` per iteration through png_crc_read\n- `handle_as_ancillary && (flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_CRITICAL_IGNORE) != 0` -> `handle_as_ancillary = 0` (demotion undone)\n- error selection: `handle_as_ancillary || PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(chunk_name) ? (flags & ANCILLARY_NOWARN)==0 : (flags & CRITICAL_USE)!=0` -> `png_chunk_warning(\"CRC error\")`, return 1; else `png_chunk_error(\"CRC error\")`\n- no CRC error -> return 0\n- `png_crc_finish(p,skip)` == `png_crc_finish_critical(p,skip,0)`\n\n### png_read_buffer (375)\n- `new_size > png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` -> return NULL (no alloc)\n- `buffer != NULL && new_size > read_buffer_size` -> free + realloc path\n- `buffer == NULL` -> `png_malloc_base`; if non-NULL and `!PNG_NO_MEMZERO` memset 0\n- alloc failure -> returns NULL (caller decides)\n\n### png_inflate_claim (413) — PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW / adler\n- `png_ptr->zowner != 0` -> RELEASE_BUILD: png_chunk_warning + `zowner=0`; else png_chunk_error\n- `ZLIB_VERNUM >= 0x1240 && SET_OPTION && PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW && ((options >> PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW) & 3) == PNG_OPTION_ON` -> `window_bits = 15`, `zstream_start = 0`\n- same but option != ON -> `window_bits = 0`, `zstream_start = 1`\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED) != 0` -> `inflateReset2(zstream, window_bits)` (zlib>=1.2.4) / `inflateReset`\n- not initialized -> `inflateInit2(zstream, window_bits)` / `inflateInit`; `ret == Z_OK` -> set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_INITIALIZED`\n- `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED && ((options >> PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32) & 3) == PNG_OPTION_ON` -> `inflateValidate(zstream, 0)`\n- `ret == Z_OK` -> `zowner = owner`; else `png_zstream_error`\n\n### png_zlib_inflate (524, zlib >= 1.2.4)\n- `zstream_start && zstream.avail_in > 0 && (*next_in >> 4) > 7` -> msg \"invalid window size (libpng)\", return Z_DATA_ERROR\n- `zstream_start && avail_in > 0` otherwise -> `zstream_start = 0`, then `inflate(...)`\n- `!zstream_start || avail_in == 0` -> straight `inflate(&zstream, flush)`\n\n### png_inflate (555)\n- `png_ptr->zowner != owner` -> msg \"zstream unclaimed\", return Z_STREAM_ERROR\n- `output != NULL` -> `zstream.next_out = output` (direct write)\n- `output == NULL` -> per-iteration `next_out = local_buffer`, `avail` clamped to `sizeof local_buffer` (PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE)\n- input chunking: `avail_in < ZLIB_IO_MAX` -> `avail = avail_in`; else `avail = ZLIB_IO_MAX`\n- output clamp: `avail_out < avail` -> `avail = avail_out`\n- flush selection: `avail_out > 0` -> `Z_NO_FLUSH`; else `finish ? Z_FINISH : Z_SYNC_FLUSH`\n- loop while `ret == Z_OK`\n- `avail_out > 0` -> `*output_size_ptr -= avail_out`; `avail_in > 0` -> `*input_size_ptr -= avail_in`\n\n### png_decompress_chunk (680) — chunk_malloc_max / prefix size\n- `limit(=png_chunk_max) < prefix_size + (terminate != 0)` -> `png_zstream_error(Z_MEM_ERROR)`, return Z_MEM_ERROR\n- `limit - prefix_size - terminate < *newlength` -> clamp `*newlength = limit`\n- `png_inflate_claim != Z_OK` -> return that; special `ret == Z_STREAM_END` from claim -> `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`\n- first pass (`output NULL`) `ret == Z_OK` -> `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`\n- first pass `Z_STREAM_END` and `inflateReset != Z_OK` -> `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`\n- `png_malloc_base(prefix_size + new_size + terminate) == NULL` -> `Z_MEM_ERROR`\n- second pass `Z_STREAM_END && new_size == *newlength` -> success; `terminate != 0` -> write NUL at `text[prefix_size + *newlength]`; `prefix_size > 0` -> memcpy prefix\n- second pass `Z_STREAM_END && new_size != *newlength` -> `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`\n- second pass `ret == Z_OK` -> `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`\n- `ret == Z_STREAM_END && chunklength - prefix_size != lzsize` -> `png_chunk_benign_error(\"extra compressed data\")`\n- always `zowner = 0` after the claimed block\n\n### png_inflate_read (835, iCCP only)\n- `zowner != chunk_name` -> \"zstream unclaimed\", Z_STREAM_ERROR\n- `zstream.avail_in == 0` -> refill: `read_size > *chunk_bytes` -> clamp; `read_size > 0` -> `png_crc_read`\n- `zstream.avail_out == 0` -> `avail = min(ZLIB_IO_MAX, *out_size)`\n- flush: `*chunk_bytes > 0` -> Z_NO_FLUSH; else `finish ? Z_FINISH : Z_SYNC_FLUSH`\n- loop while `ret == Z_OK && (*out_size > 0 || zstream.avail_out > 0)`\n\n### png_handle_IHDR (900)\nLength/position pre-checked by table `CDIHDR = 13,13,hIHDR,0,0` (exactly 13, must precede any prior IHDR, no duplicates).\n- channels: `color_type` GRAY(0)/PALETTE(3) -> 1; RGB(2) -> 3; GRAY_ALPHA(4) -> 2; RGB_ALPHA(6) -> 4; `default` (invalid) -> 1\n- `pixel_depth = bit_depth * channels`; `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width)`\n- `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED` -> stores `filter_type`\n- delegates all legality to `png_set_IHDR` -> `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:1961): `width == 0`; `width > PNG_UINT_31_MAX`; `((width+7)&~7) > ((PNG_SIZE_MAX-48-1)/8)-1`; `width > user_width_max`(or PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX); `height == 0`; `height > PNG_UINT_31_MAX`; `height > user_height_max`; `bit_depth ∉ {1,2,4,8,16}`; `color_type < 0 || ==1 || ==5 || >6`; `(color_type==PALETTE && bit_depth>8) || ((RGB|GRAY_ALPHA|RGB_ALPHA) && bit_depth<8)`; `interlace_type >= PNG_INTERLACE_LAST`; plus compression/filter type checks — each sets `error=1`\n- legal matrix therefore: GRAY×{1,2,4,8,16}; PALETTE×{1,2,4,8}; RGB/GRAY_ALPHA/RGB_ALPHA×{8,16}\n- always `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IHDR`; returns `handled_ok`\n\n### png_handle_PLTE (980)\n- `(mode & PNG_HAVE_PLTE) != 0` -> errmsg \"duplicate\"\n- `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) != 0` -> \"out of place\"\n- `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) == 0` -> \"ignored in grayscale PNG\"\n- `length > 3*PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH || (length % 3) != 0` -> \"invalid\"\n- `color_type != PALETTE && (png_has_chunk(tRNS) || png_has_chunk(bKGD))` -> \"out of place\"\n- success: `max_palette_length = (color_type==PALETTE) ? 1U << bit_depth : PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH` — i.e. bit_depth 1/2/4/8 -> 2/4/16/256 entries\n- `length > 3U*max_palette_length` -> `num = max_palette_length` (silent truncation); else `num = length/3`\n- reads `num*3` then `png_crc_finish_critical(length - 3*num, color_type != PALETTE)` (PLTE treated ancillary for non-palette images)\n- error path, `color_type == PALETTE` -> `png_crc_finish(length)` + `png_chunk_error` (fatal)\n- error path, otherwise -> `png_crc_finish_critical(length, 1)` + `png_chunk_benign_error`\n- No `PNG_READ_OPT_PLTE` conditional exists here; optionality is expressed via the `handle_as_ancillary` argument\n- table `CDPLTE = NoCheck,0,0,hIHDR,1` (multiple permitted, no length check)\n\n### png_handle_IEND (1084)\n- always `mode |= (PNG_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_HAVE_IEND)`\n- `length != 0` -> `png_chunk_benign_error(\"invalid\")` (historically data allowed)\n- always `png_crc_finish_critical(length, 1/*ancillary*/)`; returns handled_ok\n- table `CDIEND = NoCheck,0,0,aIDAT,0`\n\n### png_handle_gAMA (1101) — table 4,4,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `ugamma > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` -> benign \"invalid\", handled_error\n- `READ_GAMMA && png_ptr->chunk_gamma == 0` -> `chunk_gamma = ugamma` (last in cICP/iCCP/sRGB/gAMA precedence)\n\n### png_handle_sBIT (1140) — table 4,1,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `color_type == PALETTE` -> `truelen = 3`, `sample_depth = 8`\n- else -> `truelen = channels`, `sample_depth = bit_depth` (so 1,2,3,4 depending on color type)\n- `length != truelen` -> crc_finish(length) + benign \"bad length\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- any `buf[i] == 0 || buf[i] > sample_depth` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0` -> red/green/blue/alpha = buf[0..3]\n- grayscale -> gray=red=green=blue=buf[0], alpha=buf[1]\n\n### png_handle_cHRM (1226) — table 32,32,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- any of 8 `png_get_int_32_checked` overflow (`uval&0x80000000` set both before and after 2's complement) -> `error=1` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `READ_RGB_TO_GRAY && !png_has_chunk(mDCV)` -> `png_ptr->chromaticities = xy`\n\n### png_handle_sRGB (1281) — table 1,1,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `intent > 3` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `READ_GAMMA && (!png_has_chunk(cICP) || chunk_gamma == 0)` -> `chunk_gamma = PNG_GAMMA_sRGB_INVERSE`\n\n### png_handle_iCCP (1326) — table NoCheck,LKMin(=3+LZ77Min=14),hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `read_length = min(81, length)`; after subtract, `length < LZ77Min (11)` -> crc_finish + benign \"too short\"\n- `keyword_length` scan stops at 80 / read_length / NUL\n- `keyword_length < 1 || keyword_length > 79` -> \"bad keyword\"\n- `!(keyword_length+1 < read_length && keyword[keyword_length+1] == PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE)` -> \"bad compression method\"\n- `png_inflate_claim(png_iCCP) != Z_OK` -> errmsg = zstream.msg\n- header read `size != 0` (short) -> \"profile truncated\" (zstream.msg)\n- `png_icc_check_length(...) == 0` -> its own error, errmsg stays NULL\n- `png_icc_check_header(..., png_ptr->color_type) == 0` -> its own error\n- `png_read_buffer(profile_length) == NULL` -> \"out of memory\"\n- tag table read `size != 0` -> \"profile truncated\"\n- `png_icc_check_tag_table(...) == 0` -> its own error\n- `length > 0 && !(flags & PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN)` -> \"extra compressed data\" (error)\n- `length > 0 && BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN && size == 0` -> `png_chunk_warning(\"extra compressed data\")` then continue\n- `size == 0 && info_ptr != NULL` -> steal profile into `info_ptr->iccp_*`; `iccp_name malloc == NULL` -> \"out of memory\"\n- `size == 0 && info_ptr == NULL` -> profile left in read_buffer, handled_ok\n- `finished == 0` -> `png_crc_finish(length)` on all failure paths\n\n### png_handle_sPLT (1550) — table NoCheck,3,hIDAT,hIHDR,1\n- `USER_LIMITS && user_chunk_cache_max == 1` -> crc_finish, handled_error (silent)\n- `USER_LIMITS && --user_chunk_cache_max == 1` -> warning \"No space in chunk cache for sPLT\", handled_error\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `length < 2U || entry_start > buffer + (length - 2U)` -> warning \"malformed sPLT chunk\"\n- `new_palette.depth == 8` -> `entry_size = 6`; else `entry_size = 10`\n- `(data_length % entry_size) != 0` -> warning \"sPLT chunk has bad length\"\n- `dl > PNG_SIZE_MAX/sizeof(png_sPLT_entry)` -> warning \"sPLT chunk too long\"\n- `png_malloc_warn(nentries*sizeof entry) == NULL` -> warning \"sPLT chunk requires too much memory\"\n- per-entry: `depth == 8` -> 4×byte read; else 4×uint16 read; always +uint16 frequency\n\n### png_handle_tRNS (1686) — table 256,0,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY`: `length != 2` -> benign \"invalid\"; else `num_trans=1`, `trans_color.gray = uint16(buf)`\n- `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB`: `length != 6` -> benign \"invalid\"; else `num_trans=1`, r/g/b from buf[0,2,4]\n- `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE`: `(mode & PNG_HAVE_PLTE) == 0` -> benign \"out of place\"\n- `color_type == PALETTE`: `length > num_palette || length > PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH || length == 0` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `color_type == PALETTE` ok -> read `length` bytes, `num_trans = length`\n- else (GRAY_ALPHA / RGB_ALPHA) -> crc_finish(length) + benign \"invalid with alpha channel\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> `num_trans = 0`, handled_error\n\n### png_handle_bKGD (1771) — table 6,1,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `color_type == PALETTE && (mode & PNG_HAVE_PLTE) == 0` -> benign \"out of place\"\n- `color_type == PALETTE` -> `truelen = 1`\n- `(color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0` (RGB/RGBA) -> `truelen = 6`\n- else (GRAY/GRAY_ALPHA) -> `truelen = 2`\n- `length != truelen` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- PALETTE + `info_ptr != NULL && info_ptr->num_palette != 0 && buf[0] >= num_palette` -> benign \"invalid index\"\n- PALETTE + `info_ptr != NULL && num_palette != 0` ok -> RGB from `palette[buf[0]]`\n- PALETTE + (`info_ptr == NULL || num_palette == 0`) -> `red=green=blue=0`\n- GRAY + `bit_depth <= 8 && (buf[0] != 0 || buf[1] >= (1 << bit_depth))` -> benign \"invalid gray level\"\n- GRAY + `bit_depth == 16` -> no range check\n- COLOR + `bit_depth <= 8 && (buf[0]!=0 || buf[2]!=0 || buf[4]!=0)` -> benign \"invalid color\"\n- COLOR + `bit_depth == 16` -> no check\n\n### png_handle_cICP (1882) — table 4,4,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error; else `png_set_cICP(buf[0..3])`\n- `READ_RGB_TO_GRAY && !png_has_chunk(mDCV)` -> chromaticities TODO (no-op)\n- chunk_gamma setting is TODO (no-op)\n\n### png_handle_cLLI (1921) — table 8,8,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error; else `png_set_cLLI_fixed(uint32(buf), uint32(buf+4))` (validation inside setter)\n\n### png_handle_mDCV (1944) — table 24,24,hCOL,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- 8 × `png_get_uint_16(...) << 1` (R,G,B,white order per PNGv3, remapped to cHRM API order), + uint32 peak lum, uint32 min lum\n- `READ_RGB_TO_GRAY` -> unconditionally `png_ptr->chromaticities = chromaticities`\n\n### png_handle_eXIf (1998) — table Limit,4,0,hIHDR,0\n- `png_read_buffer(length) == NULL` -> crc_finish + benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `header != 0x49492A00 && header != 0x4D4D002A` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- table `Limit` -> `length > png_chunk_max` -> \"length exceeds libpng limit\"\n\n### png_handle_hIST (2042) — table 1024,0,hPLTE,hIHDR,0\n- `length != num*2 || num != num_palette || num > PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH` -> benign \"invalid\"\n- loop reads `num` × 2 bytes individually\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n\n### png_handle_pHYs (2086) — table 9,9,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error; else set res_x, res_y, `unit_type = buf[8]` (unvalidated here)\n\n### png_handle_oFFs (2112) — table 9,9,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error; else signed offsets + `unit_type = buf[8]`\n\n### png_handle_pCAL (2139) — table NoCheck,14,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `endptr - buf <= 12` (after purpose string) -> benign \"invalid\"\n- `(type==PNG_EQUATION_LINEAR && nparams!=2) || (BASE_E && !=3) || (ARBITRARY && !=3) || (HYPERBOLIC && !=4)` -> benign \"invalid parameter count\"\n- `type >= PNG_EQUATION_LAST` -> benign \"unrecognized equation type\" (continues!)\n- `png_malloc_warn(nparams * sizeof png_charp) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- per-param scan: `buf > endptr` -> free params + benign \"invalid data\"\n\n### png_handle_sCAL (2263) — table Limit,4,hIDAT,hIHDR,0\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `buffer[0] != 1 && buffer[0] != 2` -> benign \"invalid unit\"\n- `png_check_fp_number(...)==0 || i >= length || buffer[i++] != 0` -> benign \"bad width format\"\n- `PNG_FP_IS_POSITIVE(state) == 0` -> benign \"non-positive width\"\n- height: `png_check_fp_number(...)==0 || i != length` -> benign \"bad height format\"\n- height `PNG_FP_IS_POSITIVE(state)==0` -> benign \"non-positive height\"\n- only both-positive-and-exact-fit -> `png_set_sCAL_s`, handled_ok\n\n### png_handle_tIME (2337) — table 7,7,0,hIHDR,0\n- `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) != 0` -> `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT` (tIME allowed both sides of IDAT)\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error; else fields from buf[0..6], no field validation here\n\n### png_handle_tEXt (2374) — table NoCheck,2,0,hIHDR,1\n- `user_chunk_cache_max == 1` -> crc_finish, handled_error (silent)\n- `--user_chunk_cache_max == 1` -> benign \"no space in chunk cache\"\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(skip=0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `text != key + length` -> `text++` (skip the NUL); i.e. **no NUL present in chunk** -> `text` points at the terminating 0 -> zero-length text\n- `text_length = strlen(text)`; compression = PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE\n- `png_set_text_2(...) != 0` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- No explicit key-length validation in tEXt (unlike zTXt/iTXt)\n\n### png_handle_zTXt (2446) — table Limit,LKMin(14),0,hIHDR,1\n- three cache-limit branches as tEXt\n- `png_read_buffer(length)` (no +1) `== NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `keyword_length > 79 || keyword_length < 1` -> \"bad keyword\"\n- `keyword_length + 3 > length` -> \"truncated\"\n- `buffer[keyword_length+1] != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE` -> \"unknown compression type\"\n- else `png_decompress_chunk(length, keyword_length+2, &uncompressed_length=PNG_SIZE_MAX, terminate=1)`\n  - `!= Z_STREAM_END` -> errmsg = zstream.msg\n  - `== Z_STREAM_END && read_buffer == NULL` -> \"Read failure in png_handle_zTXt\"\n  - success -> `text.compression = PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`; `png_set_text_2 != 0` -> \"out of memory\"\n\n### png_handle_iTXt (2562) — table NoCheck,6,0,hIHDR,1\n- three cache-limit branches as tEXt\n- `png_read_buffer(length+1) == NULL` -> benign \"out of memory\"\n- `png_crc_finish(0) != 0` -> handled_error\n- `prefix_length > 79 || prefix_length