afe to 64bpp)\n- always: `row_info->width = final_width`, `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, final_width)`\n- `!PNG_READ_PACKSWAP_SUPPORTED` -> `transformations` unused\n\n### png_read_filter_row (4153) + png_init_filter_functions (4116) — 5 filter types × bpp\n- `filter <= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE(0) || filter >= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST(5)` -> **no-op** (NONE = identity; invalid values silently ignored here, caught in png_read_row)\n- `pp->read_filter[0] == NULL` -> `png_init_filter_functions(pp)` (once)\n- `bpp = (pixel_depth + 7) >> 3` -> 1 (1/2/4/8bpp), 2 (16), 3 (24), 4 (32), 6 (48), 8 (64)\n- SUB(1) -> `png_read_filter_row_sub`: loop `i = bpp .. rowbytes-1`, `*rp += *(rp-bpp)`\n- UP(2) -> `png_read_filter_row_up`: full `rowbytes` loop, `*rp += *pp++`\n- AVG(3) -> `png_read_filter_row_avg`: first `bpp` bytes `*rp += *pp/2`; then `rowbytes-bpp` bytes `*rp += (*pp + *(rp-bpp))/2`\n- PAETH(4) with `bpp == 1` -> `png_read_filter_row_paeth_1byte_pixel` (running a/c registers)\n- PAETH(4) with `bpp != 1` -> `png_read_filter_row_paeth_multibyte_pixel` (first pixel = up, then general)\n- Paeth predictor tie-break: `if (pb < pa) {pa=pb; a=b;} if (pc < pa) a = c;`\n- `PNG_USE_ABS` -> `abs()`; else ternary negation\n- `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS` defined -> `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS(pp, bpp)` may replace any entry\n\n### png_read_IDAT_data (4171)\n- `output == NULL` -> `avail_out = 0` (\"checking / swallow\" mode)\n- `zstream.avail_in == 0`:\n  - `while (idat_size == 0)` -> `png_crc_finish(0)` + `png_read_chunk_header`; `chunk_name != png_IDAT` -> `png_error(\"Not enough image data\")`\n  - `avail_in = IDAT_read_size`; `> png_chunk_max` -> clamp; `> idat_size` -> clamp to idat_size\n  - `png_read_buffer(avail_in) == NULL` -> `png_chunk_error(\"out of memory\")`\n- `output != NULL` -> `avail_out_chunk = min(ZLIB_IO_MAX, avail_out)`\n- `output == NULL` -> `next_out = tmpbuf`, `avail_out = sizeof tmpbuf`, counts extra bytes\n- always `PNG_INFLATE(png_ptr, Z_NO_FLUSH)`\n- `ret == Z_STREAM_END` -> `mode |= PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, `flags |= PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`; `zstream.avail_in > 0 || idat_size > 0` -> benign \"Extra compressed data\"; break\n- `ret != Z_OK && output != NULL` -> `png_chunk_error(zstream.msg)`\n- `ret != Z_OK && output == NULL` -> benign `zstream.msg`, return\n- loop `while (avail_out > 0)`\n- after loop `avail_out > 0 && output != NULL` -> `png_error(\"Not enough image data\")`\n- after loop `avail_out > 0 && output == NULL` -> benign \"Too much image data\"\n\n### png_read_finish_IDAT (4308)\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED) == 0` -> `png_read_IDAT_data(NULL, 0)`; if still not ENDED -> force `PNG_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`\n- `zowner == png_IDAT` -> clear next_in/avail_in, `zowner = 0`, `png_crc_finish(idat_size)` (consumes trailing bytes of current IDAT)\n- `zowner != png_IDAT` -> nothing\n\n### png_read_finish_row (4356)\n- `++row_number < num_rows` -> return\n- `interlaced == 0` -> `png_read_finish_IDAT`\n- `interlaced != 0` -> `row_number = 0`, `memset(prev_row, 0, rowbytes+1)`, then loop:\n  - `++pass >= 7` -> break\n  - recompute `iwidth = (width + inc-1 - start)/inc`\n  - `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` -> recompute `num_rows` from `png_pass_yinc/ystart`; loop continues `while (num_rows == 0 || iwidth == 0)` (skips empty passes)\n  - `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` -> break immediately (libpng deinterlacing sees every row; `num_rows` stays = height)\n- `pass < 7` -> return; else `png_read_finish_IDAT`\n\n### png_read_start_row (4407)\n- `READ_TRANSFORMS` -> `png_init_read_transformations`\n- `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` -> `num_rows = (height + yinc[0]-1 - ystart[0])/yinc[0]`\n- `interlaced != 0 && PNG_INTERLACE set` -> `num_rows = height`\n- `interlaced != 0` -> `iwidth = (width + inc[pass]-1 - start[pass])/inc[pass]`\n- `interlaced == 0` -> `num_rows = height`, `iwidth = width`\n- max_pixel_depth escalation ladder (each guard independent, order matters):\n  - `(transformations & PNG_PACK) != 0 && bit_depth < 8` -> 8\n  - `PNG_EXPAND && color_type == PALETTE && num_trans != 0` -> 32; `num_trans == 0` -> 24\n  - `PNG_EXPAND && color_type == GRAY`: `max < 8` -> 8; then `num_trans != 0` -> `*= 2`\n  - `PNG_EXPAND && color_type == RGB && num_trans != 0` -> `*= 4; /= 3`\n  - `PNG_EXPAND_16 && PNG_EXPAND set && bit_depth < 16` -> `*= 2`; `PNG_EXPAND_16 && PNG_EXPAND not set` -> clear `PNG_EXPAND_16`\n  - `PNG_FILLER && color_type == GRAY`: `max <= 8` -> 16 else 32\n  - `PNG_FILLER && (color_type == RGB || PALETTE)`: `max <= 32` -> 32 else 64\n  - `PNG_GRAY_TO_RGB && ((num_trans != 0 && PNG_EXPAND) || PNG_FILLER || color_type == GRAY_ALPHA)`: `max <= 16` -> 32 else 64\n  - `PNG_GRAY_TO_RGB` else-branch: `max <= 8 && color_type == RGB_ALPHA` -> 32; `max <= 8` -> 24; `max > 8 && RGB_ALPHA` -> 64; else 48\n  - `PNG_USER_TRANSFORM && user_transform_depth*user_transform_channels > max` -> that value\n- `maximum_pixel_depth = max_pixel_depth`, `transformed_pixel_depth = 0`\n- `row_bytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(max_pixel_depth, (width+7)&~7) + 1 + ((max_pixel_depth+7)>>3)`\n- `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K && row_bytes > 65536` -> png_error \"This image requires a row greater than 64KB\"\n- `row_bytes + 48 > old_big_row_buf_size` -> free + realloc both buffers:\n  - `interlaced != 0` -> `png_calloc(row_bytes+48)` for big_row_buf (zeroed, needed for combine)\n  - `interlaced == 0` -> `png_malloc(row_bytes+48)`\n  - big_prev_row always `png_malloc`\n  - `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED` -> 16-byte align *pixels* (`temp = big+32; row_buf = temp - (temp&0x0f) - 1`)\n  - else -> `row_buf = big_row_buf + 31`\n- `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K && rowbytes > 65535` -> png_error\n- `rowbytes > PNG_SIZE_MAX - 1` -> png_error \"Row has too many bytes to allocate in memory\"\n- always `memset(prev_row, 0, rowbytes+1)`\n- `read_buffer != NULL` -> free it (sequential reader reallocs on demand)\n- `png_inflate_claim(png_IDAT) != Z_OK` -> `png_error(zstream.msg)`\n- always `flags |= PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT`\n\n---\n\n## 2. pngread.c — sequential API\n\n### png_read_info (92) — chunk loop states\n- `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- always `png_read_sig` first\n- `chunk_name == png_IDAT && (mode & PNG_HAVE_IHDR) == 0` -> `png_chunk_error(\"Missing IHDR before IDAT\")`\n- `chunk_name == png_IDAT && color_type == PALETTE && (mode & PNG_HAVE_PLTE) == 0` -> `png_chunk_error(\"Missing PLTE before IDAT\")`\n- `chunk_name == png_IDAT && (mode & PNG_AFTER_IDAT) != 0` -> benign \"Too many IDATs found\"\n- `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (any) -> `mode |= PNG_HAVE_IDAT`\n- `chunk_name != png_IDAT && (mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) != 0` -> `mode |= PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`\n- `chunk_name == png_IHDR` -> `png_handle_chunk`\n- `chunk_name == png_IEND` -> `png_handle_chunk` (loop continues; only IDAT breaks!)\n- `HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED && (keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(chunk_name)) != 0` -> `png_handle_unknown(..., keep)`; `chunk_name == png_PLTE` -> `mode |= PNG_HAVE_PLTE`; `chunk_name == png_IDAT` -> `idat_size = 0`, **break**\n- `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (normal) -> `idat_size = length`, **break**\n- else -> `png_handle_chunk`\n\n### png_read_update_info (171)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) == 0` -> `png_read_start_row` + (`READ_TRANSFORMS`) `png_read_transform_info(info_ptr)`\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) != 0` (**called twice / after png_start_read_image**) -> `png_app_error(\"png_read_update_info/png_start_read_image: duplicate call\")` and **no re-init**\n\n### png_start_read_image (202)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) == 0` -> `png_read_start_row`\n- else -> `png_app_error(\"png_start_read_image/png_read_update_info: duplicate call\")`\n\n### png_read_row (287) — row/dsp_row NULL × pass skipping\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `(flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) == 0` -> `png_read_start_row` (implicit init)\n- `row_number == 0 && pass == 0` + WARNINGS -> per-transform \"…_SUPPORTED is not defined\" warnings for INVERT_MONO/FILLER/PACKSWAP/PACK/SHIFT/BGR/SWAP_BYTES when write-only-configured\n- interlace skip block, guard `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0`, `switch (pass)`:\n  - pass 0: `row_number & 0x07` -> `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 1: `(row_number & 0x07) || width < 5` -> `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 2: `(row_number & 0x07) != 4` -> `dsp_row != NULL && (row_number & 4)` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 3: `(row_number & 3) || width < 3` -> `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 4: `(row_number & 3) != 2` -> `dsp_row != NULL && (row_number & 2)` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 5: `(row_number & 1) || width < 2` -> `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(display); finish_row; return\n  - pass 6 / default: `(row_number & 1) == 0` -> finish_row; return (**dsp_row never combined**)\n- `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) == 0` -> `png_error(\"Invalid attempt to read row data\")`\n- `row_buf[0] = 255` sentinel then `png_read_IDAT_data(row_buf, row_info.rowbytes + 1)`\n- `row_buf[0] > PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE && < PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST` -> `png_read_filter_row`\n- `row_buf[0] >= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST` -> `png_error(\"bad adaptive filter value\")`\n- `row_buf[0] == 0` -> no filtering\n- always `memcpy(prev_row, row_buf, row_info.rowbytes + 1)`\n- `MNG_FEATURES && (mng_features_permitted & PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64) != 0 && filter_type == PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` -> `png_do_read_intrapixel`\n- `transformations != 0 || (CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX && num_palette_max >= 0)` -> `png_do_read_transformations`\n- `transformed_pixel_depth == 0` -> set from row_info; `row_info.pixel_depth > maximum_pixel_depth` -> `png_error(\"sequential row overflow\")`\n- `transformed_pixel_depth != 0 && != row_info.pixel_depth` -> `png_error(\"internal sequential row size calculation error\")`\n- interlaced + PNG_INTERLACE: `pass < 6` -> `png_do_read_interlace`; `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(1); `row != NULL` -> combine(0)\n- non-interlaced (or PNG_INTERLACE off): `row != NULL` -> combine(-1); `dsp_row != NULL` -> combine(-1)\n- always `png_read_finish_row`; `read_row_fn != NULL` -> callback(row_number, pass)\n\n### png_do_read_intrapixel (225, MNG, sequential only)\n- `(row_info->color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) == 0` -> no-op\n- `bit_depth == 8 && color_type == RGB` -> bpp 3; `== RGB_ALPHA` -> 4; else return\n- `bit_depth == 16 && color_type == RGB` -> bpp 6; `== RGB_ALPHA` -> 8; else return\n- `bit_depth ∉ {8,16}` -> no-op\n\n### png_read_rows (552)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `row != NULL && display_row != NULL` -> `png_read_row(*rp++, *dp++)` × num_rows\n- `row != NULL && display_row == NULL` -> `png_read_row(*rp++, NULL)`\n- `row == NULL && display_row != NULL` -> `png_read_row(NULL, *dp++)`\n- both NULL -> nothing at all (no rows consumed)\n\n### png_read_image (607)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `READ_INTERLACING && (flags & PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT) == 0` -> `pass = png_set_interlace_handling()` then `png_start_read_image()`\n- `READ_INTERLACING && ROW_INIT set && interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` -> `png_warning(\"Interlace handling should be turned on…\")` + force `num_rows = height`, then `pass = png_set_interlace_handling()`\n- `READ_INTERLACING && ROW_INIT set && (not interlaced or INTERLACE already on)` -> `pass = png_set_interlace_handling()`\n- `!READ_INTERLACING && interlaced` -> `png_error(\"Cannot read interlaced image -- interlace handler disabled\")`\n- `!READ_INTERLACING && !interlaced` -> `pass = 1`\n- loop `pass` times over `image_height` rows, always `png_read_row(*rp, NULL)` (display_row unused)\n\n### png_read_end (673)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `!HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED || png_chunk_unknown_handling(png_IDAT) == 0` -> `png_read_finish_IDAT`\n- `READ_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX && color_type == PALETTE && num_palette_max >= num_palette` -> `png_benign_error(\"Read palette index exceeding num_palette\")`\n- loop `do { … } while ((mode & PNG_HAVE_IEND) == 0)`:\n  - `chunk_name != png_IDAT` -> `mode |= PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`\n  - `chunk_name == png_IEND` -> `png_handle_chunk`\n  - `chunk_name == png_IHDR` -> `png_handle_chunk`\n  - `info_ptr == NULL` -> `png_crc_finish(length)` (everything else discarded)\n  - `HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN && (keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(chunk_name)) != 0`:\n    - `chunk_name == png_IDAT && ((length > 0 && !(flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED)) || (mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT) != 0)` -> `png_benign_error(\".Too many IDATs found\")`\n    - then `png_handle_unknown(..., keep)`; `chunk_name == png_PLTE` -> `mode |= PNG_HAVE_PLTE`\n  - `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (normal): `(length > 0 && !ZSTREAM_ENDED) || (mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT) != 0` -> `png_benign_error(\"..Too many IDATs found\")`; then `png_crc_finish(length)` (zero-length trailing IDAT after last IDAT is legal)\n  - else -> `png_handle_chunk`\n\n### png_read_destroy (759) / png_destroy_read_struct (829)\n- unconditional frees: big_row_buf, big_prev_row, read_buffer, palette\n- `READ_GAMMA` -> `png_destroy_gamma_table`\n- `READ_QUANTIZE` -> palette_lookup, quantize_index\n- `tRNS || READ_EXPAND || READ_BACKGROUND` -> trans_alpha\n- always `inflateEnd(&zstream)`\n- `PROGRESSIVE_READ` -> save_buffer\n- `STORE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS && READ_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS` -> unknown_chunk.data\n- `SET_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS` -> chunk_list\n- `READ_EXPAND && (ARM_NEON || RISCV_RVV)` -> riffled_palette\n- setjmp buffer + mem/error callbacks deliberately preserved\n- `png_destroy_read_struct`: `png_ptr_ptr == NULL || *png_ptr_ptr == NULL` -> return; else destroy end_info, info, then `*png_ptr_ptr = NULL`, read_destroy, destroy_png_struct\n\n### png_set_read_status_fn (855)\n- `png_ptr == NULL` -> return; else `read_row_fn = read_row_fn`\n\n### png_read_png (867) — all PNG_TRANSFORM_* + errors\n- `png_ptr == NULL || info_ptr == NULL` -> return\n- `info_ptr->height > PNG_UINT_32_MAX/sizeof(png_bytep)` -> `png_error(\"Image is too high to process with png_read_png()\")`\n- For each flag: supported -> the setter; not compiled in -> `png_app_error(\"PNG_TRANSFORM_X not supported\")`:\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_SCALE_16` -> `png_set_scale_16` / READ_SCALE_16_TO_8\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_16` -> `png_set_strip_16` / READ_STRIP_16_TO_8 (SCALE wins if both)\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_ALPHA` -> `png_set_strip_alpha`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKING` -> `png_set_packing`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_PACKSWAP` -> `png_set_packswap`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_EXPAND` -> `png_set_expand`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_MONO` -> `png_set_invert_mono`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_SHIFT` -> **only if** `(info_ptr->valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) != 0` -> `png_set_shift(&info_ptr->sig_bit)`; no sBIT -> silently nothing\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_BGR` -> `png_set_bgr`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ALPHA` -> `png_set_swap_alpha`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ENDIAN` -> `png_set_swap`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_INVERT_ALPHA` -> `png_set_invert_alpha`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_GRAY_TO_RGB` -> `png_set_gray_to_rgb`\n  - `PNG_TRANSFORM_EXPAND_16` -> `png_set_expand_16`\n- **Not handled at all**: background, gamma, quantize, filler\n- always `png_set_interlace_handling()` then `png_read_update_info`\n- `png_free_data(PNG_FREE_ROWS)`; `info_ptr->row_pointers == NULL` -> allocate height pointers + per-row `png_malloc(info_ptr->rowbytes)`, set `PNG_FREE_ROWS`\n- `row_pointers != NULL` after the free -> reuse (only possible if app-owned)\n- then `png_read_image`, `info_ptr->valid |= PNG_INFO_IDAT`, `png_read_end`; `params` unused\n\n---\n\n## 3. Simplified read API (pngread.c)\n\n### png_image_read_init (1127)\n- `image->opaque != NULL` -> `png_image_error(\"png_image_read: opaque pointer not NULL\")`\n- `png_create_read_struct == NULL` / `png_create_info_struct == NULL` / `png_malloc_warn(control) == NULL` -> unwind + `png_image_error(\"png_image_read: out of memory\")`\n- success -> `memset(image,0,…)`, `image->version = PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`, `control->for_write = 0`, return 1\n\n### png_image_begin_read_from_stdio (1336)\n- `image == NULL` -> return 0\n- `image != NULL && image->version != PNG_IMAGE_VERSION` -> \"incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"\n- `file == NULL` -> \"png_image_begin_read_from_stdio: invalid argument\"\n- `png_image_read_init == 0` -> return 0 (error already set)\n- else `io_ptr = file`, `png_safe_execute(png_image_read_header)`\n\n### png_image_begin_read_from_file (1366)\n- version mismatch -> \"incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"; `image == NULL` -> 0\n- `file_name == NULL` -> \"invalid argument\"\n- `fopen(file_name,\"rb\") == NULL` -> `png_image_error(strerror(errno))`\n- `png_image_read_init == 0` -> `fclose(fp)` then 0\n- success -> `io_ptr = fp`, `owned_file = 1`, safe_execute(read_header)\n\n### png_image_begin_read_from_memory (1435)\n- version mismatch -> \"incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION\"; `image == NULL` -> 0\n- `memory == NULL || size == 0` -> \"invalid argument\"\n- `png_image_read_init == 0` -> 0\n- success -> `opaque->memory/size`, `io_ptr = image`, `read_data_fn = png_image_memory_read`, safe_execute(read_header)\n- `png_image_memory_read` (1405): `png_ptr == NULL` -> return; `image == NULL || cp == NULL` -> `png_error(\"invalid memory read\")`; `memory == NULL || size < need` -> `png_error(\"read beyond end of data\")`; else memcpy + advance\n\n### png_image_read_header (1275)\n- `BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` -> `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)` before `png_read_info`\n- `format = png_image_format(png_ptr)` (1176): `color_type & COLOR` -> `FLAG_COLOR`; `color_type & ALPHA` -> `FLAG_ALPHA`; `else if num_trans > 0` -> `FLAG_ALPHA`; `bit_depth == 16` -> `FLAG_LINEAR`; `color_type & PALETTE` -> `FLAG_COLORMAP`\n- `(format & PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLOR) != 0 && png_image_is_not_sRGB(png_ptr)` -> `flags |= PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB` (never set for grayscale)\n- `png_image_is_not_sRGB` (1248): `png_has_chunk(cICP) || png_has_chunk(mDCV)` -> `!chromaticities_match_sRGB(&chromaticities)`; else `png_has_chunk(sRGB)` -> 0; else `png_has_chunk(cHRM)` -> `!chromaticities_match_sRGB`; else 0\n- `chromaticities_match_sRGB` (1204): any of 8 `PNG_OUT_OF_RANGE(..., sRGB_TOLERANCE=1000)` -> 0\n- colormap_entries: `color_type == GRAY` -> `1U << bit_depth`; `== PALETTE` -> `num_palette`; default -> 256; then `> 256` -> clamp 256\n\n### png_gamma_not_sRGB (1234)\n- `g < PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MIN || g > PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MAX` -> 0 (includes g == 0)\n- else `png_gamma_significant((g*11+2)/5)`\n\n### set_file_encoding (1527) / decode_gamma (1555)\n- `png_resolve_file_gamma(png_ptr) == 0` -> `png_error(\"internal: default gamma not set\")`\n- `png_gamma_significant(g) != 0 && png_gamma_not_sRGB(g) != 0` -> `file_encoding = P_FILE`, `gamma_to_linear = png_reciprocal(g)`\n- `png_gamma_significant(g) != 0 && sRGB-ish` -> `P_sRGB`\n- `png_gamma_significant(g) == 0` -> `P_LINEAR8`\n- decode_gamma: `encoding == P_FILE` -> re-resolve to `file_encoding`; `== P_NOTSET` -> `set_file_encoding` first; then P_FILE -> `png_gamma_16bit_correct(v*257, gamma_to_linear)`; P_sRGB -> `png_sRGB_table[v]`; P_LINEAR -> unchanged; P_LINEAR8 -> `*= 257`; `__GNUC__ default` -> `png_error(\"unexpected encoding (internal error)\")`\n\n### png_create_colormap_entry (1631) — BGR/AFIRST/LINEAR\n- `output_encoding = (format & FLAG_LINEAR) ? P_LINEAR : P_sRGB`\n- `convert_to_Y = (format & FLAG_COLOR) == 0 && (red != green || green != blue)`\n- `ip > 255` -> `png_error(\"color-map index out of range\")`\n- `encoding == P_FILE && file_encoding == P_NOTSET` -> `set_file_encoding` then re-read\n- `encoding == P_FILE`: gamma-correct RGB; `convert_to_Y != 0 || output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> `alpha *= 257`, encoding = P_LINEAR; else -> `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR`×3, encoding = P_sRGB\n- `encoding == P_LINEAR8` -> `*= 257` all four, encoding = P_LINEAR\n- `encoding == P_sRGB && (convert_to_Y != 0 || output_encoding == P_LINEAR)` -> table lookup ×3, `alpha *= 257`, encoding = P_LINEAR\n- `encoding == P_LINEAR && convert_to_Y != 0`: `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> `y = (y+16384)>>15`; else -> sRGB-encode y, `alpha = PNG_DIV257(alpha)`, encoding = P_sRGB\n- `encoding == P_LINEAR && convert_to_Y == 0 && output_encoding == P_sRGB` -> sRGB-encode RGB, `alpha = PNG_DIV257`, encoding = P_sRGB\n- `encoding != output_encoding` -> `png_error(\"bad encoding (internal error)\")`\n- `afirst = FORMAT_AFIRST_SUPPORTED && (format & FLAG_AFIRST) != 0 && (format & FLAG_ALPHA) != 0`, else 0\n- `bgr = FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED && (format & FLAG_BGR) != 0 ? 2 : 0`\n- `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> uint16 entry; `SAMPLE_CHANNELS` 4 -> alpha at `afirst?0:3` FALLTHROUGH; 3 -> `alpha < 65535 && alpha > 0` -> premultiply RGB; `alpha == 0` -> `red=green=blue=0`; write `[afirst+(2^bgr)], [afirst+1], [afirst+bgr]`; 2 -> alpha at `1^afirst` FALLTHROUGH; 1 -> premultiply green, write `[afirst]`\n- `output_encoding == P_sRGB` -> byte entry, same channel placement, **no premultiplication**\n\n### Colormap builders\n- `make_gray_file_colormap` (1852): 256 entries `(i,i,i,255,P_FILE)`\n- `make_gray_colormap` (1863): 256 entries `(i,i,i,255,P_sRGB)`; `PNG_GRAY_COLORMAP_ENTRIES 256`\n- `make_ga_colormap` (1875): 231 gray `(i*256+115)/231`, 1 transparent `(255,255,255,0)`, then `a=1..4 × g=0..5` -> `(g*51,…,a*51)`; total 256\n- `make_rgb_colormap` (1930): 6×6×6 opaque -> 216 entries; `PNG_RGB_INDEX(r,g,b) = 6*(6*DIV51(r)+DIV51(g))+DIV51(b)`\n\n### png_image_read_colormap (1959) — full decision tree\nAlpha-removal / background prologue:\n- `((color_type & MASK_ALPHA) != 0 || num_trans > 0) && (output_format & FLAG_ALPHA) == 0`:\n  - `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> `back_r=back_g=back_b=0` (compose on black; background arg ignored)\n  - `display->background == NULL` -> `png_error(\"background color must be supplied to remove alpha/transparency\")`\n  - `background != NULL` -> `back_g = background->green`; `(output_format & FLAG_COLOR) != 0` -> also red/blue;