& back_g==back_b)` -> error if `256 > colormap_entries` (\"gray-alpha color-map: too few entries\"); `make_gray_colormap`; `P_LINEAR` -> sRGB-ify gray + patch entry; `png_set_background_fixed`; `PNG_CMAP_NONE`\n  - alpha removed and colored non-gray background -> error if `256 > colormap_entries` (\"ga-alpha color-map: too few entries\"); 231 opaque grays, `background_index = 231`, entry 231 = background at `P_LINEAR?65535:255`, then `output_encoding == P_sRGB` -> linearize back_* via `png_sRGB_table`; `a=1..4 × g=0..5` composed entries; `PNG_CMAP_GA`\n- **RGB / RGB_ALPHA, `(output_format & FLAG_COLOR) == 0`** (output gray): `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed(PNG_ERROR_ACTION_NONE,-1,-1)`; `data_encoding = P_sRGB`\n  - `(color_type == RGB_ALPHA || num_trans > 0) && (output_format & FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` -> `expand_tRNS = 1`; error if `256 > colormap_entries` (\"rgb[ga] color-map: too few entries\"); `make_ga_colormap`; `background_index = 231`; `PNG_CMAP_GA`\n  - else: error if `256 > colormap_entries` (\"rgb[gray] color-map: too few entries\")\n    - `(color_type == RGB_ALPHA || num_trans > 0) && png_gamma_not_sRGB(png_resolve_file_gamma) != 0` -> `make_gray_file_colormap`, `data_encoding = P_FILE` (avoids double-gamma bug)\n    - else -> `make_gray_colormap`\n    - `color_type == RGB_ALPHA || num_trans > 0` -> patch background entry: `data_encoding == P_FILE` -> `output_encoding == P_sRGB` -> `gray = png_sRGB_table[gray]`; `gray = PNG_DIV257(png_gamma_16bit_correct(gray, gamma))`; overwrite entry; `data_encoding != P_FILE && output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> `gray = PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(gray*255)` + overwrite; then `expand_tRNS = 1` + `png_set_background_fixed`\n    - `PNG_CMAP_NONE`\n- **RGB / RGB_ALPHA, output color**: `data_encoding = P_sRGB`\n  - `(color_type == RGB_ALPHA || num_trans > 0) && (output_format & FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` -> error if `216+1+27=244 > colormap_entries` (\"rgb+alpha color-map: too few entries\"); `make_rgb_colormap`; transparent entry at 216, `background_index = 216`; 27 half-alpha entries (`r,g,b ∈ {0,127,255}`, alpha 128); `expand_tRNS = 1`; `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA`\n  - `(color_type == RGB_ALPHA || num_trans > 0) && no output alpha` -> error if `244 > colormap_entries` (\"rgb-alpha color-map: too few entries\"); `make_rgb_colormap`; add background entry at 216; `output_encoding == P_LINEAR` -> sRGB-ify r/g/b for the index computation\n    - `memcmp(colormap + sample_size*216, colormap + sample_size*PNG_RGB_INDEX(r,g,b), sample_size) != 0` -> `background_index = 216`, 27 composed entries via `png_colormap_compose(..., 128, back_*, output_encoding)`, `expand_tRNS = 1`, `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA`\n    - memcmp == 0 (background already in the 6×6×6 cube) -> `png_set_background_fixed`, `PNG_CMAP_RGB`\n  - no alpha/tRNS in input -> error if `216 > colormap_entries` (\"rgb color-map: too few entries\"); `make_rgb_colormap`; `PNG_CMAP_RGB`\n- **PALETTE**: `num_trans = png_ptr->num_trans`, `trans = num_trans > 0 ? trans_alpha : NULL`; `trans == NULL` -> `num_trans = 0`; `do_background = trans != NULL && (output_format & FLAG_ALPHA) == 0`; `PNG_CMAP_NONE`, `data_encoding = P_FILE`; `cmap_entries = min(num_palette, 256)`; `> image->colormap_entries` -> error \"palette color-map: too few entries\"\n  - per entry: `do_background != 0 && i < num_trans && trans[i] < 255`:\n    - `trans[i] == 0` -> entry = `(back_r,back_g,back_b,0,output_encoding)`\n    - `0 < trans[i] < 255` -> entry = `png_colormap_compose` per channel, alpha `output_encoding == P_LINEAR ? trans[i]*257 : trans[i]`\n  - else -> `(palette[i].rgb, i < num_trans ? trans[i] : 255, P_FILE)`\n  - `bit_depth < 8` -> `png_set_packing`\n- **default** -> `png_error(\"invalid PNG color type\")`\n\nEpilogue:\n- `expand_tRNS != 0 && num_trans > 0 && (color_type & MASK_ALPHA) == 0` -> `png_set_tRNS_to_alpha`\n- `data_encoding == P_sRGB` -> `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed(PNG_ALPHA_PNG, PNG_GAMMA_sRGB)` FALLTHROUGH\n- `data_encoding ∈ {P_sRGB, P_FILE} && bit_depth > 8` -> `png_set_scale_16`\n- `data_encoding == P_NOTSET` (`__GNUC__`) -> `png_error(\"bad data option (internal error)\")`\n- `cmap_entries > 256 || > image->colormap_entries` -> `png_error(\"color map overflow (BAD internal error)\")`\n- background_index cross-check: CMAP_NONE must be 256; GA must be 231; TRANS must be 254 **and** `< cmap_entries`; RGB must be 256; RGB_ALPHA must be 216; else `png_error(\"bad background index (internal error)\")` / `\"bad processing option (internal error)\"`\n\n### png_image_read_and_map (2812)\n- `interlaced == PNG_INTERLACE_NONE` -> `passes = 1`; `== ADAM7` -> `PNG_INTERLACE_ADAM7_PASSES(7)`; else `png_error(\"unknown interlace type\")`\n- ADAM7 per pass: `PNG_PASS_COLS(width, pass) == 0` -> `continue` (empty pass); else `startx/stepx/y/stepy` from PASS macros\n- non-interlaced -> `y=0, startx=0, stepx=stepy=1`\n- `switch (proc)`:\n  - `PNG_CMAP_GA`: `alpha > 229` -> `entry = (231*gray+128)>>8`; `alpha < 26` -> `entry = 231`; else `entry = 226 + 6*DIV51(alpha) + DIV51(gray)`\n  - `PNG_CMAP_TRANS`: `alpha == 0` -> `254`; `gray != 254` -> `gray`; `gray == 254` -> `255`\n  - `PNG_CMAP_RGB`: `PNG_RGB_INDEX(inrow[0..2])`, stride 3\n  - `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA`: `alpha >= 196` -> `PNG_RGB_INDEX`; `alpha < 64` -> `216`; else `back_i = 217` + `inrow[0]&0x80 ? +9`, `&0x40 ? +9`, `inrow[1]&0x80/0x40 ? +3`, `inrow[2]&0x80/0x40 ? +1`; stride 4\n  - `default` -> break (no processing)\n\n### png_image_read_colormapped (3001)\n- `PNG_SKIP_CHUNKS(png_ptr)` -> `HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED` -> keep NEVER for everything except {IHDR,PLTE,IDAT,IEND} ∪ {bKGD,cHRM,cICP,gAMA,mDCV,sBIT,sRGB} (and tRNS); else no-op\n- `colormap_processing == PNG_CMAP_NONE` -> `passes = png_set_interlace_handling(png_ptr)` (direct read into user buffer)\n- `colormap_processing != PNG_CMAP_NONE` -> `passes` stays 0 (local row + map)\n- always `png_read_update_info`\n- output format verification, `goto bad_output` -> `png_error(\"bad color-map processing (internal error)\")`:\n  - `PNG_CMAP_NONE` requires `(info_ptr->color_type == PALETTE || == GRAY) && bit_depth == 8`\n  - `PNG_CMAP_TRANS` / `PNG_CMAP_GA` require `color_type == GRAY_ALPHA && bit_depth == 8 && screen_gamma == PNG_GAMMA_sRGB && colormap_entries == 256`\n  - `PNG_CMAP_RGB` requires `color_type == RGB && bit_depth == 8 && screen_gamma == PNG_GAMMA_sRGB && colormap_entries == 216`\n  - `PNG_CMAP_RGB_ALPHA` requires `color_type == RGB_ALPHA && bit_depth == 8 && screen_gamma == PNG_GAMMA_sRGB && colormap_entries == 244`\n- `row_step (= row_stride) < 0` -> `first_row = buffer + (height-1)*(-row_step)` (bottom-up); `>= 0` -> `first_row = buffer`\n- `passes == 0` -> `png_malloc(png_get_rowbytes)` local_row + `png_safe_execute(png_image_read_and_map)` + free\n- `passes > 0` -> direct loop `passes × height` × `png_read_row(row, NULL)`, `row += row_step`\n\n### png_image_read_direct (3617) — the transform-setup decision tree\n- always `png_set_expand(png_ptr)` first\n- `base_format = png_image_format(png_ptr) & ~PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP`; `change = format ^ base_format`\n- `(change & FLAG_COLOR) != 0 && (format & FLAG_COLOR) != 0` -> `png_set_gray_to_rgb`\n- `(change & FLAG_COLOR) != 0 && output gray`: `(base_format & FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` -> `do_local_background = 1/*maybe*/`; then `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed(PNG_ERROR_ACTION_NONE, DEFAULT, DEFAULT)`\n- input gamma default: `(base_format & FLAG_LINEAR) != 0 && (flags & PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB) == 0` -> `PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR`; else `PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB`; then `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed(PNG_ALPHA_PNG, that)`\n- `linear != 0 && (base_format & FLAG_ALPHA) != 0` -> `mode = PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD`, `output_gamma = PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR`\n- `linear != 0 && no input alpha` -> `mode = PNG_ALPHA_PNG`, `output_gamma = PNG_GAMMA_LINEAR`\n- `linear == 0` -> `mode = PNG_ALPHA_PNG`, `output_gamma = PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB`\n- `(change & FLAG_ASSOCIATED_ALPHA) != 0` -> `mode = PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED`, clear the bit\n- `do_local_background != 0`:\n  - `png_muldiv(&gtest, output_gamma, png_resolve_file_g