{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mhalax3lka7pa47wzctpe4wlcsnna4o3uchwvm2ntpn6y7fyt4ta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Written to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/.work/errors_setget.md` — **252 rows**, table body only, 4 columns, `NNN` placeholder in column 1. 161 rows anchored in `pngset.c`, 91 in `pngget.c`. Every row cites a real `file:line`; no invented conditions.\n\n**Key build-config finding that changes the semantics of many rows.** The task statement said \"every `#define` in `pnglibconf.h` is ON\" — that is not quite true, and the exception matters:\n\n- `pnglibconf.h:24` → `/*#undef PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED*/` (**OFF**); `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` are ON.\n- `png.h:310` → `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE = PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BETA` (2) `< PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC` (3), so `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0` (`pngpriv.h:447`).\n\nConsequently, by default in this build:\n- `png_app_error` and `png_app_warning` both resolve to **`png_error` (fatal longjmp)** on read *and* write, because `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN`/`PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` are never set (`pngread.c:66-69`, `pngwrite.c:605-608` are behind `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD`). They only degrade to warnings after `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)`.\n- `png_benign_error` → warning on a read struct, **fatal `png_error` on a write struct**.\n- `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR)` → non-fatal `png_chunk_warning` on read, **fatal on write** (`pngerror.c:486-512`).\n- `PNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED` is off, so `png_fixed`/`png_fixed_ITU` are the real functions (`png.c:2726`, `png.c:2745`) and produce `png_error \"fixed point overflow in <text>\"`.\n\n**Notable things the enumeration surfaced:**\n- `png_set_iCCP` (`pngset.c:903-904`) has **no `return`** after `png_app_error(\"Invalid iCCP compression method\")` — if benign errors are enabled the bad compression method is accepted and the profile stored anyway.\n- `png_set_cICP` (`pngset.c:145-154`) writes all four `cicp_*` fields into `info_ptr` *before* rejecting a non-zero `matrix_coefficients`; same pattern in `png_set_IHDR` (fields stored at 445-451 before `png_check_IHDR`).\n- `png_set_tRNS` with `trans_alpha != NULL` and `num_trans` out of `1..256` (`pngset.c:1198/1205/1233`) issues **no diagnostic at all**, leaves `trans_alpha = safe_trans` pointing at an uninitialised stack buffer, and still sets `PNG_INFO_tRNS` at line 1269 with the bogus `num_trans`.\n- `png_set_sPLT`'s `continue` at `pngset.c:1329` decrements `nentries` but does not advance `entries`, so the same invalid entry is re-tested each iteration.\n- `png_set_text_2` returns **0 (the success sentinel)** for the outright-invalid-argument case at `pngset.c:963-964`.\n- Two getters can longjmp: `png_get_IHDR` (`pngget.c:974` → `png_error \"Invalid IHDR data\"`) and `png_get_sCAL_fixed` (`pngget.c:1047` → `png_error \"fixed point overflow in sCAL width\"`).\n- Four functions have **missing** NULL guards (flagged as rows): `png_set_benign_errors` (`pngset.c:1936`), `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` (`pngset.c:1960`), `png_get_io_state` (`pngget.c:1346`), `png_get_io_chunk_type` (`pngget.c:1352`). `png_set_eXIf`/`png_get_eXIf` also call `png_warning(png_ptr, ...)` with no NULL check.\n- Two rows are explicitly marked **not compiled in this build** (`\"iTXt chunk not supported\"` at `pngset.c:1063`; `\"no unknown chunk support on read\"/\"...on write\"` at `pngset.c:1442/1451`).\n- `png_get_palette_max` (`pngget.c:1364`) is the only `-1` failure sentinel in either file.\n- I expanded `png_check_IHDR` (`png.c:1969-2121`) into its 15 individual rejections under the `png_set_IHDR` call site, since that is where all IHDR range/consistency checking actually happens, plus one row for the `png_get_IHDR` call site."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_read_input_tokens":140611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":198,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BArDj2a34KBbp2djFxPFtZ","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"02fd70d8-78e5-4670-8b7c-8da1ba0acc83","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:33:13.479Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"ERRORS table: set/get"}
