pass > 7` after increment → `pass--`.\n - 125c. `pass >= 7` → break (done).\n - 125d. recompute `iwidth`; `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → break here (num_rows left unchanged).\n - 125e. else recompute `num_rows`; loop again while `iwidth == 0 || num_rows == 0`.\n\n## Callback hooks\n126. `png_push_have_info`: `info_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called with `(png_ptr, info_ptr)`.\n127. `png_push_have_end`: `end_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called.\n128. `png_push_have_row`: `row_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called with `(row, row_number, pass)`; `row` is either `row_buf+1` or NULL.\n\n## png_progressive_combine_row (pngpread.c:907)\n129. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n130. `new_row == NULL` → return without combining (empty interlace row).\n131. `new_row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(png_ptr, old_row, 1 /*blocky*/)`. NOTE: `new_row` is used purely as a flag; no check that it equals `row_buf+1`; `old_row` is not NULL-checked.\n\n## png_set_progressive_read_fn (pngpread.c:923)\n132. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n133. Any combination of `info_fn`/`row_fn`/`end_fn` NULL or non-NULL is accepted verbatim (all-NULL is legal → silent decode).\n134. Always calls `png_set_read_fn(png_ptr, progressive_ptr, png_push_fill_buffer)` → inherits pngrio.c branch: if `write_data_fn != NULL` it is cleared with a warning; `output_flush_fn` set to NULL.\n135. `png_get_progressive_ptr`: `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL; else `io_ptr`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. png.c\n\n## png_set_sig_bytes (png.c:53)\n136. `png_ptr == NULL` → return. 137. `num_bytes < 0` → treated as 0. 138. `nb > 8` (incl. large positive) → `png_error(\"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")`. 139. `0 <= nb <= 8` → stored.\n\n## png_sig_cmp (png.c:80)\n140. `num_to_check > 8` → clamped to 8.\n141. `num_to_check < 1` (0, or negative-cast-to-huge does not hit this) → return **-1** without touching `sig`.\n142. `start > 7` → return -1.\n143. `start + num_to_check > 8` → `num_to_check = 8 - start`.\n144. else → `memcmp(&sig[start], &