itch to FRACTION (delayed) then accept digit. 314. INTEGER+DIGIT otherwise → accept, mark WAS_VALID.\n315. INTEGER+E with no SAW_DIGIT → stop. 316. INTEGER+E with SAW_DIGIT → switch to EXPONENT.\n317. FRACTION+DIGIT → accept, WAS_VALID. 318. FRACTION+E with no digit (\".E\") → stop. 319. FRACTION+E with digit → EXPONENT. 320. FRACTION+SIGN/FRACTION+DOT → fall to default → stop.\n321. EXPONENT+SIGN with SAW_ANY set → stop. 322. EXPONENT+SIGN clean → accept.\n323. EXPONENT+DIGIT → accept, WAS_VALID. 324. EXPONENT+DOT / EXPONENT+E → default → stop.\n325. `i` reaches `size` → loop ends naturally.\n326. Return `(state & PNG_FP_SAW_DIGIT) != 0` — 1 if at least one digit in the *current* state segment.\n327. `size == 0` → loop never runs, returns based on incoming `*statep`.\n\n## png_check_fp_string (png.c:2261)\n328. `png_check_fp_number != 0 && (char_index == size || string[char_index] == 0)` → return non-zero `state`.\n329. number invalid → 0. 330. number valid but trailing garbage (`char_index < size && string[char_index] != 0`) → 0.\n\n## png_pow10 (png.c:2280)\n331. `power < DBL_MIN_10_EXP` → return 0. 332. `power < 0` → reciprocal path. 333. `power == 0` → return 1. 334. `power > 0` → bitwise decomposition.\n\n## png_ascii_from_fp (png.c:2317)\n335. `precision < 1` → `precision = DBL_DIG`.\n336. `precision > DBL_DIG+1` → clamp to `DBL_DIG+1`.\n337. `size < precision+5` → skip everything → `png_error(\"ASCII conversion buffer too small\")`.\n338. `fp < 0` → emit `'-'`, negate, `--size`.\n339. `DBL_MIN <= fp <= DBL_MAX` → main digit-generation path.\n340. `!(fp >= DBL_MIN)` (zero, denormal, or NaN) → emit `\"0\"`, return.\n341. else (`fp > DBL_MAX`, i.e. +inf) → emit `\"inf\"`, return.\nWithin the main path:\n342. `exp_b10 < 0 && exp_b10 > -3` → `czero = -exp_b10` leading zeros, `exp_b10 = 0`.\n343. otherwise `czero = 0`.\n344. per-digit: `cdigits+czero+1 < precision+clead` → `modf` split; else final rounded digit via `floor(fp+.5)`.\n345. rounded digit `d > 9 && cze