return).\n532. `BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` clear && (write struct or `chunk_name == 0`) → `png_error` (noreturn).\n533. `!PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` → function absent (and `png_benign_error` is macro'd to `png_error` in pngpriv.h).\n\n## png_app_warning (pngerror.c:338)\n534. `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` set → `png_warning`. 535. clear → `png_error`.\n\n## png_app_error (pngerror.c:351)\n536. `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` set → `png_warning`. 537. clear → `png_error`.\n\n## png_format_buffer (pngerror.c:380)\n538. Per chunk-name byte: `isnonalpha(c)` i.e. `c < 65 || c > 122 || (c > 90 && c < 97)` → emit `[HH]` (4 chars); else emit the char (1).\n539. `error_message == NULL` → terminate right after the name.\n540. `error_message != NULL` → append `\": \"` then up to `PNG_MAX_ERROR_TEXT-1 = 195` chars, then NUL. Worst case 4*4+2+195+1 = 214 > the callers' `msg[18+196] = 214` — exactly fits.\n\n## png_chunk_error (pngerror.c:426) — READ && ERROR_TEXT\n541. `png_ptr == NULL` → `png_error(NULL, error_message)` (which goes to `png_default_error` → `png_longjmp(NULL,1)` → `PNG_ABORT()`).\n542. `png_ptr != NULL` → prefix chunk name, `png_error(msg)`.\n\n## png_chunk_warning (pngerror.c:443) — WARNINGS\n543. `png_ptr == NULL` → `png_warning(NULL, warning_message)`. 544. else prefixed then `png_warning`.\n\n## png_chunk_benign_error (pngerror.c:460) — READ && BENIGN_ERRORS\n545. `PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` set → `png_chunk_warning`. 546. clear → `png_chunk_error`.\n\n## png_chunk_report (pngerror.c:477)\n547. READ+WRITE build && `(mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT) != 0` && `error < PNG_CHUNK_ERROR` → `png_chunk_warning`.\n548. read struct && `error >= PNG_CHUNK_ERROR` → `png_chunk_benign_error`.\n549. READ+WRITE build && `(mode & PNG_IS_READ_STRUCT) == 0` && `error < PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR` → `png_app_warning`.\n550. write struct && `error >= PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR` → `png_app_error`.\n551. READ-only build → the read pair only, `mode` untested.\n552. WRITE-only build → the write pair only.\n\n## png_fixed_error (pngerror.c:518) — ERROR_TEXT && FLOATING_POINT\n553. `name == NULL` → message is just `\"fixed point overflow in \"`. 554. `name != NULL` → appended, truncated at 195 chars. Always `png_error`.\n\n## png_set_longjmp_fn (pngerror.c:544) — SETJMP only\n555. `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL.\n556. `jmp_buf_ptr == NULL && jmp_buf_size <= sizeof(jmp_buf_local)` → use the built-in buffer, `jmp_buf_size = 0` (marker for \"not allocated\"); never fails.\n557. `jmp_buf_ptr == NULL && jmp_buf_size > sizeof(jmp_buf_local)` && `png_malloc_warn` succeeds → allocated, `jmp_buf_size = jmp_buf_size`.\n558. same but `png_malloc_warn` returns NULL → return NULL (OOM, new in 1.6).\n559. `jmp_buf_ptr != NULL && jmp_buf_size == 0 && jmp_buf_ptr == &jmp_buf_local` → effective `size = sizeof(jmp_buf_local)`.\n560. `jmp_buf_ptr != NULL && jmp_buf_size == 0 && jmp_buf_ptr != &jmp_buf_local` → `png_error(\"Libpng jmp_buf still allocated\")` (internal inconsistency).\n561. `jmp_buf_ptr != NULL && size != jmp_buf_size` → `png_warning(\"Application jmp_buf size changed\")` + return NULL.\n562. `jmp_buf_ptr != NULL && size == jmp_buf_size` → reuse.\n563. All success paths finally set `longjmp_fn = longjmp_fn` (may be NULL — then `png_longjmp` aborts) and return `jmp_buf_ptr`.\n\n## png_free_jmpbuf (pngerror.c:613)\n564. `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op.\n565. `jb == NULL` → skip to the unconditional reset.\n566. `jmp_buf_size == 0` (stack allocation) → skip the free, just reset.\n567. `jb != NULL && jmp_buf_size > 0 && jb == &jmp_buf_local` → skip the free (inconsistent state), reset.\n568. `jb != NULL && jmp_buf_size > 0 && jb != &jmp_buf_local` → set up a local `free_jmp_buf`, `setjmp` returns 0 → point `jmp_buf_ptr` at it, `longjmp_fn = longjmp`, `png_free(jb)`.\n569. same but the `png_free` errors and longjmps back → `setjmp` returns non-zero → the free is skipped (leak accepted).\n570. All paths end with `jmp_buf_size = 0; jmp_buf_ptr = NULL; longjmp_fn = 0`.\n\n## png_longjmp (pnge