{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"adfb220cbf244a475","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TH7VyeT7Ax7BCxGeRkuf7Q","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-XkCeuj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-GjGJaF/d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7/tasks/adfb220cbf244a475.output","summary":"Read all eight files (plus checked cross-file locations for functions that aren't actually in these files). Enumeration below.\n\n---\n\n# 1. pngpread.c — progressive reader\n\n## Mode constants (file-local, lines 18-25)\n`PNG_READ_SIG_MODE 0`, `PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE 1`, `PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE 2`, `PNG_READ_tEXt_MODE 4`, `PNG_READ_zTXt_MODE 5`, `PNG_READ_DONE_MODE 6`, `PNG_READ_iTXt_MODE 7`, `PNG_ERROR_MODE 8`.\nNOTE: there is **no** `PNG_SKIP_MODE` and no `PNG_READ_ERROR_MODE` in this file; `tEXt/zTXt/iTXt/ERROR` modes are never assigned by any code — only 0, 1, 2, 6 are ever stored into `process_mode`.\n\n## png_process_data (pngpread.c:50)\n1. `png_ptr == NULL` → return (no-op).\n2. `info_ptr == NULL` → return (no-op).\n3. both non-NULL → `png_push_restore_buffer(buffer, buffer_size)` then `while (png_ptr->buffer_size) png_process_some_data(...)`.\n4. sub-case `buffer_size == 0 && save_buffer_size == 0` → loop body never executes.\n5. sub-case `buffer_size == 0 && save_buffer_size > 0` → loop runs on the saved bytes only.\n6. Loop-nontermination configuration: any state where the mode handler consumes 0 bytes and doesn't call `png_push_save_buffer` (which zeroes `buffer_size`).\n\n## png_process_data_pause (pngpread.c:65)\n7. `png_ptr == NULL` → return 0.\n8. `save != 0` → `png_push_save_buffer()` (which sets `buffer_size = 0`), return 0.\n9. `save == 0 && save_buffer_size < buffer_size` → `buffer_size = 0`, return `buffer_size - save_buffer_size`.\n10. `save == 0 && save_buffer_size >= buffer_size` → `buffer_size = 0`, return 0.\n\n## png_process_data_skip (pngpread.c:92)\n11. Unconditional `png_app_warning(...)` then return 0. Sub-branch inherited from `png_app_warning`: `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` set → warning + returns 0; clear → `png_error` (longjmp, no return).\n\n## png_process_some_data (pngpread.c:108)\n12. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n13. `process_mode == PNG_READ_SIG_MODE(0)` → `png_push_read_sig`.\n14. `process_mode == PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE(1)` → `png_push_read_chunk`.\n15. `process_mode == PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE(2)` → `png_push_read_IDAT`.\n16. `default` (3,4,5,`PNG_READ_DONE_MODE 6`,7,8, any other) → `buffer_size = 0` (silently discards all remaining input; this is the only DONE-mode behaviour, no error).\n\n### Transitions\n17. SIG → CHUNK when `sig_bytes >= 8` after the copy.\n18. CHUNK → IDAT when `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (set at pngpread.c:219, and again at 272).\n19. CHUNK → DONE when `chunk_name == png_IEND` (after `png_handle_chunk`, then `png_push_have_end`).\n20. IDAT → CHUNK when a fresh chunk header is read whose `chunk_name != png_IDAT`.\n21. No transition ever sets `PNG_ERROR_MODE`; errors go via `png_error`/longjmp.\n\n## png_push_read_sig (pngpread.c:148)\nGuards: `num_checked = sig_bytes` (0..8), `num_to_check = 8 - num_checked`, clamped to `buffer_size`.\n22. `sig_bytes == 0, buffer_size >= 8` → check all 8, transition to CHUNK.\n23. `sig_bytes == 0, buffer_size == n (1..7)` → partial check of n bytes, stay in SIG mode.\n24. `sig_bytes == k (1..7), buffer_size >= 8-k` → completes signature, → CHUNK.\n25. `sig_bytes == k (1..7), buffer_size < 8-k` → partial, stay in SIG.\n26. `sig_bytes == 8` (e.g. after `png_set_sig_bytes(8)`) → `num_to_check = 8-8 = 0`; `png_push_fill_buffer(...,0)` copies nothing; `png_sig_cmp(sig, 8, 0)` → `num_to_check < 1` → returns -1 ≠ 0 → enters the mismatch branch → since `num_checked(8) >= 4`, `png_error(\"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\")`. **Distinguishable degenerate config.**\n27. `buffer_size == 0` with `sig_bytes < 8` → `num_to_check = 0` → `png_sig_cmp(sig, k, 0)` returns -1 → mismatch path. If `k < 4`: second call `png_sig_cmp(sig, k, 0-4)` with `num_to_check` underflowed to `SIZE_MAX-3` → clamped to 8 then `8-k`, compares real bytes; if those match → `png_error(\"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\")` else `png_error(\"Not a PNG file\")`. **Underflow-dependent config.**\n28. Mismatch with `num_checked < 4` and second `png_sig_cmp(sig, num_checked, num_to_check-4) != 0` → `png_error(\"Not a PNG file\")`.\n29. Mismatch with `num_checked < 4` and second compare == 0 → `png_error(\"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\")`.\n30. Mismatch with `num_checked >= 4` → `png_error(\"PNG file corrupted by ASCII conversion\")`.\n31. Match but `sig_bytes < 8` → stay SIG mode (no error, no transition).\n\n## png_push_read_chunk (pngpread.c:181)\nHeader acquisition:\n32. `(mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER) == 0 && buffer_size < 8` → `png_push_save_buffer`, return (buffer_size ← 0).\n33. `(mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER) == 0 && buffer_size >= 8` → `png_read_chunk_header()` → sets `push_length`, `chunk_name`; set `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER`.\n34. `(mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER) != 0` → reuse previously read `push_length`/`chunk_name` (re-entry after a save).\n\nIDAT pre-pass (chunk_name == png_IDAT):\n35. `mode & PNG_AFTER_IDAT` → also set `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT`.\n36. `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IHDR) == 0` → `png_error(\"Missing IHDR before IDAT\")`.\n37. `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE && (mode & PNG_HAVE_PLTE) == 0` → `png_error(\"Missing PLTE before IDAT\")`.\n38. Otherwise `process_mode = PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE`.\n39. `(mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) != 0 && (mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT) == 0 && push_length == 0` → **return immediately, leaving `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER` set** (zero-length trailing IDAT; does not set HAVE_IDAT, no benign error).\n40. Else set `PNG_HAVE_IDAT`; if `(mode & PNG_AFTER_IDAT) != 0` → `png_benign_error(\"Too many IDATs found\")`.\n\nNon-IDAT after IDAT:\n41. `chunk_name != png_IDAT && (mode & PNG_HAVE_IDAT) != 0` → set `PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_AFTER_IDAT | PNG_AFTER_IDAT`.\n\nDispatch (ordered; first match wins):\n42. `chunk_name == png_IHDR && push_length != 13` → `png_error(\"Invalid IHDR length\")`.\n43. `chunk_name == png_IHDR && push_length == 13 && push_length+4 > buffer_size` → save buffer, return (retry later).\n44. `chunk_name == png_IHDR && push_length == 13 && push_length+4 <= buffer_size` → `png_handle_chunk`, clear HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER.\n45. `chunk_name == png_IEND && push_length+4 > buffer_size` → save buffer, return.\n46. `chunk_name == png_IEND && push_length+4 <= buffer_size` → `png_handle_chunk`, `process_mode = PNG_READ_DONE_MODE`, `png_push_have_end`, clear HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER.\n47. `png_chunk_unknown_handling(chunk_name) != 0` (i.e. app registered a non-default keep) && `push_length+4 > buffer_size` → save buffer, return.\n48. same, `push_length+4 <= buffer_size` → `png_handle_unknown(..., keep)`; additionally if `chunk_name == png_PLTE` → set `PNG_HAVE_PLTE`; clear HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER.\n49. `chunk_name == png_IDAT` (reached only when keep==0 and not IHDR/IEND) → `idat_size = push_length`; `process_mode = PNG_READ_IDAT_MODE`; `png_push_have_info` (calls `info_fn` if non-NULL); `zstream.avail_out = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, iwidth)+1`; `zstream.next_out = row_buf`; **return without clearing PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER** (so `png_push_read_IDAT` skips the header read).\n50. any other chunk && `push_length+4 > buffer_size` → save buffer, return.\n51. any other chunk && `push_length+4 <= buffer_size` → `png_handle_chunk`, clear HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER.\n52. Zero-length chunk (`push_length == 0`) of a non-IDAT type: guard becomes `4 > buffer_size` — needs only the 4 CRC bytes present.\n53. `push_length` huge (near 2^31): `push_length + 4` can overflow on 32-bit `size_t` → guard may falsely pass. (`push_length` comes from `png_read_chunk_header` which uses `png_get_uint_31`, so ≤ 0x7fffffff.)\n\n## png_push_fill_buffer (pngpread.c:291) — also installed as `read_data_fn`\n54. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n55. `save_buffer_size == 0` → skip first block.\n56. `save_buffer_size != 0 && length < save_buffer_size` → copy `length`; `save_buffer_size` and `buffer_size` decremented; `length` becomes 0.\n57. `save_buffer_size != 0 && length >= save_buffer_size` → copy all of save buffer; `save_buffer_size = 0`.\n58. after block 1, `length == 0` → second block skipped.\n59. `length != 0 && current_buffer_size == 0` → second block skipped (**request under-satisfied silently — no error, caller gets uninitialized tail**).\n60. `length != 0 && current_buffer_size != 0 && length < current_buffer_size` → copy `length`.\n61. `length != 0 && current_buffer_size != 0 && length >= current_buffer_size` → copy `current_buffer_size` (**still possibly short**).\n\n## png_push_save_buffer (pngpread.c:334)\n62. `save_buffer_size != 0 && save_buffer_ptr != save_buffer` → byte-by-byte compaction to front of `save_buffer`.\n63. `save_buffer_size != 0 && save_buffer_ptr == save_buffer` → no compaction.\n64. `save_buffer_size == 0` → no compaction.\n65. `save_buffer_size + current_buffer_size <= save_buffer_max` → no realloc.\n66. Realloc needed && `save_buffer_size > PNG_SIZE_MAX - (current_buffer_size + 256)` → `png_error(\"Potential overflow of save_buffer\")`.\n67. Realloc needed && `png_malloc_warn` returns NULL → `png_free(old_buffer)` + `png_error(\"Insufficient memory for save_buffer\")`.\n68. Realloc needed && success && `old_buffer != NULL` → `memcpy(new, old, save_buffer_size)`, free old, `save_buffer_max = new_max`.\n69. Realloc needed && success && `old_buffer == NULL && save_buffer_size != 0` → `png_error(\"save_buffer error\")` (internal inconsistency).\n70. Realloc needed && success && `old_buffer == NULL && save_buffer_size == 0` → first allocation, ok.\n71. `current_buffer_size != 0` → append current buffer, `save_buffer_size += current_buffer_size`, `current_buffer_size = 0`.\n72. `current_buffer_size == 0` → nothing appended.\n73. Always ends with `save_buffer_ptr = save_buffer; buffer_size = 0`.\n\n## png_push_restore_buffer (pngpread.c:394)\n74. No NULL check on `png_ptr` (caller checks). Unconditional: `current_buffer = buffer; current_buffer_size = buffer_length; buffer_size = buffer_length + save_buffer_size; current_buffer_ptr = current_buffer`.\n75. Distinguishable inputs: `buffer == NULL && buffer_length == 0` (legal drain of saved data); `buffer_length` overflow of `buffer_length + save_buffer_size` (size_t wrap).\n\n## png_push_read_IDAT (pngpread.c:404)\nHeader block, taken only when `(mode & PNG_HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER) == 0`:\n76. `buffer_size < 8` → save buffer, return.\n77. `buffer_size >= 8` → read 4-byte length via `png_push_fill_buffer` + `png_get_uint_31` (errors if bit31 set), `png_reset_crc`, `png_crc_read(tag,4)`, set `chunk_name`, set HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER.\n78. new `chunk_name != png_IDAT && (flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED) == 0` → `process_mode = PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE` then `png_error(\"Not enough compressed data\")`.\n79. new `chunk_name != png_IDAT && PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED set` → `process_mode = PNG_READ_CHUNK_MODE`, return cleanly (**HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER stays set so CHUNK mode reuses the header**).\n80. new `chunk_name == png_IDAT` → `idat_size = push_length` (may be 0).\n\nSave-buffer consumption block:\n81. `idat_size == 0` → skipped.\n82. `save_buffer_size == 0` → skipped.\n83. `idat_size < save_buffer_size` → `save_size = idat_size` (consume only the chunk remainder).\n84. `idat_size >= save_buffer_size` → `save_size = save_buffer_size`, `idat_size(local) = save_size`.\n85. Then `png_calculate_crc` + `png_process_IDAT_data(save_size)`; decrement `idat_size`, `buffer_size`, `save_buffer_size`; advance `save_buffer_ptr`.\n\nCurrent-buffer consumption block: same four configurations (86-89) with `current_buffer_size`/`current_buffer_ptr`.\n\nCRC finish:\n90. `idat_size != 0` after both blocks → return, nothing else (wait for more data).\n91. `idat_size == 0 && buffer_size < 4` → save buffer, return (CRC not yet available).\n92. `idat_size == 0 && buffer_size >= 4` → `png_crc_finish(png_ptr, 0)`, clear HAVE_CHUNK_HEADER, set `PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, `zowner = 0`.\n93. Degenerate: zero-length IDAT (`push_length == 0`) → both consumption blocks skipped, goes straight to the CRC branch in the same call.\n\n## png_process_IDAT_data (pngpread.c:497)\n94. `buffer_length == 0 || buffer == NULL` → `png_error(\"No IDAT data (internal error)\")`.\n95. `buffer_length > UINT_MAX` → truncation on the `(uInt)` cast (flagged TODO in source).\n96. Loop guard `avail_in > 0 && (flags & PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED) == 0`; if `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED` already set on entry → loop skipped → falls to 105.\n97. In-loop, `avail_out == 0` → reset `avail_out = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth,iwidth)+1`, `next_out = row_buf`.\n98. `ret = PNG_INFLATE(Z_SYNC_FLUSH)`; `ret != Z_OK && ret != Z_STREAM_END` → set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`, `zowner = 0`; then:\n - 98a. `row_number >= num_rows || pass > 6` → `png_warning(\"Truncated compressed data in IDAT\")`, return.\n - 98b. else `ret == Z_DATA_ERROR` → `png_benign_error(\"IDAT: ADLER32 checksum mismatch\")`, return.\n - 98c. else → `png_error(\"Decompression error in IDAT\")`.\n99. `ret in {Z_OK, Z_STREAM_END}` and `next_out == row_buf` (no output produced) → skip output handling.\n100. output produced && `row_number >= num_rows || pass > 6` → `png_warning(\"Extra compressed data in IDAT\")`, set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`, `zowner = 0`, return.\n101. output produced && in-range && `avail_out == 0` (complete row) → `png_push_process_row`.\n102. output produced && in-range && `avail_out != 0` (partial row) → nothing yet.\n103. `ret == Z_STREAM_END` → set `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED` (terminates the loop).\n104. Loop exits with `avail_in == 0` → no trailing warning.\n105. Loop exits with `avail_in > 0` (only via `PNG_FLAG_ZSTREAM_ENDED`) → `png_warning(\"Extra compression data in IDAT\")`.\n\n## png_push_process_row (pngpread.c:609)\n106. `row_buf[0] == PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE(0)` → no filter applied.\n107. `0 < row_buf[0] < PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST` → `png_read_filter_row(...)`.\n108. `row_buf[0] >= PNG_FILTER_VALUE_LAST` → `png_error(\"bad adaptive filter value\")`.\n109. `transformations != 0` → `png_do_read_transformations`; `== 0` → skip.\n110. `transformed_pixel_depth == 0 && row_info.pixel_depth <= maximum_pixel_depth` → record depth.\n111. `transformed_pixel_depth == 0 && row_info.pixel_depth > maximum_pixel_depth` → `png_error(\"progressive row overflow\")`.\n112. `transformed_pixel_depth != 0 && != row_info.pixel_depth` → `png_error(\"internal progressive row size calculation error\")`.\n113. `transformed_pixel_depth != 0 && == row_info.pixel_depth` → ok.\n114. `interlaced == 0 || (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) == 0` → single `png_push_have_row(row_buf+1)` + `png_read_push_finish_row`.\n115. `interlaced != 0 && (transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0 && pass < 6` → `png_do_read_interlace` first; `pass == 6` → no expansion.\nPer-pass switch (each row-callback pattern is a distinct configuration):\n116. `pass == 0` → up to 8 real-row callbacks while `pass==0`; then if `pass == 2` up to 4 NULL callbacks; then if `pass == 4 && height <= 4` up to 2 NULL callbacks; then if `pass == 6 && height <= 4` one NULL callback.\n117. `pass == 1` → up to 8 real callbacks; then if `pass == 2` up to 4 NULL callbacks.\n118. `pass == 2` → up to 4 real callbacks; then up to 4 NULL callbacks; then if `pass == 4` up to 2 NULL callbacks.\n119. `pass == 3` → up to 4 real callbacks; then if `pass == 4` up to 2 NULL callbacks.\n120. `pass == 4` → up to 2 real; then up to 2 NULL; then if `pass == 6` one NULL.\n121. `pass == 5` → up to 2 real; then if `pass == 6` one NULL.\n122. `pass == 6` or default (`pass > 6`) → one real callback; if `pass` still 6 → one more NULL callback.\n\n## png_read_push_finish_row (pngpread.c:839)\n123. `++row_number < num_rows` → return.\n124. row_number reached num_rows && `interlaced == 0` → nothing (no pass advance).\n125. `interlaced != 0` → `row_number = 0`, zero `prev_row` (`rowbytes+1`), then the do/while pass advance:\n - 125a. `pass==1 && width < 5` → skip to pass 2; `pass==3 && width < 3` → skip; `pass==5 && width < 2` → skip.\n - 125b. `pass > 7` after increment → `pass--`.\n - 125c. `pass >= 7` → break (done).\n - 125d. recompute `iwidth`; `(transformations & PNG_INTERLACE) != 0` → break here (num_rows left unchanged).\n - 125e. else recompute `num_rows`; loop again while `iwidth == 0 || num_rows == 0`.\n\n## Callback hooks\n126. `png_push_have_info`: `info_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called with `(png_ptr, info_ptr)`.\n127. `png_push_have_end`: `end_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called.\n128. `png_push_have_row`: `row_fn == NULL` → no-op; non-NULL → called with `(row, row_number, pass)`; `row` is either `row_buf+1` or NULL.\n\n## png_progressive_combine_row (pngpread.c:907)\n129. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n130. `new_row == NULL` → return without combining (empty interlace row).\n131. `new_row != NULL` → `png_combine_row(png_ptr, old_row, 1 /*blocky*/)`. NOTE: `new_row` is used purely as a flag; no check that it equals `row_buf+1`; `old_row` is not NULL-checked.\n\n## png_set_progressive_read_fn (pngpread.c:923)\n132. `png_ptr == NULL` → return.\n133. Any combination of `info_fn`/`row_fn`/`end_fn` NULL or non-NULL is accepted verbatim (all-NULL is legal → silent decode).\n134. Always calls `png_set_read_fn(png_ptr, progressive_ptr, png_push_fill_buffer)` → inherits pngrio.c branch: if `write_data_fn != NULL` it is cleared with a warning; `output_flush_fn` set to NULL.\n135. `png_get_progressive_ptr`: `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL; else `io_ptr`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. png.c\n\n## png_set_sig_bytes (png.c:53)\n136. `png_ptr == NULL` → return. 137. `num_bytes < 0` → treated as 0. 138. `nb > 8` (incl. large positive) → `png_error(\"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")`. 139. `0 <= nb <= 8` → stored.\n\n## png_sig_cmp (png.c:80)\n140. `num_to_check > 8` → clamped to 8.\n141. `num_to_check < 1` (0, or negative-cast-to-huge does not hit this) → return **-1** without touching `sig`.\n142. `start > 7` → return -1.\n143. `start + num_to_check > 8` → `num_to_check = 8 - start`.\n144. else → `memcmp(&sig[start], &png_signature[start], num_to_check)`; returns <0/0/>0.\n145. Note: `sig` is never NULL-checked; `start<=7 && num_to_check>=1` always dereferences.\n\n## png_zalloc / png_zfree (png.c:104, 131)\n146. `png_ptr == NULL` → return NULL.\n147. `size != 0 && items >= (~(png_alloc_size_t)0)/size` → `png_warning(\"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\")`, return NULL.\n148. `size == 0` → overflow check skipped; `num_bytes = 0` → `png_malloc_warn(0)`.\n149. else → `png_malloc_warn(size*items)` (may itself return NULL after a warning).\n150. `png_zfree` → `png_free(png_ptr, ptr)`; NULL ptr or NULL png_ptr is a no-op.\n\n## png_reset_crc (png.c:140)\n151. Single configuration: `crc = crc32(0, Z_NULL, 0)`. No NULL check on `png_ptr`.\n\n## png_calculate_crc (png.c:152)\n152. `PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(chunk_name)` && `(flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_ANCILLARY_MASK) == (USE|NOWARN)` → `need_crc = 0`.\n153. ancillary && any other ancillary-flag combination → `need_crc = 1`.\n154. critical && `(flags & PNG_FLAG_CRC_CRITICAL_IGNORE) != 0` → `need_crc = 0`.\n155. critical && flag clear → `need_crc = 1`.\n156. `need_crc == 0` → returns without reading `ptr` (so `ptr==NULL` is safe only here).\n157. `need_crc != 0 && length == 0` → returns without calling crc32.\n158. `need_crc != 0 && length > 0 && length <= UINT_MAX` → single crc32 call.\n159. `need_crc != 0 && length > UINT_MAX` (i.e. `(uInt)length` truncates) → loop; sub-case `(uInt)length == 0` → `safe_length = (uInt)-1` (\"evil, but safe\") unless `__COVERITY__`.\n\n## png_user_version_check (png.c:206)\n160. `user_png_ver == NULL` → set `PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH`.\n161. `user_png_ver != NULL` → char-by-char compare until 2 dots seen or either string ends; mismatch anywhere sets the flag.\n162. flag set → build 128-byte message via `png_safecat`, `png_warning`, return