= 0`.\n343. otherwise `czero = 0`.\n344. per-digit: `cdigits+czero+1 < precision+clead` → `modf` split; else final rounded digit via `floor(fp+.5)`.\n345. rounded digit `d > 9 && czero > 0` → `--czero, d = 1` (and `--clead` if `cdigits==0`).\n346. `d > 9 && czero == 0` → carry-propagation back through emitted digits, with sub-cases `exp_b10 != -1` (increment exponent) and `ch == 46` (step back over the '.' and set `exp_b10 = 1`).\n347. carry reaching the beginning (`cdigits == 0 && d > 9`): `exp_b10 == -1 && ch == 46` → restore DP, `exp_b10 = 1`; `exp_b10 == -1 && ch != 46` → keep `exp_b10 = -1`; else `++exp_b10`; output `'1'`.\n348. `d == 0` → `++czero` (deferred), `++clead` when `cdigits == 0`.\n349. `d != 0` → flush pending zeros, inserting `'.'` when `exp_b10 == 0`, then the digit.\n350. loop ends when `cdigits+czero >= precision+clead` or `fp <= DBL_MIN`.\n351. `-1 <= exp_b10 <= 2` → pad with `'0'`s, NUL-terminate, return (no exponent).\n352. exponent needed, `exp_b10 < 0` → emit `'E'`, `'-'`, magnitude digits.\n353. exponent needed, `exp_b10 >= 0` → emit `'E'` + digits.\n354. after exponent digits generated, `size > cdigits` → write them + NUL, return.\n355. `size <= cdigits` → **falls through** to `png_error(\"ASCII conversion buffer too small\")`.\n\n## png_ascii_from_fixed (png.c:2643)\n356. `size <= 12` → `png_error(\"ASCII conversion buffer too small\")`.\n357. `fp < 0` → emit `'-'`, `num = -fp`.\n358. `num > 0x80000000` (overflow of the negate) → fall through to `png_error`.\n359. `fp == 0` → `ndigits == 0` → emit single `'0'`.\n360. `ndigits > 5` → integer digits emitted first.\n361. `first <= 5` (a non-zero fractional digit exists) → emit `'.'`, leading zeros to pad to 5, then digits down to `first` (trailing zeros suppressed).\n362. `first > 5` (fraction all zeros) → no decimal point emitted.\n\n## png_fixed (png.c:2726) / png_fixed_ITU (png.c:2745)\n363. `png_fixed`: `r = floor(100000*fp+.5)`; `r > 2147483647. || r < -2147483648.` → `png_fixed_error(png_ptr, text)` (a `png_error`); else return `(png_fixed_point)r`.\n364. `png_fixed_ITU`: scale 10000; `r > 2147483647. || r < 0` → `png_fixed_error`; else `(png_uint_32)r` (negatives rejected).\n\n## png_muldiv (png.c:2770)\n365. `divisor == 0` → return 0 (failure).\n366. `a == 0 || times == 0` → `*res = 0`, return 1.\n367. FLOATING_ARITHMETIC build: `-2147483648. <= floor(a*times/divisor+.5) <= 2147483647.` → store, return 1; else return 0.\n368. Fixed build: sign folding over the three negative/positive combinations of `a`, `times`, `divisor`.\n369. Fixed build: `s32 >= D` → overflow → return 0.\n370. Fixed build: `s32 < D` → 31-step shift-subtract division, rounding `if (s00 >= D>>1) ++result`, negation if needed.\n371. Fixed build final sign check: `(negative && result <= 0) || (!negative && result >= 0)` → store, return 1; else (sign flip = overflow) return 0.\n\n## png_reciprocal (png.c:2886)\n372. FP build: `a == 0` → division by zero in `1E10/a` → inf → out of range → return 0. 373. FP build in range → value. 374. Fixed build: `png_muldiv(&res,100000,100000,a) != 0` → res; else 0.\n\n## png_product2 (png.c:2930, fixed builds only)\n375. `png_muldiv(a,b,100000)` succeeds → res; fails → 0.\n\n## png_reciprocal2 (png.c:2952)\n376. FP build: `a == 0 || b == 0` → 0. 377. FP build, `1E15/a/b` in range → value; out of range → 0. 378. Fixed build: `png_product2(a,b) == 0` → 0; else `png_reciprocal(product)`.\n\n## png_gamma_significant (png.c:2909)\n379. `gamma_val < PNG_FP_1 - PNG_GAMMA_THRESHOLD_FIXED` → 1. 380. `gamma_val > PNG_FP_1 + PNG_GAMMA_THRESHOLD_FIXED` → 1. 381. within the threshold band → 0.\n\n## png_log8bit / png_log16bit / png_exp / png_exp8bit / png_exp16bit (fixed-arith builds)\n382. `png_log8bit`: `(x & 0xff) == 0` → return -1; else 3 normalization branches on `0xf0`/`0xc0`/`0x80`.\n383. `png_log16bit`: `(x & 0xffff) == 0` → -1; else 4 normalization branches (`0xff00`,`0xf000`,`0xc000`,`0x8000`); then `x <= 65536U` → add-interpolate branch, `> 65536U` → subtract-interpolate branch.\n384. `png_exp`: `0 < x <= 0xfffff` → 6 individual bit tests (`0x800`,`0x400`,`0x200`,`0x100`,`0x080`,`0x040`) plus the low-6-bit block, then `e >>= x>>16`.\n385. `png_exp`: `x <= 0` → `png_32bit_exp[0]` (max). 386. `x > 0xfffff` → 0 (underflow).\n\n## png_gamma_8bit_correct (png.c:3273)\n387. `value == 0` → return 0 (bypasses computation). 388. `value >= 255` → return `value & 0xff`.\n389. `0 < value < 255`, FP build → `floor(255*pow(value/255., gamma*1e-5)+.5)`.\n390. `0 < value < 255`, fixed build, `png_muldiv` ok → `png_exp8bit(res)`. 391. fixed build, `png_muldiv` overflow → `value = 0` → return 0.\n\n## png_gamma_16bit_correct (png.c:3321)\n392. `value == 0` → 0. 393. `value >= 65535` → `value` unchanged. 394. in-range FP build → pow formula. 395. in-range fixed build ok → `png_exp16bit`. 396. fixed build overflow → 0.\n\n## png_gamma_correct (png.c:3356)\n397. `png_ptr->bit_depth == 8` → `png_gamma_8bit_correct`.\n398. `bit_depth != 8 && PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED` → `png_gamma_16bit_correct`.\n399. `bit_depth != 8 && !PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED` → returns 0 (\"should not reach this\").\n\n## png_build_16bit_table (png.c:3381)\n400. Derived from `shift`: `num = 1<<(8-shift)`, `max = (1<<(16-shift))-1`, `max_by_2 = 1<<(15-shift)`; `shift == 0` → 256 sub-tables; `shift == 8` → 1 sub-table.\n401. `png_gamma_significant(gamma_val) != 0` → per-entry gamma computation (`ig = (j<<(8-shift))+i`); fixed build additionally rescales `ig` only when `shift != 0`.\n402. `png_gamma_significant == 0` → identity/fast fill, again rescaling only when `shift != 0`.\n\n## png_build_16to8_table (png.c:3458)\n403. Fills for `i = 0..254` using `bound = (png_gamma_16bit_correct(i*257+128, gamma)*max + 32768)/65535 + 1`, advancing `last`.\n404. Tail: `last < (num<<8)` → remaining entries set to 65535.\n\n## png_build_8bit_table (png.c:3526)\n405. `png_gamma_significant != 0` → 256 gamma-corrected entries. 406. `== 0` → identity table.\n\n## png_destroy_gamma_table (png.c:3545)\n407. `gamma_table` freed unconditionally (NULL-safe via png_free).\n408. `gamma_16_table != NULL` → free `1 << (8 - gamma_shift)` sub-tables then the array. 409. `== NULL` → skipped.\n410. Same pattern for `gamma_16_from_1` and `gamma_16_to_1` (each guarded by its own non-NULL test), and unconditional frees of `gamma_from_1`/`gamma_to_1`, all under `READ_BACKGROUND || READ_ALPHA_MODE || READ_RGB_TO_GRAY`.\n411. Note `gamma_shift` must still be valid at destroy time or the sub-table loop count is wrong.\n\n## png_build_gamma_table (png.c:3616)\n412. `gamma_table != NULL || gamma_16_table != NULL` → `png_warning(\"gamma table being rebuilt\")` + `png_destroy_gamma_table`.\n413. `screen_gamma > 0` → `linear_to_screen = png_reciprocal(screen_gamma)`, `correction = png_reciprocal2(screen_gamma, file_gamma)`.\n414. `screen_gamma <= 0` (unset) → `linear_to_screen = file_gamma`, `correction = PNG_FP_1` (identity).\n415. `bit_depth <= 8` → `png_build_8bit_table(&gamma_table, correction)`.\n416. `bit_depth <= 8 && (transformations & (PNG_COMPOSE|PNG_RGB_TO_GRAY)) != 0` → also build `gamma_to_1` (from `file_to_linear`) and `gamma_from_1` (from `linear_to_screen`).\n417. `bit_depth <= 8` and neither COMPOSE nor RGB_TO_GRAY → only the one table.\n418. `bit_depth > 8 && (color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0` → `sig_bit = max(sig_bit.red, .green, .blue)`.\n419. `bit_depth > 8 && grayscale` → `sig_bit = sig_bit.gray`.\n420. `0 < sig_bit < 16` → `shift = 16 - sig_bit`. 421. `sig_bit == 0 || sig_bit >= 16` → `shift = 0` (all 16 bits).\n422. `(transformations & (PNG_16_TO_8|PNG_SCALE_16_TO_8)) != 0 && shift < 16-PNG_MAX_GAMMA_8` → `shift = 16-PNG_MAX_GAMMA_8` (default 5).\n423. `shift > 8` → clamped to 8 (guarantees ≥1 sub-table).\n424. `(transformations & (PNG_16_TO_8|PNG_SCALE_16_TO_8)) != 0` → `png_build_16to8_table(shift, png_reciprocal(correction))`.\n425. else → `png_build_16bit_table(shift, correction)`.\n426. `bit_depth > 8 && (transformations & (PNG_COMPOSE|PNG_RGB_TO_GRAY)) != 0` → also `gamma_16_to_1(file_to_linear)` and `gamma_16_from_1(linear_to_screen)`.\n427. `!PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED` → the entire `bit_depth > 8` branch is absent.\n\n## png_set_option (png.c:3769)\n428. `png_ptr == NULL` → `PNG_OPTION_INVALID`.\n429. `option < 0` → `PNG_OPTION_INVALID`.\n430. `option >= PNG_OPTION_NEXT (16)` → `PNG_OPTION_INVALID`.\n431. `(option & 1) != 0` (odd option number) → `PNG_OPTION_INVALID`.\n432. valid even option in `[0,16)` → `options = (options & ~(3<<option)) | ((2 + (onoff!=0)) << option)`; returns the **previous** 2-bit value (`PNG_OPTION_UNSET 0`, `PNG_OPTION_OFF 2`, `PNG_OPTION_ON 3`).\n433. `onoff == 0` → stores 2 (OFF); `onoff != 0` (any non-zero) → stores 3 (ON).\nLegal option numbers: 434. `PNG_ARM_NEON 0` (only when `PNG_ARM_NEON_API_SUPPORTED`). 435. `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW 2`. 436. `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE 4`. 437. `PNG_MIPS_MSA 6`. 438. `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32 8`. 439. `PNG_POWERPC_VSX 10`. 440. `PNG_MIPS_MMI 12`. 441. `PNG_RISCV_RVV 14`. 442. Odd numbers 1,3,…,15 and ≥16 → INVALID. Note: `png_set_option` performs no check that the option is compiled in — setting e.g. 0 on a non-ARM build still succeeds.\n\n## png_get_io_state / png_get_io_chunk_type\n443. Both live in **pngget.c:1344/1350** and **dereference `png_ptr` without a NULL check** (`return png_ptr->io_state;` / `return png_ptr->chunk_name;`). Only compiled with `PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED`.\n\n## png_image_free_function / png_image_free / png_image_error (png.c:3959, 4019, 4034)\n444. `png_image_free_function`: `cp->png_ptr == NULL` → return 0 (failure).\n445. STDIO build && `cp->owned_file != 0 && io_ptr != NULL` → `fclose` + clear `io_ptr`.\n446. `owned_file != 0 && io_ptr == NULL` → just clear the flag.\n447. `owned_file == 0` → no file work.\n448. `c.for_write != 0` → `png_destroy_write_struct` (or `png_error(\"simplified write not supported\")`).\n449. `c.for_write == 0` → `png_destroy_read_struct` (or `png_error(\"simplified read not supported\")`).\n450. `png_image_free`: `image == NULL` → no-op. 451. `image->opaque == NULL` → no-op. 452. `image->opaque->error_buf != NULL` (inside error handling) → no-op (defers to `png_safe_execute`). 453. all clear → free + `opaque = NULL`.\n454. `png_image_error`: unconditionally `png_safecat` message, set `PNG_IMAGE_ERROR`, `png_image_free`, return 0. (`image == NULL` would crash.)\n\n## png_safe_execute (pngerror.c:815)\n455. `setjmp == 0 && function(arg) returns true` → restore `error_buf`, return 1.\n456. `setjmp == 0 && function(arg) returns false` → fall through to the failure tail.\n457. `setjmp != 0` (a `png_error` longjmped in) → failure tail.\n458. failure tail with `saved_error_buf == NULL` (outermost call) → `png_image_free(image)` then return 0.\n459. failure tail with `saved_error_buf != NULL` (nested) → return 0 without freeing.\n\n---\n\n# 3. pngmem.c\n\n460. `png_destroy_png_struct`: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; else copy to a stack dummy, zero the real struct, `png_free(dummy, png_ptr)`, and under SETJMP also `png_free_jmpbuf(&dummy)`.\n461. `png_calloc`: `png_malloc` returns NULL (only possible if `png_ptr == NULL`, since otherwise it errors) → return NULL without memset; non-NULL → `memset(ret,0,size)`.\n462. `png_calloc` with `size == 0` → `malloc(0)` result memset of 0 bytes.\n463. `png_malloc_base`: `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K` build && `size > 65536U` → NULL.\n464. `size > PNG_SIZE_MAX` → NULL.\n465. `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED && png_ptr != NULL && malloc_fn != NULL` → `malloc_fn(png_ptr, size)` (whatever it returns, incl. NULL).\n466. `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED && (png_ptr == NULL || malloc_fn == NULL)` → system `malloc((size_t)size)`.\n467. `!PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED` → always system `malloc`.\n468. `size == 0` → passes all limit checks → implementation-defined `malloc(0)` (may return NULL → caller treats as OOM). **No alignment padding is performed anywhere in this file.**\n469. `png_malloc_array_checked`: `req <= PNG_SIZE_MAX/element_size` → `png_malloc_base(req*element_size)`; else NULL.\n470. `png_malloc_array`: `nelements <= 0` → `png_error(\"internal error: array alloc\")`.\n471. `png_malloc_array`: `element_size == 0` → same `png_error`.\n472. `png_malloc_array` valid → `png_malloc_array_checked` (may return NULL, no error).\n473. `png_realloc_array`: `add_elements <= 0` → `png_error(\"internal error: array realloc\")`.\n474. `element_size == 0` → same error. 475. `old_elements < 0` → same error. 476. `old_array == NULL && old_elements > 0` → same error.\n477. `add_elements > INT_MAX - old_elements` → return NULL (no error).\n478. allocation fails → return NULL.\n479. allocation succeeds && `old_elements > 0` → memcpy old + memset the added tail, return new.\n480. allocation succeeds && `old_elements == 0` → memset the whole new array, return new.\n481. `png_malloc`: `png_ptr == NULL` → return NULL (no error).\n482. `png_malloc`: base returns NULL → `png_error(\"Out of memory\")` (lowercase 'm' identifies this path).\n483. `png_malloc`: success → pointer.\n484. `png_malloc_default` (USER_MEM builds only): `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL; `png_malloc_base(NULL, size)` bypasses the app allocator; NULL → `png_error(\"Out of Memory\")` (capital 'M' identifies this path); else pointer.\n485. `png_malloc_warn`: `png_ptr == NULL` → NULL silently.\n486. `png_malloc_warn`: base non-NULL → pointer. 487. base NULL → `png_warning(\"Out of memory\")` + NULL.\n488. `png_free`: `png_ptr == NULL` → return. 489. `ptr == NULL` → return.\n490. USER_MEM && `free_fn != NULL` → `free_fn(png_ptr, ptr)`.\n491. USER_MEM && `free_fn == NULL` → `png_free_default` → `free(ptr)`.\n492. `!USER_MEM` → `free(ptr)` directly (`png_free_default` does not exist as a separate function; the `#endif` splices the two bodies).\n493. `png_free_default` called directly with `png_ptr == NULL` or `ptr == NULL` → return.\n494. `png_set_mem_fn`: `png_ptr == NULL` → no-op; else stores `mem_ptr`, `malloc_fn`, `free_fn` (any may be NULL, giving the four fn-set/uns