{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_r6y7be5wbpfhcerumsosqxjvg7doxygxzscu6t5j3ciy57c7gawa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/.work/errors_read.md` — 374 table-body rows, 4 columns each, no header/prose/fences. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\n**Coverage (rows per file):** `pngrutil.c` 182, `pngread.c` 113, `pngrtran.c` 45, `pngpread.c` 34.\n\n**What each row is derived from:** every `png_error` / `png_chunk_error` / `png_app_error` / `png_benign_error` / `png_chunk_benign_error` / `png_warning` / `png_chunk_warning` / `png_app_warning` / `png_fixed_error` / `png_image_error` call site (verified by grep against the four files — 222 total call sites, all accounted for), plus every `return NULL` / `return 0` / `return handled_error` / zlib-error-code sentinel, every `png_crc_finish` / `png_crc_finish_critical` check in each chunk handler, every explicit length/range/null check, and every signature / IHDR / chunk-ordering validation.\n\n**Notable findings worth flagging to the caller:**\n\n- **The chunk-position/duplicate/length table is the single densest validation site.** `read_chunks[]` (`pngrutil.c:2986-3083`) plus `png_handle_chunk` (`pngrutil.c:3106-3217`) implements ordering (`pos_before`/`pos_after`), duplicate suppression (`multiple`), and min/max length in six generic branches producing exactly five messages: `\"missing IHDR\"`, `\"out of place\"`, `\"duplicate\"`, `\"too short\"`, `\"too long\"`, `\"length exceeds libpng limit\"`. Each then bifurcates: critical chunk → `png_chunk_error` (longjmp); ancillary → `png_crc_finish` + `png_chunk_benign_error`. A port must reproduce the per-chunk constants from the `CDcHNK` macros, not just the messages.\n- **Message strings are deliberately terse and reused.** `\"invalid\"` alone appears 11 times across IEND/gAMA/sBIT/cHRM/sRGB/tRNS(×3)/bKGD/eXIf/hIST; `\"out of memory\"` 9 times; `\"out of place\"` 5 times. `png_chunk_benign_error` prepends the chunk name, so byte-for-byte fidelity requires the prefixing behaviour too, not just the literal.\n- **Three near-identical \"Too many IDATs found\" strings differ only by leading dots** — `\"Too many IDATs found\"` (`pngread.c:125`, `pngpread.c:229`), `\".Too many IDATs found\"` (`pngread.c:729`), `\"..Too many IDATs found\"` (`pngread.c:747`). These are distinct byte sequences and easy to normalise away by mistake.\n- **`PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX`/`PNG_USER_HEIGHT_MAX` (both 1000000) are *not* checked in these four files.** `png_handle_IHDR` (`pngrutil.c:968`) delegates all IHDR field validation to `png_set_IHDR` → `png_check_IHDR` in `pngset.c`/`png.c`. Recorded as one row noting the delegated messages. `PNG_USER_CHUNK_CACHE_MAX` (1000) and `PNG_USER_CHUNK_MALLOC_MAX` (8000000, via `png_chunk_max`) *are* enforced locally, at 12 and 8 sites respectively.\n- **~25 rows are lexically present but compiled out in this all-defines-ON configuration**, and are marked \"(not compiled in this build)\": the 7 `png_read_row` `PNG_READ_*_SUPPORTED is not defined` warnings, the 13 `png_read_png` `PNG_TRANSFORM_* not supported` app-errors, `pngread.c:648`, `pngrtran.c:1083`, `pngrutil.c:2892`, and the two `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K` \"row greater than 64KB\" errors. I kept them rather than dropping them, since a port targeting other configs will need them, but they should not be treated as reachable test targets here.\n- **Two non-obvious silent-recovery paths** that a port could easily turn into hard errors: `png_handle_PLTE` (`pngrutil.c:1033`) silently *truncates* a palette that is too large for the bit depth (explicitly to preserve 1.6 behaviour), and `png_handle_pCAL` (`pngrutil.c:2207`) emits `\"unrecognized equation type\"` and then **continues processing** with no `return`.\n- **`png_image_read_colormap` contributes 22 rows of internal-consistency `png_error`s** (11 \"too few entries\" variants, 5 `bad_background`