{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_butiuoomprvo3mmkedpak6ukcwcwlty232hkz3bcl63lbwkmdbea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_017HiYu4RWw8bU8EJ79mBRKf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nhdr = \"\"\"# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md`: every VALID input configuration the C reference\nimplementation (libpng 1.6.59, `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h`, essentially every\nfeature ON) treats differently.  Derived mechanically from the axes the C code\nbranches on:\n\n* every runtime option / mode / flag the public API can set (grep of the public\n  setters in `png.h` against the `if` / `switch` branches on\n  `PNG_FLAG_*`, `PNG_TRANSFORM_*`, `PNG_BACKGROUND_*`, `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_*`,\n  `PNG_INTERLACE_*`, `PNG_FILTER_*`, `PNG_COMPRESSION_*`, `PNG_OPTION_*`,\n  `PNG_FORMAT_*`, `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_*`);\n* every distinct input SHAPE the code special-cases (the 15 legal\n  bit-depth/colour-type pairs, interlaced vs not, widths that straddle the\n  sub-byte packing boundaries, heights 0/1/many, palette sizes 1..256, tRNS\n  present or absent, zero-length and multi-chunk IDAT, empty/one/many text\n  chunks, 16-bit byte order);\n* the FULL set of public entry points, including the lowest-level ones\n  (`png_read_row` / `png_write_row` / `png_process_data` / `png_write_chunk_*` /\n  `png_get_uint_32` / `png_muldiv` / `png_gamma_*` / `png_XYZ_from_xy` / ...),\n  not just the one-shot wrappers.  Cross-checked against the 384 symbols the C\n  `.so` exports.\n\n## How the rows are tested\n\nEvery row is covered by a differential test in `tests/` that calls BOTH\nlibraries through their `.so` exports and compares the results byte-for-byte:\n\n| test file | scope |\n|---|---|\n| `t01_low_level.rs` | pure/scalar helpers: byte order, `png_sig_cmp`, `png_muldiv`, reciprocals, gamma helpers, `png_XYZ_from_xy`/`png_xy_from_XYZ`, `png_safecat`, `png_format_number`, `png_check_fp_*`, `png_ascii_from_*`, `png_fixed(_ITU)`, grayscale palette, time conversion |\n| `t02_write.rs` | the whole write pipeline: `png_write_info`/`_row`/`_rows`/`_image`/`_end`/`_flush`, `png_write_png`, every filter subset, every zlib option, every write transform, every ancillary chunk, text chunks, unknown chunks, MNG features, the raw `png_write_chunk*` API |\n| `t03_read.rs` | the whole read pipeline: `png_read_info`/`_update_info`/`_row`/`_rows`/`_image`/`_end`, `png_read_png`, the progressive reader at every feed size, every read transform alone and in combination, gamma/background/alpha-mode/rgb-to-gray/quantize, every ancillary chunk, all options and limits |\n| `t04_simplified.rs` | the simplified API: `png_image_begin_read_from_memory`/`_from_file`/`_from_stdio`, `png_image_finish_read` for every `PNG_FORMAT_*` and `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_*`, `png_image_write_to_memory`/`_to_file`/`_to_stdio`, colormapped and not, both row-stride signs |\n| `t05_info.rs` | every `png_set_*` / `png_get_*` pair round-tripped, `png_get_valid`/`png_set_invalid`, `png_free_data`/`png_data_freer`, the EASY_ACCESS getters, `png_info_init_3`, memory callbacks |\n| `t20_err_*.rs` | the `ERRORS.md` rows (Phase C) |\n\nThe `[ ]` column is ticked when the row's differential test passes across the\nrandomised inputs of its test.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n\"\"\"\nn=0\nout=[hdr]\nfor line in open('.work/configs_body.md'):\n    line=line.rstrip('\\n')\n    if not line.strip().startswith('|'): continue\n    n+=1\n    out.append(line.replace('| NNN |','| %d |'%n,1))\nopen('translation/CONFIGS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(out)+'\\n')\nprint(\"rows:\",n)\nPY\ngrep -c '^| [0-9]' translation/CONFIGS.md","description":"Assemble CONFIGS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":269683,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1118,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"81ac2df6-65af-4aeb-a9db-36711889f559","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:51:49.600Z"}
