{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_tcqwjyho752jlif73hj4w66znf6rupzpsgctuwuuw5huowqbznnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01ULCxkZD4zFb42w4dLYkpGA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write info set/get roundtrip tests","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF\nCrate dir:   /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/translation\nNEVER modify anything under c_src/. NEVER modify tests/common/*, tests/t01_*, t02_*, t03_*, t04_*, gen_api.py, src/**, or Cargo.toml.\nYour ONLY output file: translation/tests/t05_info.rs\n\nGOAL: A differential test file that round-trips EVERY `png_set_*` / `png_get_*`\npair in libpng through BOTH shared libraries (loaded via libloading) and asserts\nthey behave identically. The C reference is ALWAYS correct; report divergences,\nnever \"fix\" the C and never edit translation/src/.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read these first)\n- translation/tests/common/mod.rs      -- types (png_color, png_color_8,\n  png_color_16, png_text, png_time, png_sPLT_t, png_sPLT_entry,\n  png_unknown_chunk, png_image), all PNG_* constants, `Rng` (seeded PRNG),\n  `eq_dbg`, `eq_bytes`, `cstr_to_string`\n- translation/tests/common/api.rs      -- `apis()` -> `&'static Both` with `.c`\n  and `.rs`, each an `Api` struct of resolved `extern \"C\"` fn pointers named\n  exactly like the C symbols, e.g. `(a.png_set_gAMA_fixed)(p, info, 45455)`\n- translation/tests/common/harness.rs  -- `reset_all()`, `set_cur_is_c(bool)`,\n  `warn_cb`, `error_cb`, `write_cb`, `flush_cb`, `log_take()`, `out_take()`\n- translation/tests/t02_write.rs, t03_read.rs -- worked examples of the pattern\n\nStart with `mod common;` then `use common::api::{apis, Api}; use common::harness::*; use common::*;`\n\n## Pattern\nFor each case, run the SAME sequence against `apis().c` (with\n`set_cur_is_c(true)`) and `apis().rs` (`set_cur_is_c(false)`), collecting a\n`Vec<String>` describing every getter result, then `eq_dbg` the two vectors.\nCreate the struct with `png_create_write_struct` (or `_read_struct`) passing\n`PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING.as_ptr() as *const c_char`, `Some(error_cb)`,\n`Some(warn_cb)`; always `reset_all()` first and destroy the struct at the end.\nAlso append `log_take()` (the warning transcript) to the compared vector.\n\n## What to cover — use MANY randomised values per setter (fixed seed)\n1. Round-trip every info setter/getter pair, on BOTH a read struct and a write\n   struct: png_set_IHDR/png_get_IHDR, PLTE, tRNS (palette form AND colour-key\n   form), bKGD, sBIT, hIST, gAMA and gAMA_fixed, cHRM / cHRM_fixed /\n   cHRM_XYZ / cHRM_XYZ_fixed, sRGB, sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM, iCCP, sPLT (8-bit and\n   16-bit depth, 1/2/many entries), pHYs, oFFs, pCAL (all 4 equation types,\n   0/1/many params), sCAL / sCAL_fixed / sCAL_s, tIME, text / text_2 (tEXt,\n   zTXt, iTXt, compressed and not, empty and long), eXIf / eXIf_1,\n   cICP, cLLI / cLLI_fixed, mDCV / mDCV_fixed, unknown_chunks +\n   unknown_chunk_location, rows (png_set_rows/png_get_rows).\n   For each: verify the getter returns the same flag AND the same values in both\n   libraries. Use the FIXED-point setter with the FIXED-point getter and the\n   floating-point setter with the floating-point getter, and also cross them\n   (set fixed, get float and vice versa) — the C converts between them.\n2. `png_get_valid` for every PNG_INFO_* flag before and after each setter, and\n   `png_set_invalid` with single flags, 0, and all-ones.\n3. The EASY_ACCESS getters, both with the underlying chunk present and absent:\n   png_get_pixels_per_meter, png_get_x/y_pixels_per_meter,\n   png_get_pixels_per_inch, png_get_x/y_pixels_per_inch,\n   png_get_pixel_aspect_ratio(_fixed), png_get_x/y_offset_pixels,\n   png_get_x/y_offset_microns, png_get_x/y_offset_inches(_fixed),\n   png_get_pHYs_dpi, png_get_image_width/height, png_get_bit_depth,\n   png_get_color_type, png_get_channels, png_get_rowbytes,\n   png_get_interlace_type, png_get_compression_type, png_get_filter_type,\n   png_get_signature, png_get_palette_max.\n   IMPORTANT: `png_get_IHDR` runs png_check_IHDR and raises png_error\n   \"Invalid IHDR data\" on an EMPTY info struct — only call it after a valid\n   png_set_IHDR (see the guard in t03_read.rs `dump_info`).\n   Likewise `png_get_sCAL_fixed` can png_error on overflow — only call it with\n   in-range values.\n4. State/pointer getters on both struct kinds: png_get_io_ptr, png_get_error_ptr,\n   png_get_mem_ptr, png_get_progressive_ptr, png_get_user_chunk_ptr,\n   png_get_user_transform_ptr, png_get_io_state, png_get_io_chunk_type,\n   png_get_user_width_max, png_get_user_height_max, png_get_chunk_cache_max,\n   png_get_chunk_malloc_max, png_get_compression_buffer_size,\n   png_get_current_pass_number, png_get_current_row_number,\n   png_get_rgb_to_gray_status. Compare after the corresponding setters\n   (png_set_error_fn, png_set_mem_fn, png_set_read_fn/png_set_write_fn,\n   png_set_progressive_read_fn, png_set_read_user_chunk_fn,\n   png_set_user_transform_info, png_set_user_limits, png_set_chunk_cache_max,\n   png_set_chunk_malloc_max, png_set_compression_buffer_size).\n   For POINTER-valued getters compare only whether the pointer is NULL or equals\n   the value you passed in (raw addresses legitimately differ between libraries).\n5. `png_free_data` and `png_data_freer` with every PNG_FREE_* mask and\n   `num` = -1 and specific indices; then re-query the getters and compare.\n6. `png_info_init_3`, `png_create_info_struct`, `png_destroy_info_struct`,\n   `png_create_read_struct_2` / `png_create_write_struct_2` with custom\n   `png_malloc_ptr`/`png_free_ptr` callbacks (write a pair of `extern \"C\"`\n   allocator callbacks in your file that forward to a simple bump/Vec allocator\n   or to `std::alloc`), and `png_malloc`/`png_calloc`/`png_malloc_warn`/\n   `png_malloc_default`/`png_free`/`png_free_default`/`png_malloc_array`?\n   (only use the symbols that exist in tests/common/api.rs).\n7. `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_set_option` (every option x every on/off),\n   `png_set_benign_errors`, `png_set_check_for_invalid_index`,\n   `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` (all four keep values, with and without a\n   chunk list), `png_handle_as_unknown` for many chunk names,\n   `png_set_sig_bytes` + `png_get_signature`, `png_set_compression_*` and\n   `png_set_text_compression_*` (compare via the produced output in a full\n   write, or at least assert no divergence in the warning transcript),\n   `png_set_filter`, `png_set_filter_heuristics(_fixed)`,\n   `png_set_flush`, `png_set_read_status_fn`, `png_set_write_status_fn`,\n   `png_set_interlace_handling` (compare the returned pass count).\n\n## Rules\n- Only VALID inputs here (a separate Phase C file covers rejections), EXCEPT\n  where the C merely warns and continues — those are valuable, keep them and\n  compare the warning text exactly via `log_take()`.\n- Fixed seeds; reproducible.\n- Keep total runtime under ~120 seconds.\n- Build/iterate:\n    cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/translation && \\\n      timeout 600 cargo build --release --test t05_info 2>&1 | tail -40\n    timeout 600 cargo test --release --test t05_info -- --test-threads=1 2>&1 | tail -40\n- A `png_error` on a valid path aborts the process (that is by design of the\n  harness). If that happens, your input was not actually valid — narrow it down\n  (the `error_cb` prints the message to stderr) and restrict the case, adding a\n  comment citing the C file:line that rejects it.\n- Iterate until ALL tests in your file PASS.\n\nReport: number of #[test] functions, coverage summary, the final `test result:`\nline verbatim, and any genuine C-vs-Rust divergence with the exact case.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1803,"cache_read_input_tokens":270801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1803,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"0ced37bd-33b3-42fa-a4f6-ed222b2c5f5a","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:53:09.648Z"}
