{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_d7igrfg7q4mitnv33vmnw27mq352jauxiencr4iq4jnsor4x6e5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote the configuration-surface table to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/.work/configs_body.md`.\n\n## Result\n\n**250 rows**, table body only — no header, title, prose, or code fences. Every row is exactly `| NNN | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |`; verified programmatically that all 250 lines contain exactly 5 pipes and match the strict 3-column shape (an earlier draft had 11 rows with literal `|` inside constant expressions like `PNG_EXPAND|PNG_EXPAND_tRNS`, which would have silently broken the column count — those are now written as prose).\n\n**Coverage:** cross-checked against every `PNG_EXPORT`/`PNG_FP_EXPORT`/`PNG_FIXED_EXPORT` declaration in `png.h` (258 declarations) — zero public entry points left unnamed. Symbol names are spelled out in full rather than abbreviated with suffixes, so each is greppable.\n\n**Grouping** follows the requested order: low-level scalar helpers → memory/error/IO → IHDR and limits → read chunk handlers → read row pipeline → read transforms → write pipeline → write transforms → progressive reader → simplified API → getters.\n\n## Notable findings from deriving this mechanically\n\n- **The legal IHDR matrix is 15 combinations**, not the naive 25: GRAY takes all five depths, PALETTE takes 1/2/4/8 (16 rejected), and RGB/GRAY_ALPHA/RGB_ALPHA take only 8/16. `png_check_IHDR` accumulates a warning per violated guard and errors once at the end.\n- **`png_read_filter_row` branches on `bpp`, not bit depth** — PAETH selects a 1-byte-pixel implementation when `(pixel_depth+7)>>3 == 1`, covering depths 1/2/4/8 identically, and a multibyte one for bpp 2/3/4/6/8.\n- **`png_combine_row` is the widest single dispatch**: sub-8-bit mask loops × pass × sparkle/block × PACKSWAP, then `bytes_to_copy` special cases 1/2/3 plus aligned/unaligned default paths — and it hard-errors on `pixel_depth & 7`, so a user transform producing a non-byte-multiple depth is rejected there rather than at set time.\n- **Read-transform order is fixed at 23 steps** and `PNG_GRAY_TO_RGB` appears twice in it, gated on `PNG_BACKGROUND_IS_GRAY` — so the same flag combination runs at two different points depending on background colour.\n- **Several setters mutate state before validating.** `png_set_IHDR` stores all fields before `png_check_IHDR` can error; `png_set_cICP` stores its fields then declines to set the valid bit; `png_set_pCAL` and `png_set_sCAL_s` can leave partially-populated info on an allocation failure.\n- **`png_set_benign_errors` is the only public path to three flags at once** (`BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN`, `APP_WARNINGS_WARN`, `APP_ERRORS_WARN`) — they cannot be set independently, which collapses what would otherwise be 8 error-policy configurations to 2.\n- **`PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` (option 4) is settable but never read** anywhere in this tree, and `png_set_filter_heuristics(_fixed)` are empty deprecated stubs — both are configuration surface with no behavioural branch, worth knowing before writing tests that expect an effect.\n- This version has **no `png_check_chunk_length`**; chunk length/position/duplicate gating is table-driven through `png_handle_chunk` against a `read_chunks[]` descriptor with `NoCheck` and `Limit` sentinels, and the limit itself is the `png_chunk_max()` macro."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633,"cache_read_input_tokens":375142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":633,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ENcKrdvkSWX3EWDu34L7aM","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"8fee73aa-c117-4e1f-8387-3bf0a2f9a3fb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:02:53.306Z","subagent_type