{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zvqw65me5ymjsu6zmkspyh33ee36m2wtmyra6gyxhmmui2x7btka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HToFN23FCmJT1ACgxSmMPa","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write getter error-path tests","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF\nCrate dir:   /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/translation\nNEVER modify anything under c_src/. NEVER modify tests/common/*, tests/gen_api.py, any other tests/t*.rs, src/**, or Cargo.toml.\nYour ONLY output file: translation/tests/t21_err_getters.rs\n\nCONTEXT: This is a differential C-vs-Rust verification of libpng 1.6.59.\n`translation/ERRORS.md` is the error-surface table (1183 rows). Your file covers\nthe rows that come from `c_src/src/pngget.c` (91 rows) plus the NULL-pointer\nguards of the `png_set_*` functions in `c_src/src/pngset.c` that merely `return`\nsilently. All of these are NON-FATAL: they return a sentinel (0, -1, NULL,\nPNG_UINT_32_MAX, 8, ...) or do nothing, so they can be tested IN-PROCESS.\n\n## Harness (read these first)\n- translation/tests/common/mod.rs      -- types, all PNG_* constants, `Rng`,\n  `eq_dbg`, `eq_bytes`, `cstr_to_string`\n- translation/tests/common/api.rs      -- `apis()` -> `&'static Both` with `.c`\n  and `.rs`, each an `Api` struct of resolved `extern \"C\"` fn pointers named\n  exactly like the C symbols\n- translation/tests/common/harness.rs  -- `reset_all()`, `set_cur_is_c(bool)`,\n  `warn_cb`, `error_cb`, `log_take()`\n- translation/tests/t03_read.rs        -- see `dump_info` for the comparison idiom\n- translation/tests/t23_err_write.rs   -- see how fatal cases are handled\n\nStart with `mod common;` then\n`use common::api::{apis, Api}; use common::harness::*; use common::*;`\n\n## Method\nFor each case build the SAME sequence against `apis().c` and `apis().rs`,\ncollect every result into a `Vec<String>`, append `log_take()`, and `eq_dbg`\nthe two vectors. Always `reset_all()` and `set_cur_is_c(..)` first.\nCreate structs with `png_create_read_struct` / `png_create_write_struct`\npassing `PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING.as_ptr() as *const c_char`, `Some(error_cb)`,\n`Some(warn_cb)`.\n\n## What to cover — read ERRORS.md rows whose `function` column starts with\n## `png_get_` or is a `png_set_*` NULL guard, and cover EVERY one:\n1. EVERY `png_get_*` function in tests/common/api.rs called with:\n   - `png_ptr == NULL, info_ptr == NULL`\n   - `png_ptr == NULL, info_ptr` valid\n   - `png_ptr` valid, `info_ptr == NULL`\n   - both valid but the relevant `PNG_INFO_*` valid bit CLEAR (fresh info struct)\n   - both valid and the bit SET (via the matching `png_set_*`)\n   Compare the return value AND every out-parameter (initialise out-params to a\n   recognisable sentinel like 0xDEADBEEF first so you can see whether the C\n   wrote to them). Also pass NULL for each individual out-parameter pointer\n   where the C tolerates it.\n   IMPORTANT EXCEPTIONS (they are FATAL and must NOT be called on an empty info):\n   - `png_get_IHDR` raises png_error \"Invalid IHDR data\" (pngget.c:974)\n   - `png_get_sCAL_fixed` raises png_error \"fixed point overflow in sCAL width\"\n     (pngget.c:1047)\n   For those two, cover the NULL-argument sentinels only, and put the fatal\n   cases in a sub-process the way `tests/t23_err_write.rs` does (copy its\n   `harness_child` pattern: a `#[test] fn harness_child()` that checks\n   `child_case()`, plus `diff_case(\"...\")` in the parent).\n2. `png_get_palette_max` -- the only `-1` sentinel; also with a palette set.\n3. `png_get_rowbytes` / `png_get_channels` / `png_get_bit_depth` /\n   `png_get_color_type` / `png_get_interlace_type` / `png_get_compression_type`\n   / `png_get_filter_type` on an empty info (0 sentinels).\n4. `png_get_current_row_number` (PNG_UINT_32_MAX sentinel) and\n   `png_get_current_pass_number` (8 sentinel) with `png_ptr == NULL` and on a\n   struct where reading has not started.\n5. `png_get_io_state` / `png_get_io_chunk_type` with `png_ptr == NULL`\n   (pngget.c:1346/1352 have NO NULL guard -- check the C first; if it really\n   dereferences, do NOT test NULL there, and add a comment saying so).\n6. The EASY_ACCESS getters with the chunk absent AND with out-of-range stored\n   values: png_get_pixels_per_meter, png_get_x/y_pixels_per_meter,\n   png_get_pixels_per_inch, png_get_x/y_pixels_per_inch,\n   png_get_pixel_aspect_ratio(_fixed), png_get_x/y_offset_pixels /_microns\n   /_inches(_fixed), png_get_pHYs_dpi. Drive the out-of-range cases by calling\n   png_set_pHYs / png_set_oFFs with extreme values (0, 1, u32::MAX,\n   i32::MIN, i32::MAX) and every unit_type including out-of-range ones.\n7. `png_get_valid` with flag = 0, every single PNG_INFO_* bit, an undefined bit\n   (e.g. 0x8000_0000) and `!0`.\n8. `png_get_error_ptr` / `png_get_io_ptr` / `png_get_mem_ptr` /\n   `png_get_progressive_ptr` / `png_get_user_chunk_ptr` /\n   `png_get_user_transform_ptr` with `png_ptr == NULL` (compare NULL-ness only).\n9. `png_get_text` / `png_get_unknown_chunks` / `png_get_sPLT` / `png_get_hIST` /\n   `png_get_PLTE` / `png_get_tRNS` / `png_get_eXIf(_1)` / `png_get_iCCP` /\n   `png_get_pCAL` / `png_get_sCAL_s` with a NULL out-parameter and with the\n   chunk absent.\n10. Every `png_set_*` NULL guard: call each `png_set_*` in api.rs with\n    `png_ptr == NULL` and/or `info_ptr == NULL` and assert nothing happens and\n    nothing is returned differently. Then re-query the matching getter.\n11. `png_get_chunk_cache_max` / `png_get_chunk_malloc_max` /\n    `png_get_user_width_max` / `png_get_user_height_max` /\n    `png_get_compression_buffer_size` with `png_ptr == NULL`.\n12. `png_get_signature` with `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` NULL and before any read.\n\n## Rules\n- Before testing a NULL argument, CHECK THE C SOURCE that it actually has a\n  guard. If the C dereferences the pointer with no check, that input is\n  UNDEFINED BEHAVIOUR and must NOT be tested -- instead add a comment naming\n  the C file:line and saying no check exists. Getting this wrong shows up as a\n  SIGSEGV in both libraries.\n- Fixed seeds; reproducible; runtime under ~60 seconds.\n- Build/iterate:\n    cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/translation && \\\n      timeout 600 cargo build --release --test t21_err_getters 2>&1 | tail -40\n    timeout 600 cargo test --release --test t21_err_getters -- --test-threads=1 2>&1 | \\\n      grep -vE 'Box<dyn Any>|panicked at src/pngerror' | tail -40\n  (The `Box<dyn Any>` lines on stderr are the Rust build's panic-as-longjmp\n  mechanism and are expected noise; filter them out.)\n- Iterate until ALL tests in your file PASS.\n- Add a `#[test] fn self_check()` that PROVES the comparison is not vacuous:\n  assert that at least a dozen DISTINCT sentinel values / messages are actually\n  observed from the C library across your cases.\n\nReport: number of #[test] functions, roughly how many individual cases, the\nfinal `test result:` line verbatim, any C source location where you found no\nNULL guard, and any genuine C-vs-Rust divergence.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":295,"cache_read_input_tokens":391122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":295,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"766f7241-b6ca-486c-a1da-ea50e62361c5","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:07:35.964Z"}
