 Cover every colour type x bit depth x shift value\n   0..=17 and 255.\n2. `png_set_filler` / `png_set_add_alpha`: the low-bit-depth-grey rejection\n   (\"png_set_filler is invalid for low bit depth gray output\"), the palette\n   case, the already-has-alpha case, flags out of range (-1, 2, 255), and the\n   write-side rejections.\n3. Every read transform called AFTER `png_read_update_info` or after\n   `png_start_read_image` -> `\"info change after png_start_read_image or\n   png_read_update_info\"` (the `png_rtran_ok` guard in pngrtran.c). Do this for\n   EVERY `png_set_*` read transform: palette_to_rgb, expand, expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8,\n   tRNS_to_alpha, expand_16, gray_to_rgb, rgb_to_gray_fixed, strip_16, scale_16,\n   strip_alpha, swap, packing, packswap, shift, invert_mono, invert_alpha,\n   swap_alpha, bgr, filler, add_alpha, gamma_fixed, alpha_mode_fixed,\n   background_fixed, quantize, interlace_handling, read_user_transform_fn,\n   user_transform_info.\n4. `png_set_gamma_fixed` / `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed`: gamma outside\n   [PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MIN=1000, PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MAX=10000000] ->\n   `\"gamma out of supported range\"` (pngrtran.c:344). Cover 0, 1, 999, 1000,\n   10000000, 10000001, i32::MIN, i32::MAX, and the special flag values\n   PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB (-1) and PNG_GAMMA_MAC_18 (-2). Note the C only WARNS for\n   png_set_gamma but ERRORS for png_set_alpha_mode — verify which from the\n   source and cover both.\n5. `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed` with `mode` out of range (-1, 4, 255) ->\n   `\"invalid alpha mode\"`.\n6. `png_set_background_fixed`: `background_gamma_code` out of range\n   (PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_UNKNOWN=0 and >3), `need_expand` for a palette image\n   without expansion, and the interaction with png_set_alpha_mode.\n7. `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed`: `error_action` out of range (0, 4, 255),\n   red/green coefficients whose sum exceeds 100000, negative coefficients,\n   and PNG_RGB_TO_GRAY_ERR (3) on a genuinely coloured image ->\n   `\"png_do_rgb_to_gray found nongray pixel\"`.\n8. `png_set_quantize`: `num_palette` <= 0 and > 256, `maximum_colors` <= 0 and\n   > num_palette, a NULL palette, a NULL histogram with full_quantize.\n9. `png_set_crc_action` with each of `crit_action` / `ancil_action` out of range\n   (0, 6, 255) and the documented warnings.\n10. `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`: `keep` out of range (-1, 4, 255) ->\n    `\"png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: invalid keep\"`, a NULL chunk list with\n    num_chunks != 0, num_chunks < 0, a chunk name that is not 4 bytes, and the\n    \"invalid chunk list\" cases.\n11. `png_set_user_limits` / `png_set_chunk_cache_max` / `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`\n    set SMALLER than the image being read, so that the read then fails with\n    `\"Image width exceeds user limit in IHDR\"` /\n    `\"Image height exceeds user limit in IHDR\"` /\n    the chunk-cache and chunk-malloc limit messages. Cover 0, 1, exactly the\n    image size, one less than it, and u32::MAX.\n12. `png_permit_mng_features` on a read struct and the\n    `\"MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream\"` path (an IHDR with\n    filter_method = PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING = 64).\n13. `png_set_sig_bytes` with 0, 1, 8, 9, -1, 100.\n14. `png_set_read_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info` with\n    transform depth/channels that make libpng's internal row-size check fail\n    (`\"internal row size calculation error\"` in png_combine_row).\n15. Every `png_set_*` info setter called on a READ struct with an invalid\n    argument that reaches `png_app_error` (mirror the write-side list in t23 but\n    on a read struct, where the outcome differs).\n16. For a representative subset of the above, ALSO run the case with\n    `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)` applied first, to cover the\n    warn-instead-of-error branch. Use a separate case-name suffix, e.g.\n    \"...:benign\".\n\n## Rules\n- Before adding a NULL-pointer case, CHECK THE C actually guards it. If it\n  dereferences with no check, that is UB — do not test it; add a comment citing\n  the C file:line instead. `diff_case` will fail loudly with\n  \"died from signal ... in BOTH libraries without emitting anything\" if you get\n  this wrong; when that happens, remove the case and document why.\n- Build/iterate:\n    cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GjGJaF/translation && \\\n      timeout 600 cargo build --release --test t22_err_setters 2>&1 | tail -40\n    timeout 600 cargo test --release --test t22_err_setters -- --test-threads=4 2>&1 | \\\n      grep -E 'test result|MISMATCH|ERROR-PATH|died from|FAILED' -A12 | head -40\n- Keep total runtime under ~200 seconds (each case is a sub-process; aim for\n  <2000 cases).\n- Iterate until ALL tests in your file PASS.\n- Include a `#[test] fn self_check()` proving the comparison is not vacuous:\n  assert that several specific expected messages (e.g.\n  \"png_set_shift: invalid shift values\", \"gamma out of supported range\",\n  \"info change after png_start_read_image or png_read_update_info\") are actually\n  observed verbatim in the C transcripts.\n\nReport: number of #[test] functions, number of case strings, the final\n`test result:` line verbatim, every C location where you found no NULL guard,\nand any genuine C-vs-Rust divergence (exact case + both transcripts).","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-XkCeuj/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-GjGJaF/d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7/tasks/a90161cb2d5e7cc4e.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
