{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01117DfgthQ2xvenWPM5hTLS","type":"tool_result","content":"CONFIGS.md\nCargo.lock\nCargo.toml\nERRORS.md\nSYMBOLS.md\nTRANSLATION_GUIDE.md\nbuild.rs\ncheck_syms.sh\nsrc\ntarget\ntests\n# ERRORS.md — the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE\n\nEvery distinct way the C reference implementation (libpng 1.6.59, built with\n`c_src/include/pnglibconf.h`) rejects or errors on input.  Derived mechanically\nfrom the C sources: one row per `png_error` / `png_chunk_error` /\n`png_app_error` / `png_benign_error` / `png_chunk_benign_error` / `png_warning`\n/ `png_chunk_warning` / `png_app_warning` / `png_chunk_report` /\n`png_fixed_error` call site, per `return NULL` / `return 0` / `return -1` /\n`return handled_error` failure sentinel, per explicit range / null / limit\ncheck, and per min/max constant.\n\n## Build-configuration facts that determine the observable result\n\n* `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is **OFF** (`pnglibconf.h:24`);\n  `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` are ON.\n* `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BETA` (2) `<`\n  `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC` (3), so `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0`.  Therefore\n  `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` / `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` are never set by\n  default and **`png_app_error` and `png_app_warning` are both fatal\n  `png_error`s** unless `png_set_benign_errors(png_ptr, 1)` was called.\n* `png_benign_error` → warning on a *read* struct, fatal on a *write* struct.\n* `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_WRITE_ERROR)` → non-fatal on read, fatal on\n  write (`pngerror.c:486-512`).\n* `PNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED` is OFF, so `png_fixed` / `png_fixed_ITU`\n  are real functions that can raise `\"fixed point overflow in <text>\"`.\n* Limits in force: `PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX` = `PNG_USER_HEIGHT_MAX` = 1000000,\n  `PNG_USER_CHUNK_MALLOC_MAX` = 8000000, `PNG_USER_CHUNK_CACHE_MAX` = 1000,\n  `PNG_MAX_GAMMA_8` = 11, `PNG_GAMMA_THRESHOLD_FIXED` = 5000,\n  `PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT` = 8, `PNG_MAX_ERROR_TEXT` = 196.\n\n## How the rows are tested\n\nRows are covered by the differential error-path tests in `tests/`\n(`t20_err_*.rs`, `t21_err_*.rs`, ...).  Because `png_error` must not return,\nthe low-level rows are exercised in a **sub-process**: the test binary\nre-executes itself once per library with an error handler that prints the\nmessage and exits, and the parent asserts the two transcripts (warnings, in\norder, then the error message, then the exit code) are byte-identical.  Rows\nreachable through the simplified API are additionally checked in-process by\ncomparing `png_image.warning_or_error` and `png_image.message`.\n\nRows flagged **not compiled in this build** are `#ifdef`-excluded here and are\ntherefore not reachable; they are retained for completeness of the surface.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n\n| 1 | `png_error` (`pngerror.c:39`) | called with any `error_message`; `png_ptr != NULL && png_ptr->error_fn != NULL` | calls `(*error_fn)(png_ptr, error_message)`; if it returns, falls through to `png_default_error` -> `png_longjmp(png_ptr, 1)` -> non-zero `setjmp`; declared `PNG_NORETURN` |\n| 2 | `png_error` (`pngerror.c:42`) | `png_ptr == NULL` or `png_ptr->error_fn == NULL` | skips custom handler, calls `png_default_error(png_ptr, error_message)` -> `png_longjmp(png_ptr,1)`; never returns |\n| 3 | `png_safecat` (`pngerror.c:76`) | `buffer == NULL` | returns `pos` unchanged, copies nothing (silent no-op) |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01H4bkgNE6Ud9yVg834dhBsz","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"c9dafcdd-db9f-4132-ba95-c7e681cada2f","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:08:16.336Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write setter/transform error tests"}
