en the return says success). Define the\n   `png_xy` / `png_XYZ` repr(C) structs yourself (see tests/t01_low_level.rs).\n   Drive with a large randomised sweep (fixed seed) plus targeted values around\n   110000, 0, 5 and i32 extremes.\n5. **png_zstream_error**: all TEN distinct message strings. Call it with every\n   zlib return code (Z_OK=0, Z_STREAM_END=1, Z_NEED_DICT=2, Z_ERRNO=-1,\n   Z_STREAM_ERROR=-2, Z_DATA_ERROR=-3, Z_MEM_ERROR=-4, Z_BUF_ERROR=-5,\n   Z_VERSION_ERROR=-6) and also out-of-range codes (-7, -100, 2, 100, i32::MIN,\n   i32::MAX), then read back `png_ptr->zstream.msg`. You cannot see the struct\n   field directly, so instead trigger the message through a path that reports\n   it, OR compare it indirectly: after `png_zstream_error`, provoke a\n   diagnostic that includes the message. If neither is feasible, drive the codes\n   through `png_reset_zstream` / a corrupt-zlib read instead and compare the\n   resulting error text; explain your approach in a file comment.\n6. **png_icc_check_header / _length / _tag_table**: EVERY rejection reason\n   (there are ~22 in png.c, distinguishing the four that only WARN and return 1\n   from the ones that return 0). Build ICC profiles byte-by-byte in the test:\n   vary the length field, the signature at offset 36 (`acsp`), the device class\n   at 12, the colour space at 16, the PCS at 20, the version at 8, the rendering\n   intent at 64, the PCS illuminant at 68..80 (D50 = 0x0000f6d6, 0x00010000,\n   0x0000d32d), the tag count at 128, and the tag table entries. Drive them both\n   directly (in-process, comparing the int return AND the warning transcript)\n   AND through a crafted `iCCP` chunk read with the simplified API (see\n   tests/t20_err_read.rs `simple_read` for that idiom — reimplement it locally,\n   do not modify t20).\n7. **png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer**: all NINE `return 0` field checks\n   (year > 9999, month == 0, month > 12, day == 0, day > 31, hour > 23,\n   minute > 59, second > 60, out == NUL