ve of each |\n| `simplified_read_from_file_and_stdio` | item 6 — 30 temp files under `std::env::temp_dir()`, driven through `_from_file` and `_from_stdio` (FILE\\* from `fopen` resolved via `dlopen(NULL, RTLD_NOW\\|RTLD_GLOBAL)`), native + 3 formats × 3 strides; plus the non-existent-file `strerror` path |\n| `simplified_write_to_memory` | item 7a — all 20 formats × 7 shapes × `convert_to_8_bit` {0,1} × 5 strides, each with `memory==NULL` (query), exact, generous (+64) and one-byte-short buffers; also asserts nothing is written past `*memory_bytes` |\n| `simplified_write_to_file_and_stdio` | item 7b — all 20 formats × 4 shapes × convert8 × 3 strides through `_to_file` and `_to_stdio`, comparing the two libraries' file contents |\n| `simplified_round_trip` | item 8 — write to memory then `begin_read_from_memory`+`finish_read` in 6 output formats × 2 strides, for 20 formats × 5 shapes × convert8 × 3 strides |\n| `simplified_image_free` | item 9 — fresh zeroed struct, twice in a row, wrong `version`, after `begin_read`, after `begin_read`+corrupted version, after a successful and after a failed `finish_read`, after `write_to_memory` |\n| `simplified_documented_error_returns` | the API-level \"return 0 + message\" paths: NULL/zero-size memory, NULL filename, NULL `FILE*`, bad `version` on 5 entry points, NULL buffer, colour-mapped format with no colour-map, `row_stride` too small (read and write), NULL `memory_bytes` |\n| `simplified_read_randomised_matrix` | 30 000 randomised (fixed seed `0x040c_2024`) cases mixing shape, geometry (≤64×24), format, flags, background, stride and input source (memory / file / stdio) |\n| `simplified_write_randomised_matrix` | 12 000 randomised (fixed seed `0x040d_2024`) write cases: query/exact/generous/short buffers, and every 4th case also to file and stdio — additionally asserting memory == file == stdio bytes — followed by a randomised read-back |\n\n### Notable implementation points\n- An 8-byte-aligned `ABuf` (`Vec<u64>` backing) is used for every image/colour-map buffer, because the simplified API casts the caller's buffer to `png_uint_16*` for LINEAR formats; a plain `Vec<u8>` would be misaligned.\n- Buffers are pre-filled with fixed patterns (`0xa5` / `0x5c` / `0xcd`) so both libraries start from identical memory and untouched bytes are still compared meaningfully (no uninitialised reads).\n- A `Tally` guard per test asserts that a majority of cases actually reach the happy path **and** that the only failure message seen is the one documented case `\"background color must be supplied to remove alpha/transparency\"` (input has alpha, output format does not, `background == NULL`). Any new failure kind fails the test rather than being silently absorbed.\n- Verified the comparisons are live: temporarily XOR-ing one bit of the C output buffer failed 9 tests, and one bit of the C PNG bytes failed 3 tests. Both sabotage hooks were removed afterwards.\n- Colour-map write indices are taken modulo `colormap_entries` so the tests never trip the (correct) `\"Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette\"` error, which belongs in Phase C.\n- `T04_DEBUG=1` prints every case that returns 0 together with its `warning_or_error`/message, which is how the single legitimate failure class above was identified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1810,"cache_read_input_tokens":190829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1810,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012CPpz7bU3bkntXCbBPR1Mq","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"3f58c46f-49f8-4a73-a24d-9dfc328149cb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:09:18.948Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write simplified API tests"}
