em/progressive/user_chunk/user_transform pointers (compared as `NULL`/`EQ`/`OTHER`), io_state, io_chunk_type, user limits, chunk cache/malloc max (incl. `0`→`PNG_SIZE_MAX`), compression buffer size, pass/row number, rgb_to_gray_status.\n- **`png_free_data`/`png_data_freer`**: all 12 `PNG_FREE_*` masks × `num = -1, 0, 1, 2` × both freer values.\n- **Allocation**: `png_info_init_3` (size 0 → realloc path, and large → memset), create/destroy info struct, `png_create_{read,write}_struct_2` with a custom bump allocator, `png_malloc`/`calloc`/`malloc_warn`/`malloc_default`/`free`/`free_default`. Allocator balance is `live_after_destroy:0` in both libraries (no leak). (`png_malloc_array` is not exported, so it is not in `tests/common/api.rs`; likewise `png_set_text_2` is `PRIVATE`.)\n- **Options/misc**: `png_set_option` for options −2..18 × 4 on/off values (read back twice), `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_set_benign_errors`, `png_set_check_for_invalid_index`→`png_get_palette_max`, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` (all 4 keeps × default/list-A/list-B/all-known/reset) probed with `png_handle_as_unknown` over 14 names, `png_set_sig_bytes` 0..8 + `png_get_signature`, all compression/text-compression setters, `png_set_filter` (12 masks + MNG method 64), `png_set_filter_heuristics(_fixed)`, `png_set_flush`, read/write status fns, `png_set_interlace_handling` (1 fresh, 7 after `png_write_info` on ADAM7).\n- **Full-write byte comparison** (`t_compression_output`): 33 combinations of level/mem_level/strategy/window_bits/buffer_size/filters/text-compression settings, comparing the complete output stream byte-for-byte (lengths observed 170–759, so the settings genuinely change the bytes and both libraries agree).\n- **Warn-and-continue paths** (`t_benign_warning_paths`, after `png_set_benign_errors(p,1)`): cICP non-zero matrix coefficients, 7 invalid tIME values, non-positive sCAL/sCAL_fixed dimensions, the deprecated `png_set_eXIf`/`png_get_eXIf` pair, hIST without a palette, out-of-range tRNS colour key, cLLI/mDCV over the PNG light-level limit, mDCV chromaticities out of range, invalid cHRM XYZ, iCCP with a bogus compression method, 4 pCAL rejections, 4 out-of-range text compression modes, sPLT with NULL name/entries, invalid `keep` and missing chunk list, unknown-chunk relocation to an invalid location, over-long PLTE on a non-palette image, sub-minimum compression buffer size — messages compared verbatim.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** Every one of the 418,698 compared lines is identical between the C reference and the Rust translation.\n\nDetection was verified with a negative control: injecting one library-dependent value into `dump_info` made 19 of 24 tests fail immediately; it was then reverted.\n\nTwo reference behaviours worth recording (both libraries agree, so they are documented in the file rather than reported as bugs):\n- `png_get_valid(PNG_INFO_tRNS)` returns **0** after any successful `png_set_tRNS`, because `png_set_tRNS` only updates `info_ptr->num_trans` while `png_get_valid` gates on `png_ptr->num_trans` (`pngget.c:29` vs `pngset.c:1264`).\n- `png_get_iCCP` reports the profile length read out of the profile's own first four bytes, not `info_ptr->iccp_proflen` (`pngget.c:730`); the test therefore only ever stores profiles carrying a consistent big-endian length header, since anything else makes the getter over-read.\n\nNotable build-configuration constraints that shaped what counts as \"valid\" (cited in the file header): `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is off and `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is 0, so on a fresh struct `png_app_error`/`png_app_warning` both call `png_error` — those paths only appear after `png_set_benign_errors(p, 1)`. Also `PNG_OPTION_NEXT` is 16 in `png.h:3493`, while the copy in `tests/common/mod.rs:310` says 10; `t05_info.rs` defines its own correct constant rather than editing the shared harness."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_inp