_app_error` — `png_ptr->flags` (reached indirectly).\n\nPer-out-parameter NULLs that are also unguarded and therefore only exercised while the chunk is *absent*: `png_get_eXIf_1`'s `num_exif` (`pngget.c:910`), `png_get_PLTE`'s `num_palette` (`pngget.c:1140`), and `unit`/`width`/`height` of `png_get_sCAL`, `png_get_sCAL_fixed`, `png_get_sCAL_s` (`pngget.c:1042-1049, 1067-1069, 1085-1087`).\n\n## Notable C facts confirmed (both libraries agree)\n- **`png_get_sCAL_fixed` is *not* fatal on an empty info** — the `valid & PNG_INFO_sCAL` test returns 0 first (pngget.c:1039). It is only fatal when a stored sCAL string overflows `png_fixed`; I drove that via `png_set_sCAL_s(..., \"1e40\", ...)` → `png_error \"fixed point overflow in sCAL width\"` (and the height variant), in a sub-process. `png_get_sCAL`/`png_get_sCAL_s` on the very same info return `16384` non-fatally.\n- **`png_get_IHDR` on a zeroed info** emits `WARN:Image width is zero in IHDR`, `WARN:Image height is zero in IHDR`, `WARN:Invalid bit depth in IHDR`, then `ERROR:Invalid IHDR data` — identical in both libs. Its out-parameters are filled before the longjmp, so they cannot be printed after; the out-parameter behaviour is instead covered in-process against a *valid* IHDR (all 7 individual-NULL variants + all-NULL).\n- **ERRORS.md row 541 reproduced**: `png_set_tRNS` never writes `png_ptr->num_trans`, so `png_get_valid(p, info, PNG_INFO_tRNS)` returns 0 immediately after a successful `png_set_tRNS` even though `info_ptr->valid` has the bit — both libraries.\n\n## Divergences\n**None.** No C-vs-Rust difference was observed in any of the ~4,927 in-process comparisons or the 8 sub-process transcripts (exit code, signal, warning order and error text all matched).\n\n`self_check` is non-vacuous by construction: it asserts ≥4,000 observations, ≥40 distinct returned values, and the presence of 18 specific distinct C sentinels/messages (`palette_max=-1`, `row_number=4294967295`, `pass_number=8`, `signature=NULL`, `SENT