ck >= 1` | reaches `memcmp(&sig[start], ...)` (png.c:96) |\n| `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` | `ptime == NULL` | dereferences `ptime->year` (png.c:751) |\n| `png_write_image` | `image == NULL` | dereferences `image[i]` |\n| `png_write_row` | `row == NULL` | no NULL check |\n| `png_write_data` | never calling `png_set_write_fn` | `png_default_write_data` calls `fwrite` on a NULL `FILE*`; and passing NULL to `png_set_write_fn` installs that same default (pngwio.c:130), so the \"Call to NULL write function\" branch (pngwio.c:40) is unreachable through the public API |\n| `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` | non-NULL but bogus `image->opaque` | `png_image_read_init` only allocates when `opaque == NULL` (pngread.c:1130), then the caller dereferences `image->opaque->memory` (pngread.c:1448) |\n| `png_free_data` | `num` outside the stored array | indexes `info_ptr->text[num]` with no bounds check (png.c:498) |\n| `png_get_io_state`, `png_get_io_chunk_type` | `png_ptr == NULL` | no NULL guard (pngget.c:1344, 1350) |\n| `png_set_benign_errors`, `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` | `png_ptr == NULL` | no NULL guard (pngset.c:1926, 1956) |\n| `png_set_read_user_transform_fn` | `png_ptr == NULL` | no NULL guard (pngrtran.c:1133) |\n| `png_get_eXIf_1`, `png_get_PLTE`, `png_get_sCAL*` | individual out-parameters NULL while the chunk IS present | written to unconditionally (pngget.c:910, 1140, 1042-1087) |\n\nTwo rows resolve to `PNG_ABORT()` rather than a message and are compared as\nsuch (identical terminating signal in both libraries): `png_longjmp` with no\n`jmp_buf` installed, and `png_error` with `png_ptr == NULL`.\n\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"\\n| # | function |\"\ni = s.index(marker)\ns = s[:i] + add + s[i+1:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\nhead -60 translation/ERRORS.md | tail -25; wc -l translation/ERRORS.md","description":"Add coverage summary to ERRORS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input