lor type`, `Image width/height exceeds user limit in IHDR`, `MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream`, `Too many bytes for PNG signature`, `invalid background gamma type`, `Application must supply a known background gamma`, `png_do_rgb_to_gray found nongray pixel` (warn and error), `Can't discard critical data on CRC error`, `IDAT/tEXt: CRC error`, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: no chunk list`, `tEXt: no space in chunk cache`, `unknown chunk exceeds memory limits`, `invalid compression buffer size`, `Invalid sCAL unit`, `Invalid palette length`, `Invalid iCCP compression method`.\n\n**C locations with no NULL/range guard (excluded as UB, documented in the file header):**\n- `pngset.c:1936-1937` — `png_set_benign_errors` writes `png_ptr->flags` with no NULL check.\n- `pngrtran.c:1139` — `png_set_read_user_transform_fn` writes `png_ptr->transformations` with no NULL check (also the only read transform with neither a NULL check nor `png_rtran_ok`).\n- `pngrtran.c:823` — `png_set_quantize` `memcpy(png_ptr->palette, palette, (unsigned)num_palette*sizeof)` into a fixed 256-entry buffer: `num_palette < 0` or `> 256` is OOB. `pngrtran.c:725-727` — `maximum_colors <= 0` with `histogram == NULL` indexes `hash[i]` for `i <= max_d` past the 769-entry array.\n- `pngset.c:1719` — `chunk_list+5*i` read unchecked, so a list shorter than `5*num_chunks` is OOB.\n- `pngrutil.c:3927` — `png_do_read_interlace` copies through `png_byte v[8]; /* SAFE; pixel_depth does not exceed 64 */`.\n\n**Divergence found (real, but rooted in a C UB path, so the case was removed):** with a user-transform pixel depth above 64 bits on an *interlaced* image, e.g. `utinfo:32,4,6,1` (`png_set_user_transform_info(depth=32, channels=4)`), the C completed:\n`[\"set_user_transform_info returned\",\"update_info returned\",\"rowbytes=128\",\"rows read\",\"read_end returned\",\"OK\"]` (exit 0), while Rust died with SIGSEGV after `[\"set_user_transform_info returned\",\"update_info returned\",\"rowbytes=128