{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_y3q6mephqgk4fg4ilpjfekfpuoa5unuqrwqjubmcd5qkqav74xia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**ALL CHECKS PASSED.** No behavioural divergence found between the C reference and the Rust translation on any input the C defines.\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (in `translation/`):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 384 C exports, all present in the Rust `.so`; 0 missing, 0 extra. Only undefined imports are libc/libm/libgcc_s/zlib — same surface as the C build. (`png_err` and `png_set_strip_error_numbers` are declared in `png.h` but `#ifdef`-ed out of both libraries.)\n- `ERRORS.md` — **1183 rows**, mechanically derived from every error/warning call site, failure sentinel, range check and limit constant in the 15 C files. Each row names the test that reproduces it.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **250 rows** of valid option×shape combinations the C branches on, all ticked.\n\n**Phases B & C:** 12 test files, **186 tests**, >150 000 differential cases, ~23 s total. Every test loads both `.so`s via `libloading` and calls only exported symbols.\n\nTwo comparison mechanisms: **in-process** (compares output bytes, ~90 getter results, and the ordered warning transcript) and **sub-process** (each `png_error` case re-executes the binary per library; parent compares warnings-in-order + error text + exit status + terminating signal, so `PNG_ABORT()` paths are compared too). Every file has a `self_check` asserting the C really emits the expected distinct messages, so nothing can pass vacuously — confirmed by temporarily XOR-sabotaging the C output during development.\n\n**Phase D:** symbol diff empty; `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so `default` is the only configuration (the runner still derives the list from `cargo metadata` so adding one extends the matrix).\n\n## Two bugs found in *my own* test coverage, now fixed\n- `t03_read.rs`'s progressive tests delivered **zero rows** — libpng needs `png_start_read_image` from the info callback. Both libraries were \"agreeing\" on a degenerate path.\n- `pngbuild` only emitted filter type 0, so `png_read_filter_row`'s Sub/Up/Avg/Paeth reconstruction was never exercised. Added `t06_filters_roundtrip.rs` (all filter types + cross-library round trips).\n\n## Inputs excluded as C-level UB (documented in `ERRORS.md`)\nEach was attempted, crashed in **both** libraries with no diagnostic, and verified against the C to have no guard: NULL `sig`/`ptime`/`row`/`image`, out-of-range `num` in `png_free_data` (`png.c:498`), bogus `png_image.opaque`, missing NULL guards in `png_get_io_state`/`png_set_benign_errors`/etc. Notably `png_write_data`'s `\"Call to NULL write function\"` branch is **unreachable** via the public API, since `png_set_write_fn(NULL)` installs the stdio default.\n\nOne real divergence surfaced and was traced to C UB: a user transform declaring >64 bits/pixel on an interlaced image overruns `png_byte v[8]` in `png_do_read_interlace` — whose own comment reads `/* SAFE; pixel_depth does not exceed 64 */`. The C survives its stack overflow by luck; Rust faults. Non-interlaced >64-bit transforms agree and are covered.\n\n`c_src/` and `translation/src/` were not modified (timestamps unchanged). Changes were confined to `translation/tests/`, `Cargo.toml` (dev-dependency + matching dev profile), and the new docs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":599301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1054,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"231e0674-da68-4bed-b353-5484f33ed592","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:31:08.370Z"}
