{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_25fhxvakbk4xyhqqfqukqhk63rixvvoba4eg3m5u6a3ckkcyzeka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/t24_err_misc.rs` (3292 lines) is written and all tests pass.\n\n## Result\n\n**`#[test]` functions:** 21 (19 differential groups + `harness_child` + `self_check`)\n\n**Individual cases:** ~1,473 sub-process cases (2,946 child processes: 881 ASCII-buffer, 378 `png_check_IHDR`, 126 fixed-point, 37 array-alloc, 24 write-side zlib, 16 creator version, 11 rio/wio) plus ~181,000 in-process comparisons (108,203 muldiv/reciprocal/gamma; 35,309 colour-space; 20,096 rfc1123; 8,568 unknown-chunk queries over 168 keep-configs; 4,241 safecat/format_number/check_fp/formatted_warning; 4,039 check_keyword; 465 iCCP-chunk reads; 346 ICC direct; 154 zalloc/zfree; 44 array sentinels; 30 version-check; 30 zstream codes; 8 reset_zstream).\n\n**Final result line (verbatim):**\n```\ntest result: ok. 21 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 3.17s\n```\nRuntime ~3.2 s (well under the 200 s budget). `t01`, `t20`, `t23` still pass unchanged.\n\n## C locations with no guard (UB — deliberately not tested, cited in comments)\n- `png.c:2737` / `png.c:2756` — `png_fixed`/`png_fixed_ITU` cast `r` to `png_fixed_point`/`png_uint_32` after the range test; for NaN neither test fires and the cast is UB. **NaN is excluded** (x86 `cvttsd2si` yields `INT_MIN`, Rust `as` saturates — that difference is not a spec violation).\n- `png.c:751` — `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` dereferences `ptime->year` with no NULL check (only `out == NULL` is guarded at `png.c:748`).\n- `pngrio.c:59` / `pngwio.c:57` — `png_default_read_data`/`png_default_write_data` call `fread`/`fwrite` on `png_ptr->io_ptr` with no NULL check; a real stdio stream (`/dev/null` opened read-only) is used instead.\n- `pngerror.c:310` / `:463` — `png_benign_error`/`png_chunk_benign_error` dereference `png_ptr->flags` with no NULL check.\n- `pngset.c:1611`, `:1665` — `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` invalid `keep`/NULL list are fatal `png_app_error`s in this build, so only valid configs are used in-process.\n\n## Unreachable rows (recorded, not tested)\n- `png.c:1989` \"Image width is too large for this architecture\" — threshold is `0x1fff_ffff_ffff_fffd` on 64-bit, above any `png_uint_32`.\n- `png.c:118` \"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\" — smallest RHS is `(2^64-1)/(2^32-1) = 2^32+1`, larger than any 32-bit `items`.\n- `pngmem.c:88` `size > PNG_SIZE_MAX` — dead code (`PNG_SIZE_MAX == SIZE_MAX`). The reachable overflow is `pngmem.c:113`, which is covered.\n- `pngrio.c:95` / `pngwio.c:130` — passing NULL to the setters installs the stdio default, so \"Call to NULL read/write function\" is only reachable via the cross-wiring branches (`pngrio.c:106` / `pngwio.c:157`); both are covered, including the shared warning text.\n- `pngrutil.c:824` (the only `zstream.msg` report that does not touch zlib) — unreachable because `png_read_buffer`'s limit at `pngrutil.c:380` is strictly larger and rejects the chunk first.\n\n## Item 5 (`png_zstream_error`) — partial, with reason\n`zstream.msg` cannot be read back: **every** path ending in `png_error(png_ptr, png_ptr->zstream.msg)` first calls `deflateInit2`/`deflateReset`/`inflateInit2`/`inflateReset2`, all of which assign `strm->msg = Z_NULL` before validating, destroying any injected string. So the test (a) calls `png_zstream_error` directly with all 9 zlib codes + 6 out-of-range codes on read and write structs and asserts both libraries are silent and the struct stays usable, and (b) drives real corrupt zlib streams. Only **3 of the 10 strings are observable at all**, and all three are asserted in `self_check`/the test itself: `\"missing LZ dictionary\"` (FDICT), `\"truncated\"` (Z_BUF_ERROR), `\"bad parameters to zlib\"` (write-side `deflateInit2` failure). `\"zlib IO error\"` (Z_ERRNO, gz-API only) and `\"unsupported zlib version\"` (Z_VERSION_ERROR) cannot be produced by any input. `png_check_IHDR` covers 14 of its 15 compiled warning sites plus the terminal `\"Invalid IHDR data\"`.\n\n## C-vs-Rust divergences\n**None.** Every comparison agreed, including stricter checks than the existing tests make: `png_muldiv` leaves `*res` untouched on failure in both; all 19 ICC rejection strings (18 asserted present in the C, plus `\"profile too long\"`) match byte-for-byte through both the direct calls and a crafted `iCCP` chunk; `png_check_keyword`'s rewritten 80-byte buffer, returned length and `png_formatted_warning` text match; the sub-process transcripts (warning order, message text, exit code) are identical for all 1,473 cases."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":370939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":617,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YVWdKEQN8gJaNH8hEvMTG4","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"ff9bf6a7-b73c-4f54-afbb-2ab6d549c0b9","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:31:57.865Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write misc/internal error tests"}
