ad. The reachable overflow guard is `png_malloc_array_checked` (pngmem.c:113), which IS covered. |\n| `png_read_data` / `png_write_data` \"Call to NULL read/write function\" (pngrio.c:95, pngwio.c:130) | passing NULL to `png_set_read_fn` / `png_set_write_fn` installs the stdio default instead, so the NULL branch cannot be reached. The cross-wiring warnings (pngrio.c:106, pngwio.c:157) ARE reachable and are covered, including the shared message text. |\n| `pngrutil.c:824` (the only `zstream.msg` report that does not go through zlib) | `png_read_buffer`'s limit at pngrutil.c:380 is strictly larger and rejects the chunk first. |\n\n### `png_zstream_error`: only 3 of its 10 messages are observable\n\nEvery code path that ends in `png_error(png_ptr, png_ptr->zstream.msg)` first calls\n`deflateInit2` / `deflateReset` / `inflateInit2` / `inflateReset2`, and zlib\nassigns `strm->msg = Z_NULL` inside each of those before validating — so a string\nplaced in `zstream.msg` by `png_zstream_error` cannot be read back out through any\npublic entry point.  `t24_err_misc.rs` therefore (a) calls `png_zstream_error`\ndirectly with all nine zlib return codes plus six out-of-range codes, on read and\nwrite structs, asserting both libraries stay silent and the struct remains usable,\nand (b) drives real corrupt zlib streams.  Three messages are reachable that way\nand all three are asserted verbatim: `\"missing LZ dictionary\"` (FDICT set),\n`\"truncated\"` (`Z_BUF_ERROR`), `\"bad parameters to zlib\"` (write-side\n`deflateInit2` failure).  `\"zlib IO error\"` (`Z_ERRNO`, only produced by zlib's\ngz* API, which libpng never calls) and `\"unsupported zlib version\"`\n(`Z_VERSION_ERROR`) cannot be produced by any input to this library.\"\"\"\nassert anchor in s\ns = s.replace(anchor, add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ERRORS.md updated\")\n\np='translation/VERIFICATION.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"Two reference behaviours worth recording\"\nnew = \"\"\"A third class is recorded in `ERRORS.md` but not asserted: five rows are\npresent in the C yet **unreachable for any input** (a width limit above every\n`png_uint_32`, a `png_zalloc` overflow check the C itself calls \"vestigial\", a\ndead `size > PNG_SIZE_MAX` test, the two \"Call to NULL read/write function\"\nbranches that `png_set_read_fn`/`png_set_write_fn` make unreachable by\ninstalling the stdio default, and one `zstream.msg` report shadowed by an\nearlier limit).  Each was verified against the source rather than assumed.\n\nSeparately, only 3 of `png_zstream_error`'s 10 message strings are observable\nthrough any public entry point, because zlib clears `strm->msg` inside\n`deflateInit2` / `inflateInit2` / the reset calls before libpng can report it.\nAll three reachable ones are asserted verbatim; the reasoning and the two\nstrings that no input can produce are documented in `ERRORS.md`.\n\nTwo reference behaviours worth recording\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"VERIFICATION.md updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c '^| ' translation/ERRORS.md; ./translation/run_verification.sh tests 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Document t24 findings and re-run suite","timeout":900000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":604163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1574,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","uuid":"f0d2a8a9-1713-4c71-8f9f-86e00a69fe83","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:32:43.102Z"}
