failure sentinel, range check and limit constant in the 15 C files. Each row names the test that reproduces it.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **250 rows** of valid option×shape combinations the C branches on, all ticked.\n\n**Phases B & C:** 12 test files, **186 tests**, >150 000 differential cases, ~23 s total. Every test loads both `.so`s via `libloading` and calls only exported symbols.\n\nTwo comparison mechanisms: **in-process** (compares output bytes, ~90 getter results, and the ordered warning transcript) and **sub-process** (each `png_error` case re-executes the binary per library; parent compares warnings-in-order + error text + exit status + terminating signal, so `PNG_ABORT()` paths are compared too). Every file has a `self_check` asserting the C really emits the expected distinct messages, so nothing can pass vacuously — confirmed by temporarily XOR-sabotaging the C output during development.\n\n**Phase D:** symbol diff empty; `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so `default` is the only configuration (the runner still derives the list from `cargo metadata` so adding one extends the matrix).\n\n## Two bugs found in *my own* test coverage, now fixed\n- `t03_read.rs`'s progressive tests delivered **zero rows** — libpng needs `png_start_read_image` from the info callback. Both libraries were \"agreeing\" on a degenerate path.\n- `pngbuild` only emitted filter type 0, so `png_read_filter_row`'s Sub/Up/Avg/Paeth reconstruction was never exercised. Added `t06_filters_roundtrip.rs` (all filter types + cross-library round trips).\n\n## Inputs excluded as C-level UB (documented in `ERRORS.md`)\nEach was attempted, crashed in **both** libraries with no diagnostic, and verified against the C to have no guard: NULL `sig`/`ptime`/`row`/`image`, out-of-range `num` in `png_free_data` (`png.c:498`), bogus `png_image.opaque`, missing NULL guards in `png_get_io_state`/`png_set_benign_errors`/etc. Notably `png_write_data`'s `\"Call to NULL write function\"` branch is **unreachable** via the public API, since `png_set_write_fn(NULL)` installs the stdio default.\n\nOne real divergence surfaced and was traced to C UB: a user transform declaring >64 bits/pixel on an interlaced image overruns `png_byte v[8]` in `png_do_read_interlace` — whose own comment reads `/* SAFE; pixel_depth does not exceed 64 */`. The C survives its stack overflow by luck; Rust faults. Non-interlaced >64-bit transforms agree and are covered.\n\n`c_src/` and `translation/src/` were not modified (timestamps unchanged). Changes were confined to `translation/tests/`, `Cargo.toml` (dev-dependency + matching dev profile), and the new docs.","ttft_ms":2442,"type":"result","duration_ms":4101975,"uuid":"71c79b0d-1061-40ad-b5d3-f96aa399bdff","ttft_stream_ms":2320,"time_to_request_ms":61,"queued_turn_count":0}
{"duration_api_ms":14064147,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d61bc42a-4e8d-424f-b737-52a7165119c7","total_cost_usd":129.99977075000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8157,"cache_read_input_tokens":1810255,"output_tokens":4679,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":923},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8157},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":1380,"outputTokens":1208266,"cacheReadInputTokens":150112254,"cacheCreationInputTokens":3956815,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":129.99977075000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":267513,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":13,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":13},"started_in_background":13,"max_depth":2,"spawned_by_subagents":3,"completed":13,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":10,"Explore":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The final Phase C sub-agent's report arrived; I verified its claims against the C source myself and folded them into the artifacts. **Suite still green: ALL CHECKS PASSED.**\n\n## What the last file added\n\n`tests/t24_err_misc.rs` — 21 tests, ~1,473 sub-process cases (2,946 child processes) plus ~181,000 in-process comparisons: `png_ascii_from_*` undersized buffers, `png_fixed`/`png_fixed_ITU` overflow, `png_muldiv`/`png_reciprocal` sentinels (108k cases), all `png_XYZ_from_xy`/`png_xy_from_XYZ` failure branches (35k), all 19 ICC rejection strings both directly and through a crafted `iCCP` chunk, the nine `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` field checks (20k), `png_check_IHDR` (14 of 15 compiled warning sites + the terminal error), `png_check_keyword`, `png_user_version_check`, the array-allocation sentinels, `png_zalloc`/`png_zfree`, and the reachable `pngrio.c`/`pngwio.c` paths. No divergence.\n\n## Claims I independently verified before documenting\n\nI checked each \"unreachable\" assertion against the C rather than taking the report's word:\n\n- `png.c:1989` width limit — threshold derives from `PNG_SIZE_MAX`; the C's own comment says the comparison \"will always be false\" on 64-bit. ✓\n- `png.c:118` `png_zalloc` overflow — `items >= (~0)/size` with both operands `unsigned int` means the smallest RHS is `2^32+1`, above any 32-bit `items`; the C comment calls the check \"vestigial\". ✓\n- `pngmem.c:88` `size > PNG_SIZE_MAX` — `PNG_SIZE_MAX == SIZE_MAX` and `size` is a `size_t`, so it's dead code; the *reachable* guard is `png_malloc_array_checked` (`pngmem.c:113`), which is covered. ✓\n- The `zstream.msg` clearing happens inside **zlib**, not libpng — consistent with `grep` finding no such assignment in `c_src`. ✓\n\n## One honest limitation now documented\n\nOnly **3 of `png_zstream_error`'s 10 messages are observable** through any public entry point: every path that reports `zstream.msg` first calls `deflateInit2`/`inflateInit2`/a reset, and zlib nulls `msg` inside those before validating. The three reachable ones (`\"missing LZ dictionary\"`, `\"truncated\"`, `\"bad parameters to zlib\"`) are asserted verbatim; `\"zlib IO error\"` (gz* API only) and `\"unsupported zlib version\"` cannot be produced by any input. This is recorded in `ERRORS.md` with the reasoning rather than left as an unexplained gap.\n\n## Final state\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Symbol parity | 384/384, 0 missing, 0 extra |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 1183 rows; 1131 with a passing test, 52 `n/a` (each individually justified: `#ifdef`-excluded, unreachable, or no check exists in the C) |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 250 rows, all ticked |\n| Tests | 12 files, 186 tests, >330,000 differential cases, ~23 s |\n| Divergences on defined C behaviour | **none** |\n\n`c_src/` and `translation/src/` remain unmodified.","ttft_ms":9811,"type":"result","duration_ms":92765,"uuid":"7cdd0cfc-cefa-4e31-a34c-2378af8f932e","ttft_stream_ms":4307,"time_to_request_ms":86,"queued_turn_count":0}
